"hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:"
36073,"(36073) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that he used to recite The Qur’an is in seven verses."
36074,"(36074) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, he said: A people who have not yet reached the age of piety"
36075,"(36075) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, he said: Ziyad bin Hadir: I wish I were in a space of iron and with something that would be right for me. I would not speak, and they would not speak to me."
36076,"(36076) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Qays, who said: If you are in any of The matter of this world is open, and if you are concerned about any matter of the hereafter, stay as long as you can. And if Satan comes to you while you are praying, He said: You are showing off, so increase and prolong it."
36077,"(36077) Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Khaythama said: You sit. And Ibrahim was in the mosque and gathered with you. I saw Al-Harith bin Qais, when two men gathered with him, he stood up. And he left them."
36078,"(36078) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: If a man were to knock Al-Fustat, he said: They will find a sound like the sound of bees, so why are these people safe as long as they were afraid?"
36079,"(36079) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabi’ah, he said: He said Utba bin Farqad to Abdullah bin Rabi’a: O Abdullah, won’t you help me against your brother’s son? He said: What is that? He said: He helps me with the work I am doing. Then Abdullah said to him: O Amr, obey your father. He said: Then he looked at Ma’adid and he said: He was sitting, so he said: Do not obey them {and prostrate and draw near}. He said: Then Amr said: Oh, my father, I am only a slave working in your jaws. My neck, he said: Then Utba cried and said: O my son, I love you with two loves: the love of God and the love of a father for his child, he said: and he said: Amr: O father, you have brought me money amounting to seventy thousand, so if you ask me about it then take it. Otherwise, he will leave me and let him go. He said to him: He cursed him, so he let him go. He said: So he led him away until not a dirham remained of him."
36080,"(36080) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, he said: Ammar narrated to us, he said: The family of Shuraih bin went out with us. Coming to Mecca, he went out with us and led us in the procession. He said: And it was as he said to us: Strive to travel, for your riders will not It avails you nothing from God, and a man has never lost anything in this world that is easier for him than abandoning himself. Amara said: I never mentioned any of his words except that I benefited from them."
36081,"(36081) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Mahan say: Isn’t any of you ashamed to The animal that he rides and the garment that he wears are more remembrance of God than of himself, so he would not stop saying “Allahu Akbar” And the tahlil."
36082,"(36082) Muhammad ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, the muezzin of Banu Hanifi, who said: I saw the meaning of the Hanafi and he commanded it. Al-Hajjaj wanted him to be crucified at his door. He said: I looked at him and he was probably on the wood and he was glorifying God, glorifying God, and glorifying God. And praise be to God, until he reached the age of twenty-nine, so he held his hand and stabbed him while he was in that state. I saw after a month Twenty-nine in his hand. He said: And he used to see the light at night."
36083,"(36083) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Abu Al-Bakhtari was a gentle man. He hears your wailing and weeps."
36084,"(36084) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, in his saying: “They took their rabbis.” And their lords are lords besides Allah. So they worshiped them with that."
36085,"(36085) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mas’ar told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, he said: Abu Al-Bakhtari said: Because I will be It is more beloved to me to be among a people who are more knowledgeable than me than to be among a people whom I know."
36086,"(36086) Abu Asama told us, he said: Sa’id bin Salih told us, he told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, he said: Abu Al-Bakhtari: Three because something else is more beloved to me than the heavens than being one of them: a people who have deemed permissible hadiths that have adornment and glory. And they were fed up with the Qur’an, and a people who obeyed created beings in their disobedience to the Creator, meaning the people of the Levant and the Kharijites."
36087,"(36087) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, that Abu Al-Bakhtari And his companions used to bend his shoulders and say: I submit to God when he heard anyone praising him, or a feeling of admiration entered him."
36088,"(36088) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, he said: The land To lose the believer, and the places are decorated for the believer if he wants to pray."
36089,"(36089) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: It used to be said: Hasten to work. Four: With life before death, with health before sickness, and with free time before work, and I did not memorize the fourth."
36090,"(36090) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, regarding his saying: {You will not attain righteousness}. He said: righteousness. Heaven"
36091,"(36091) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: He used to put a peg in a wall. The mosque, and when he was tired of standing during prayer and it was difficult for him, he would hold the peg and lean on it, or tie it to it. A rope to hold on to."
36092,"(36092) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Amr ibn Maymun performed Hajj sixty out of two Hajj. And his life"
36093,"(36093) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Abu Sinan told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, in His saying {That is because they disliked what God sent down, so He nullified their deeds} He said: The obligations."
36094,"(36094) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Afaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: It is heard under the skin of an infidel. And the flesh of worms is like the flesh of wild animals."
36095,"(36095) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hanash, he said: I saw Amr ibn Maymun and he had concerns."
36096,"(36096) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, who said: Whenever Amr met a man from among his brothers, he would say: May God provide for him yesterday. Of prayer such-and-such, and God provided yesterday with such-and-such goodness. (Hakim 527)"
36097,"(36097) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda’, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: You have seen us, and we are only learning. Piety"
36098,"(36098) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Umar ibn Qais al-Nasir, on the authority of al-Dahhak, he said: Our companions overtook us, And they learn nothing but piety."
36099,"(36099) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, he said: I said to Al-Dahhak: Why was it called Sidrat Al-Muntaha? He said: Because Everything of God’s command ends with it."
36100,"(36100) Amr bin Saad Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla said: The soul is in the hand of an angel who walks with it, so when he enters his grave, he places it in it."
36101,"(36101) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla He is praying, and when he enters, he comes to his bed and leans on it."
36102,"(36102) Affan told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, he said: {Neither oppression nor humiliation shall overwhelm their faces} He said: after they have looked to their Lord."
36103,"(36103) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, He said: The polytheists say: {Oh, woe to us! Who has raised us from our resting place?} He said: The believers say: {This is what the Most Gracious promised and is true. The Messengers}"
36104,"(36104) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Salamah, who said: They were not the companions of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, they were shaken, but not dead, and they used to recite poetry in their gatherings, and they mentioned the matter of Their ignorant nature, so if one of them was tried to do anything regarding a religious matter, his eyes would turn around as if he were crazy."
36105,"(36105) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu Salamah narrated to us, that the morning of the Day of Resurrection That night will last as long as three nights, so those who fear their Lord will rise and pray until they have finished their prayers. They went back and slept until their sides were tired, then they got up and prayed until, when they had finished their prayer, they looked at the sun from the morning. Its rising, and behold, it has risen from its west."
36106,"(36106) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who said: Among the perfection of piety is You seek what you know of it. Learn what you do not know, and know that the deficiency in what you know is abandoning the desire for an increase in it, but only A man is blamed for abandoning the pursuit of increase in what he has learned, and the lack of benefit from what he has learned."
36107,"(36107) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun, who said: It is sufficiently arrogant for you to take Thank you to others."
36108,"(36108) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun, who said: The one who remembers is like the one who remembers among the heedless, like the one who fights among those who flee. And he who is heedless of those who remember is like a fugitive, neglectful of the fighters."
36109,"(36109) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun, who said: He informed him of forgiveness before sin {May God pardon Why did you give them permission?"
36110,"(36110) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, he said: No one comes down Death is its true status, except for a servant who promises a tomorrow that is not for him. How many days are in the future that will not be completed, and there is hope for a tomorrow that will not be fulfilled. If you had seen the term and its path, you would have hated hope and its arrogance."
36111,"(36111) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun, who said: He was, it is said: Who May God improve his image and place him in a righteous position, then he humbled himself for the sake of God. He was sincere to God."
36112,"(36112) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit {For those who do good, goodness and increase} He said: looking at one’s face God"
36113,"(36113) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: God says: Indeed, O son of Adam, as long as you worship Me and hope in Me, then I will forgive you for what you have done. My servant asks Me for guidance. How can I mislead My servant when he is They ask Me for guidance, and I am the judge."
36114,"(36114) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: Good news to those who walk in injustice. night to prayers with perfect light on the Day of Resurrection."
36115,"(36115) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Karim, who heard it from Ibn Sabit: {And indeed, it is in the Mother of the Book with us. Perhaps Ali is Wise. He said: In the Mother of the Book every thing will exist until the Day of Resurrection."
36116,"(36116) Abu Asama told us, he said: I heard Al-A’mash, he said: Amr bin Murra told us, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, he said: He arranges a matter. There are four worldly things: Gabriel, Mikael, Israfil, and the Angel of Death. As for Gabriel, he is the companion of the hosts and the wind. As for Mikael, he is the owner of the pot and the plant, and as for the Angel of Death, he is appointed to seize souls, and as for Israfil, he descends. By enjoining upon them what they are commanded."
36117,"(36117) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, who said: I heard Ibrahim Al-Taymi He says: I did not put my words ahead of my actions except for fear that I would be a liar."
36118,"(36118) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsiya, who said: I heard Ibrahim Al-Taymi saying: Oh God, we are We are weak. From weakness You created us, and to weakness we will never become. So whatever You wish, not whatever We wish, so please us that we remain upright."
36119,"(36119) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, who said: It was part of his speech that he said: : What grief is greater for a person than to see his servant whom God has given him permission in this world, and in the sight of God he is better? revealed from Him on the Day of Resurrection, and what grief to a person is greater than that God should give him wealth in this world? Then someone else will inherit it, and he will work in it in obedience to God, so his burden will be on him and his reward will be on someone else, and what a sorrow for him? A person is too great to see a servant whose sight was blind in this world. God has opened his sight to him while he himself has been blind. Then he says: Those who were before you were fleeing from the world while it was coming to them, and they had a long history similar to theirs. And you are following it while it is turning away from you, and you will have a torment similar to yours, so measure your affairs and the affairs of the people."
36120,"(36120) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi: {And death will come to him from Every place} He said: even from the ends of his hair."
36121,"(36121) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi: {Indeed, We have guided you}. He said: Adopt."
36122,"(36122) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, he said: He used to wear With the robe, it reaches his buttocks from behind him and his breasts from between his hands. He said: I said: O father, if only you You took on a robe wider than this robe of yours. He said: My son, do not say that, for by God, there is no morsel on the earth that you have uttered. She is good, but I wish she were among the people who hate me the most."
36123,"(36123) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, he said: He went out to Basra. So he bought a slave for four thousand. He said: So they built a house for him, then he sold them for a profit of four thousand. He said: So I said to him: Oh. She refused if you went to Basra and bought something like these and won from them. Then he said: Do not tell me that, for by God it would not I was happy with her when she was afflicted, and I never told myself that I would go back and be afflicted with something like her."
36124,"(36124) Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yazid bin Shajara, he said: There is no He dies until those sitting with him at the time of his death appear to him. If they are people of diversion, then they are Is there a mention? Is there a mention?"
36125,"(36125) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Shajar, who said: The grave says to the infidel or immoral man: Did you not mention my injustice? Did you not mention my loneliness? Did I not mention my distress? Did you not mention my grief?"
36126,"(36126) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Yazid bin Shajara, he said: He used to tell stories and he His actions confirm his words."
36127,"(36127) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Kurdous, who said: He used to tell us stories in the morning and evening. And he says: Indeed, Paradise is not attained except by doing work for it. Mix desire with terror, and always do good deeds, and fear God with hearts. Sound and good deeds, and it is often said: He who fears will fall."
36128,"(36128) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zanba`, on the authority of Abu al-Dhaqan, who said: While A young man was walking with Al-Ahnaf, and he said to him: O son of my brother, when the truth is presented to you, then seek for him and his family more than anyone else."
36129,"(36129) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, saying: Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin He frowned, he said: It used to be said: Work while you are feeling pity and leave work while you desire it. A small good deed will last forever."
36130,"(36130) Yahya bin Sa’id and Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah. Yahya said: If he prostrates, and Ibn Mahdi said: If a man covers his forehead, then he is free of arrogance."
36131,"(36131) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I heard them mentioning, on the authority of Shurayh, that he saw his neighbors transformed. He said: What is the matter with you? They said: We have finished. He said: And this is the order of the empty."
36132,"(36132) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: The easiest rituals are clothing and walking."
36133,"(36133) Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, he said: Abu Sinan told us, he said: Abdullah bin complained to us. One day, Abu al-Dhail rebuked his sins, and a man said to him: O Abu al-Mughirah, are you not pious? He said: So he said: Oh God, your servant This man wanted to get close to me, and I bear witness to your abhorrence of him."
36134,"(36134) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash said: I came and was told: Your brother has died, so I came quickly, and he was covered with his garment. I am at the head of My brother, I ask forgiveness for him and come back when the garment was revealed from his face, and he said: Peace be upon you, so we said: And peace be upon you, Glory be to God. He said: Glory be to God. Indeed, I came to God after you and was met with a spirit and fragrance and a Lord who is not angry, and He clothed me with green clothes of Sundus and Istibraq, and I found the matter easier than you think, and do not despair. Indeed, I have asked my Lord for permission to inform you. And I bring you good tidings, carry me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for he has covenanted with me that I will not leave until I come to him, then He turned off his seat. He said: And he took a pebble and threw it at him. He said: I do not know whether he was faster or not."
36135,"(36135) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, he said: They were good people when they met each other. They entrust one another with three things, and if they are absent, they write to one another: “Whoever does a good deed for the hereafter, God is sufficient for this world.” Whoever makes peace between himself and God, God will suffice people, and whoever makes peace with his secrets, God will make peace with his public affairs."
36136,"(36136) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbă narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sinan, that he saw He accompanied him while he was asleep, and he said: What thing did you see that was better when you learned of the matter? He said: The prostrations of the mosque."
36137,"(36137) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Toama’a, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, who said: He was among those who were before you. A man worshiped God for forty years on land, then he said: O Lord, I long to worship You on the sea. Then a people came So he begged them, and they carried him, and their ship sailed with them as God wished for it to run. Then it got up and saw a tree near it. Water, he said: He said: They put you on this tree, he said: They said: What will make you live on this tree? He said: I only made it bearable for you. So they placed me where I wanted. So they placed me and their ship sailed with them. Then an angel wanted to ascend to the heavens and spoke his words. The one who was ascending it was unable to do so, so he knew that it was a sin on his part, so the companion of The tree and asked him to intercede on his behalf with his Lord. He said: So he prayed and prayed for the angel. He said: He asked his Lord to be him. He seized himself so that it would be easier for him than the angel of death, so he came to him when his time had come, and he said: I have sought my Lord. That He may intercede for me on your behalf just as He interceded for you on my behalf, and that I may take your soul, so from wherever you wish, I may take it.’ He said: So he prostrated. He prostrated and tears came out of his eyes and he died."
36138,"(36138) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: He used to say: When winter comes, O People of the Qur’an, the night is long for your prayers and the day is short for your fasting, so take advantage."
36139,"(36139) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: Al-Mujahid was not There is nothing among you except like a player who goes on."
36140,"(36140) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: The people of the graves expect news. If you do not come to them, they say: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. Take a different path than ours."
36141,"(36141) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: He will bring a great, tall man. On the Day of Resurrection, it will be placed in the scale, and it will not weigh in the sight of God. weight}"
36142,"(36142) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair: {Every door-to-door has a guardian} He said: The one who does not sit A seat, then he gets up and asks God for forgiveness."
36143,"(36143) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Part of the sincerity of faith and righteousness is performing ablution completely. In times of hardship, it is part of the sincerity of faith and righteousness that a man is alone with a beautiful woman and leaves her alone, not leaving her except for the sake of Allah."
36144,"(36144) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, in his saying: That is a zannaim. He pushed a thousand and one into Hell."
36145,"(36145) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair: {There is a guardian for every person.} He said: The one who remembers his sins in private and asks for their forgiveness."
36146,"(36146) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr: {Every day is about a matter} He said: It is his duty to relieve a suffering person, or answer a supplicant, or heal a sick person, or give a gift to a beggar."
36147,"(36147) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: You will be recorded at God bless your names, your marks, your gatherings, and your adornments."
36148,"(36148) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, regarding the saying of God {I touched them. Misfortunes and hardships} He said: Miseries: misery, and hardships: harm, then he said: hardships: prosperity, and hardships: hardship."
36149,"(36149) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: A man had three Some of their friends are more particular to him than others. He said: Then a calamity befell him. He met the most particular of the three, and he said: O so-and-so, it is. Such-and-such has happened to me, and I would love for you to help me. He said: I am not doing what I am doing, so he went off to the one next to him. The elite, and he said: O so-and-so, such-and-such has happened to me, and I would like you to help me. So he said: I will go with you until You reach the place you want, and when you reach it, I will return and leave you. So he went to the meanest of the three, and said: O so-and-so, he has Such-and-such happened to me, and I would like you to help me. He said: I will go with you wherever you go, and I will enter with you wherever you go. I entered, and he said: As for the first, it is his wealth. He was succeeded by his family, and nothing of it followed him, and the second is his family and his clan. They took him to his grave, then they came back and left him, and the third was with him wherever he went and will enter with him wherever he goes. He entered"
36150,"(36150) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr {On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come} He said: The appearance The sun from the west."
36151,"(36151) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: God has made lawful and forbidden Whatever he made lawful, they made lawful, and what he made unlawful, they avoided it, and he left out some things from that which he neither made lawful nor forbidden, so that is a pardon. From God pardoned him, then he recited: {O you who have believed, do not ask about things} until the end of the verse."
36152,"(36152) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: Allah will never cease to exist. The servant has a need that the servant never had before God."
36153,"(36153) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Qays ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Umair said: The people of the graves stand close to the dead, just as a passenger meets him. They ask him, and when they ask him, what did he do? So-and-so is among those who died, and he says: Did he not come to you? They say: To Allah we belong, and to Him we shall return. He was taken to his mother. Al-Hawīyah"
36154,"(36154) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of his father, said: The grave will say: O son of Adam, what have you prepared for me? Did you not know that I am a stranger’s house? And the house of the lonely, and the house of food, and the house of worms."
36155,"(36155) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, who said: If Noah were to meet a man Of his people, and he strangles him until he falls unconscious. He said: Then he comes back to himself and says: My Lord, forgive my people. For they do not know."
36156,"(36156) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, saying: I heard him narrating, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair. Al-Laythi: When Noah’s people drowned, he said: There was a woman with them who had a child of hers. He said: So she raised him to the Her loins, and when the water reached him, she raised them to her breast. Then, when the water reached him, she raised them to her breasts, so God said: If only I were “merciful to any of them,” meaning “by her mercy,” meaning the boy."
36157,"(36157) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: If God wanted a servant He learned the religion well and taught him the right guidance in it."
36158,"(36158) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: Ibrahim, It will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Enter Paradise through whatever gates of Paradise you wish. He said: Then he will say: O Lord, my father, and it will be said. To him: He is not one of you. If he persisted in the question, he was told: Your father is better than you. He said: Then he turned around and saw that it was a hyena. So he says: I have no need in it, so his soul will be satisfied with it, so he takes Abraham to Paradise, and he departs. With his father to Hell."
36159,"(36159) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, He said: The poor immigrants will come on the Day of Resurrection, their spears and swords dripping with blood. He said: Then it will be said to them: As Until you are held accountable for it. He said: Then they say: Have you given us anything for which you will hold us accountable? He said: Then that will be considered. There are only their villages on which they migrated. He said: They will enter Paradise five hundred years before the people."
36160,"(36160) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Rashid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair {Indeed, it was for the returnees Forgiving} The Most Merciful One who remembers his sins in private and seeks forgiveness from them."
36161,"(36161) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: When God wanted Oh, to destroy the companions of the elephant, He sent upon them birds created from the sea like hawksbills, each of which carries Three stones in pieces: two stones in his feet and a stone in his beak. He said: It came until it lined up over their heads, then She shouted and threw what was in her legs and beaks. Not a stone falls on a man’s head without it coming out of his back, and it does not fall on him. Something from his body came out from the other side. He said: And God sent a strong wind that struck the stones and increased their intensity. So they were destroyed all together."
36162,"(36162) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: It was. It is said: Satan says: He has not defeated me. The son of Adam will never be able to defeat me in three matters: to take money that is not his due, or to deny him what is due to him, or To put it in something other than what it deserves."
36163,"(36163) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: It was. It is said: Satan says: How? The son of Adam overpowers me, and when he is satisfied, I come so that I can be in his heart, and when he is angry, I fly so that I can be in his head. (Hanad 1304, Ahmad 4)"
36164,"(36164) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Khaythamiah saying in these verses: {One day. He will make the children grey. He said: A herald will call on the Day of Resurrection. A messenger of fire will emerge from every thousand nine hundred and ninety. And ninety-nine, and from that the children will turn gray."
36165,"(36165) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: Khaythamiya called me, and when I came, the owners of the turbans And the horses were riding, and I was ashamed of myself and came back. He said: He met me after that and said: What is the matter with you that you did not come? He said: I said: You have. I came, but I saw the owners of turbans and cloaks on horses, and I felt despised myself. He said: By God, you are more beloved to me than them. He said: And when we entered upon him, he would take the basket from under the bed and say: Eat, by God, I do not desire it, and I will only do it. punch"
36166,"(36166) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, he said: His people used to harm him, and he said: These They harm me, and by God, none of them asks me for anything except that I fulfill it, and I do not bring harm to any of them. And I hate them more than the black dog, and they did not see that. Indeed, by God, He never loves a hypocrite with a believer."
36167,"(36167) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: The angels say: O Lord, your faithful servant. It distances him from this world and exposes him to trials. He said: Then He says to the angels: Reveal to them his reward, and when they see His reward. They said: O Lord, whatever afflicts him in this world will not harm him. He said: And they say: Your disbeliever servant, from whom calamities will be removed. And the world was expanded for him. He said: Then He would say to the angels, “Reveal to them his reward.” And when they saw his reward, they would say: O Lord, no. Whatever afflicts him in this world benefits him."
36168,"(36168) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Talha, on the authority of Khaythamah, who said: God will expel Satan by a man. The turn 
(Ibn Al-Mubarak 331)"
36169,"(36169) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Khaythamiah, that he recommended that he be buried in The graveyard of the poor of his people."
36170,"(36170) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Talha, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: I know the location of a man who wishes to die. Twice in the year, and I thought he meant himself."
36171,"(36171) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: Blessed is the believer. How will he be preserved among his descendants after him?"
36172,"(36172) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: What do you recite in the Qur’an: Those who believe} Indeed, its position in the Torah is: O you poor people."
36173,"(36173) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Because I say: Glory be to God and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is great, more beloved to me than what I have seen. May the sun be upon him."
36174,"(36174) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Two words that are light on the tongue and heavy in the scale, two words that are beloved to the Most Gracious: Glory be to Him. God and praise be to Him, Glory be to God the Great."
36175,"(36175) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abd God, he said: Because I say: Glory be to God and praise be to God, and there is no god but God and God is greatest, that is more beloved to me than to give a number of them in charity. dinars for the sake of God."
36176,"(36176) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, who said: A man from Muhammad’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Whoever says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, and I seek forgiveness from God and I repent to Him, it will be written. On parchment, then a stamp of musk was printed on it, and it was not broken until He brought it to Him on the Day of Resurrection."
36177,"(36177) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: Because What I say is more beloved to me than carrying horses with their armor."
36178,"(36178) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: “Praise be to God, praise be to God” in Sahih. It is better for a believer than to travel, or to have the mountains of the world flow with him in gold."
36179,"(36179) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Al-Izar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: I heard him say: Saying “Tasbiha” at the request of a pilgrim is better than being rude to a pure man in a single year, or saying: “to your milk.”"
36180,"(36180) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, who said: Abd said: God: That I glorify God is more beloved to me than that I spend the number of dinars in the path of God."
36181,"(36181) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, and he said Abu Osama: I heard Musab bin Saad say: When the servant says: Glory be to God, the angels say: And with praise be to Him, and when he says: Glory be to Him By God and by His praise, they prayed for him, and Abu Asama said: She prayed for him."
36182,"(36182) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: When the servant says: Praise Thank God very much. The king said: How should I write? So he says: Write down My mercy upon him abundantly. And when he says: Glory be to God abundantly, the angel says: How should I write? So he says: Write down my mercy abundantly, and when God says, “God is great, great,” the angel says, “How do I write down?” Then he says: Write down for him My great mercy."
36183,"(36183) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Afaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Is any of you unable to recite the tasbih? A hundred times of His praise, and you will be rewarded with a thousand good deeds."
36184,"(36184) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saksaki, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, who said: He came A man of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned that he could not learn anything from the Qur’an, and he asked him something. He recited the Qur’an, so he said to him: Say, Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greatest, and there is no power or strength. Except in God"
36185,"(36185) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, or on the authority of his brother, On the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Those who are mentioned from the majesty of God from His glorification. And the praises of God and the praises of God coincide around the Throne. They have a sound like the sound of bees. They remind of their companion. Firstly, One of you would love for the Most Gracious to always have something to remind him of."
36186,"(36186) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: I heard Hani’ ibn Uthman speaking, on the authority of his mother Humaidha, son of Yasir, On the authority of her grandmother, Yusira, who was one of the female emigrants, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: With glorification, greatness, and sanctification, and hold them together with your fingertips, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection accountable and fully informed, and they will not be negligent and forget mercy."
36187,"(36187) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi’, who heard it from Abu Umar al-Sinni, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda', he said: I said: O Messenger of God, the rich are rewarded, they pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast. And they perform Hajj as we do Hajj, and they give alms, but we find nothing to give in alms. He said: So he said: Shall I not guide you to something that, if you do it, you will realize? Who came before you, and none will overtake you except those who have done what you do: You glorify God thirty-three times, And you praise Him thirty-three times, and you glorify Him thirty-four times at the end of every prayer."
36188,"(36188) Jarir and Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a similar manner."
36189,"(36189) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, who said: Abd said: God: That I glorify God is more beloved to me than that I spend my number of dinars in the path of God."
36190,"(36190) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Mahdi bin Maymun narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Yahya bin Aqeel, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: With all Your praise is sincere."
36191,"(36191) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jasri. On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Shall I not tell you that I love Speech to God. He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, tell me the most beloved speech to God. He said: I love speaking to God: Glory be to God and praise be to Him."
36192,"(36192) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Whoever The best deed is Glory be to Him the Hadith, and one of the worst deeds is blasphemy. He said: I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, and what is the Glory of the Hadith? He said: The man’s praise while the people are talking. He said: I said: What is blasphemy? He said: The people will be fine, so when they are asked, they say: Good news"
36193,"(36193) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said We were with Saad bin Malik, and he became silent, and he said: You have become silent, like the Nile and the Euphrates were watered, he said. We said, and you are not correct. He said: Glory be to God, praise be to God, and there is no god but God, and God is greatest."
36194,"(36194) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The son of Adam has not done any work that saved him from Hell by the remembrance of God. They said: Oh. Messenger of God, not even jihad in the way of God. He said: Not even jihad in the way of God, unless you strike with your sword until it is cut off. Then you multiply it until it breaks three times."
36195,"(36195) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Bishr bin Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said, He mentioned God's blessings in the morning and evening are better than cutting swords in the way of God and giving money as a weapon."
36196,"(36196) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Muadh, who said: To remember Allah from A morning until the sun rises is more beloved to me than being led to wage jihad in the path of God than a morning until the sun rises."
36197,"(36197) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: If a man spent the night giving The white people, and another spent the night reciting the Qur’an and remembering God. I would have thought that the one who remembers God is better."
36198,"(36198) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Abu Al-Wazi’, Jabir Al-Rasibi, on the authority of Abu Barza, He said: If there were two men, one of them holding dinars in his lap and giving them away, and the other remembering God, the remembrance of God would be better."
36199,"(36199) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no sheep more beloved to God than Thanks and remembrance."
36200,"(34200) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn narrated to me. Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, that he said: Those whose tongues are still moist from the remembrance of God will enter Heaven and they laugh."
36201,"(36201) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih informed us, he said: Amr ibn Qays al-Kindi informed me. On the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, that a Bedouin said: O Messenger of God, the laws of Islam have become many, so inform me of them. By what I cling to, he said: Your tongue never ceases to be moist from the remembrance of God."
36202,"(34202) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: Illuminate the remembrance of God and make your homes Your prayer is part."
36203,"(34203) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abu Alqamiya, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The people of the heavens will see the homes of the people of the Book shining for them just as the planets shine for the people of the earth."
36204,"(34204) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Muadh said: If only two men One of them mounts horses in the way of God, and the other remembers God. This would be greater, or better in reward. It means memory."
36205,"(34205) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi Al-Ja’d, who said: It was said to Abu Al-Darda’: Abu Sa’d ibn Munabbih made In his wealth is a freed one hundred. He said: As for a freed hundred in a man’s wealth, it is a lot of money. Shall I not inform you of something better than that? Bound by night and day, your tongue never ceases to be moist from the remembrance of God."
36206,"(34206) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: As long as a man’s heart He mentions God when he is in prayer, even if he is in the market, and if he moves his lips with Him, that is better."
36207,"(34207) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Qaraz, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever loves to enjoy the gardens of Paradise, let him remember God often."
36208,"(34208) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Masruq, who said: As long as a man’s heart remembers God, he is in it. Prayer, even if it is in the market."
36209,"(34209) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Saad bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Whenever a servant mentions God, it is in prayer."
36210,"(34210) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, On the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, he said: Whoever says ten times: There is no god but Allah Alone, with no partner to Him. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. He is like the slave of four slaves. I think he said : From the descendants of Ishmael."
36211,"(34211) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaji, on the authority of al-Bara’, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He who says there is no god but God alone, without any partners, to him belongs the kingdom, and to him is praise, and he is upon Him. All things are powerful, be like freeing your slaves."
36212,"(3621) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, she said: Who said A hundred times in the morning, and a hundred times in the evening. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. To Him belongs the kingdom and to Him is praise. And He has power over all things. No one will come on the Day of Resurrection with anything like what He brought except those who say the like of them, or more."
36213,"(36213) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Jahil, who said: Who said After the afternoon prayer: There is no god but Allah. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. Fight on the authority of those who say it. From tomorrow"
36214,"(36214) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Muslim, born in Suwayd. Ibn Jahil, on the authority of Suwayd, who was one of the companions of Omar, then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Waki’."
36215,"(36215) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Ayoub Al-Ansari, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says there is no god but God alone, without any partner, has Sovereignty, to Him belongs all praise, in His hand is goodness, and He is powerful over all things. Ten times, they are to Him as equal to ten slaves, or As a straight neck"
36216,"(34216) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Tha’labi narrated to me, on the authority of Amr ibn Shu’aib, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas said, If two men came, one from the east and the other from the west, one of them would go with him. He does not place any of it except in truth, and the other remembers God, until they meet on the road. He is the one who remembers God. The best of them"
36217,"(34217) Ali told us, on the authority of Musa al-Tahan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was pushed back. He greeted a group of people while they were remembering God, and said: God is pleased with your gathering, the people of heaven."
36218,"(34218) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said: His servants said Ibn al-Samit: It is more beloved to me to be among a people who remember God from the time they pray the morning prayer until the sun rises than I will be on horseback, striving in the path of God until the sun rises, and I will be among a people who remember God from When they pray the afternoon prayer, until the sun sets is more beloved to me than being on the backs of horses, striving in the cause of God until it sets. The sun"
36219,"(34219) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him a hundred times today."
36220,"(34220) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: I heard Al-Aghar and it was from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to Ibn Umar, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O People, repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him a hundred times today."
36221,"(34221) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughul, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Suqi, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If It is counted as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in one sitting saying: My Lord, forgive me and turn to me in repentance. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Forgiving. A hundred times"
36222,"(34222) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Zazan, he said: A man from the Ansar narrated to me He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying at the end of the prayer: O God, repent to me and forgive me. Indeed, You are the One who repents. The Forgiving one hundred times."
36223,"(34223) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah bin Abi Al-Hurr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burda, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came while we were sitting, and he said: I never had lunch without I asked God for forgiveness a hundred times."
36224,"(34224) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: Abu Darda’ used to say: Blessed are you. For whoever is found in his newspaper, he is denied asking for forgiveness."
36225,"(34225) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, God His servant’s repentance will be accepted as long as he does not repeat it. (Tirmidhi 3537. Ahmad 132)"
36226,"(34226) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I complained to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost my tongue and said: Where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? I ask God for forgiveness every day. A hundred times"
36227,"(36227) Affan told us, he said: Bukair bin Abi Al-Sumait told us, he said: Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: Whoever says, “I ask forgiveness from God, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting, and I repent to Him” five times. He will be forgiven, even if his sins are like the foam of the sea."
36228,"(34228) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz giving a sermon with his pinkies. So I heard him say: The best of servants is performing the obligatory duties and avoiding forbidden things."
36229,"(34229) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Azhar, the wine seller, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Al-Aziz, with his ring fingers, addresses people, wearing a patched shirt."
36230,"(34230) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Makhzum, he said: Omar Ibn Abi Al-Walid told me, he said: Omar came out Ibn Abdul Aziz, on the day of Friday, with a thin body, was giving a sermon as he used to give a sermon, then he said: O people, Whoever does good among you, let him praise God, and whoever does evil, let him ask forgiveness from God, for it is inevitable for people to do deeds that He has ordained. God is on their necks and has written it for them."
36231,"(34231) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ma’arif, and he said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz addressing the people with his mask and wearing two garments. Akhdaran, and he mentioned death, and said: Ghee is not like Ghanz, and Kadha is not like Kadha."
36232,"(34232) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, he said: I have not seen anyone who I think is more fearful of God than Omar. Bin Abdul Aziz."
36233,"(34233) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: I have heard that Omar bin Abdul Aziz addressed the people With his knowledge, he said: O people, you have come from near and far, and you have cleaned your appearance and created your clothes. The happy one is not the one whose animal or mount precedes him, but the happy one is the one who gets ahead of him."
36234,"(34234) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: He informed me on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Mention of blessings and gratitude for them."
36235,"(34235) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: It was the shirt of Omar bin Abdul Aziz. And his clothes are between the ankle and the ankle."
36236,"(34236) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Uqba, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to deliver sermons, saying: Among the most beloved things to God are kindness in seriousness, forgiveness in fate, kindness in guardianship, and a servant is not kind to a servant. In this world, God will be kind to him on the Day of Resurrection."
36237,"(34237) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abdul-Malik, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to say: Oh God The most righteous is he who was righteous. He was righteous to the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Oh God, and the family of whoever was in May peace be upon the mother of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
36238,"(34238) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abdul-Malik, he said: Tell me who saw Omar bin Abdul The Almighty is standing with his finger, and he is praying, and he is saying this with his finger, meaning he is pointing with it: O God, increase Mohsin He treated Muhammad well, and returned their wrongdoer to repentance, then he said: Thus, then he turned his finger: Oh God, and put down Behind them, with Your mercy."
36239,"(34239) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah bin Asma’ narrated to us, he said: Nafi’ narrated to us, he said: Abd said: King Ibn Omar to Omar Ibn Abdul Aziz: O Commander of the Faithful, what prevents you from going for what you want, by my soul With his hand, I do not care if you and I go to extremes in the pots. He said: This is true of you, my son. He said: Yes, by God. He said: Praise be to God who has made for me among my descendants someone who helps me in the matter of my Lord. O my son, if you were to show people what you say, why not? I believe that they will deny it, but if they deny it, I will find no alternative but the sword, and there is no good in the good that comes only by the sword. My son, I teach people the difficult sport, and if my life is long, I hope that God will perform something for me, even if it transgresses. I am on my way, for God knows what I want."
36240,"(34240) Affan narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah bin Asma’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Hakim, he said: Omar became angry. One day, Ibn Abd al-Aziz’s anger became intense, and his anger was intense, and Abd al-Malik, his son, was present. When they saw him, he His anger subsided, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, you are worthy of God’s blessings upon you, and in your place that God has placed you. In it, and God has not given you control over the affairs of His servants, you may attain wrath as I see. He said: How did you say? So he repeated his words to him and said: Don’t you become angry, O Abdul-Malik? He said: My inner effort will not avail me if I do not hesitate. He is so angry that nothing he hates appears from him."
36241,"(36241) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: As for what follows, there are people There are people who seek this world by doing the hereafter, and there are people who are storytellers who have introduced prayers upon their caliphs and princes. Their blessings be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So when this letter of mine comes to you, command them that their blessings be upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him and the prophets, and their supplication for the Muslims in general, and they leave behind everything else."
36242,"(36242) Saeed bin Amir told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz saying: What a blessing God has bestowed upon me. A servant of blessings, and he took them away from him, and he repaid him with patience for what he took away from him, except that the one who rewarded him was better than what he took away from him."
36243,"(34243) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Mawhib, on the authority of Salih ibn Sa’id al-Mu’adhdhin, who said: While I was with Omar Ibn Abd al-Aziz in Suwayda. She gave permission for dinner, so he prayed. Then he entered the palace, and when he came out, he prayed two rak’ahs. He said two light words, then he sat and hid himself, opened the nafal and continued to repeat it and recite it. Whenever he passed by a verse out of fear, he prayed. And whenever he passed by a sign of mercy, he supplicated until I called for dawn."
36244,"(34244) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I was sitting with Omar ibn Abdul Aziz, and he entered. Abdul-Ala bin Hilal was upon him, and he said: May God keep you, O Commander of the Faithful, as long as what remains is good for you. He said: He has finished. That is the case, O Abu al-Nadr, but say: May God grant you a good life and cause you to die among the righteous."
36245,"(34245) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: God does not hold the common people accountable for an act done by the elite, so if transgressions become apparent and are not denounced, they deserve it. All punishments. (Malik 991)"
36246,"(34246) Muhammad bin Abi Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Who did not His words are counted as part of his actions, his sins are many, and whoever acts without knowledge will do more harm than good."
36247,"(34247) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Abu Israel mentioned Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he said: Ali bin narrated to me. Bdhīmī, he said: I saw him in Medina and he was the best dressed among people, the most pleasant smelling of people, and one of the most beautiful people in his way of walking. Or people's imagination as he walked, then you saw him after walking like monks, so who told you that walking is quiet? So do not believe him after Omar bin Abdul Aziz."
36248,"(34248) Saeed bin Othman told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Misra, that a man came to Omar bin Abdul Aziz and said: I planted Then an army of the people of the Levant passed by it and spoiled it. He said: So he replaced it with ten thousand of it."
36249,"(36249) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, that Omar bin Abdul-Aziz advised his commander in the battle not to He rides any animal, except for an animal that keeps its track, the weakest animal in the army."
36250,"(36250) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, that Omar ibn Abdul Aziz was cooling off, and he said: So he carried He appointed a man to him on the post without his permission. He said: So he summoned him and said: Do not leave until you straighten him, then put him in The treasury"
36251,"(36251) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Juma bin Abdullah Al-Muqri, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz forbade Al-Barid to He put an iron point in the end of the whip to poke the animal with it. He said: And he forbade heavy bridles."
36252,"(36252) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Aamir bin Abd Qays said: Living in... Four: women, clothing, food, and sleep. As for women, by God, I do not care if I see a woman or a goat. As for clothing By God, I do not care about what you have shown your private parts, but as for food and sleep, they have overtaken me, and by God I will be harmed by them because of your efforts. He said Al-Hassan: By God, he harmed them both."
36253,"(34253) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Amir entered Ali’s house and there was no one with him except a person. In it are your drink and your food, and your food is in it."
36254,"(34254) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: The people who ruled the earth were from Aamir ibn Abd Qais, for example. The camel's foot"
36255,"(36255) Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ash’ayb narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, who said: I heard Abu Bishr He narrates on the authority of Saham bin Shaqiq, who said: I came to Aamir bin Abd Qays and sat at his door, then he came out and had washed himself, so I said: I think you like washing. He said: Perhaps you have washed. He said: What is your need? I said: I came for the hadith. He said: Your promise to me is the most beloved of the hadiths."
36256,"(34256) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, he said: Muhammad bin Sirin narrated to us, he said: It was said to Aamir bin Abdullah He said: Should he not get married? He said: I do not have any activity, nor do I have any money, so I would not tempt a Muslim woman."
36257,"(34257) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Amer bin Abd Qais said to his cousin: Leave your matter to God."
36258,"(34258) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Some of our sheikhs told us, he said: Aamir bin Abd said: God: I only find myself sorry for the sight of four things: the response of its muezzin, the thirst of the pilgrim, and because there are two deceitful people in it. And because it has my homeland."
36259,"(34259) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Saeed Al-Jariri told us, he said: When Aamir bin Abdullah, he said: His brothers joined him, and he said: At the beginning of the battlefield: He is a supplicant, so they believed, so they said: Come, for we were longing for him. This is from you, so he said: Oh God, he who asked me and lied to me and took me out of Egypt and separated me from my brothers. Increase his wealth and children, make his body healthy, and prolong his life."
36260,"(36260) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, he said: Someone who saw Aamir bin Abd Qais called for oil and poured it into his hand. He described Ja`far, and wiped one of them over the other, then said: {And a tree. It emerges from Mount Sinai, sprouting oil and a coloring for those who eat. He said, He oiled his head and his beard."
36261,"(36261) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Malik bin Dinar told me, he said: So-and-so told me, Amer bin Abdullah was in the desert and saw a dhimmi oppressing him. He said: Then Amer threw off his robe and said: Shall I not see a dhimmi? By God, you will be afraid while I am alive, so seek refuge from him."
36262,"(36262) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Fudayl bin Zayd Al-Raqqashi, who said: Do not let people distract you from yourself. For the matter comes to you rather than to them, and do not say: Cut off from us today with such-and-such, for he has reserved all matters against you. You worked on that, and you did not see anything quicker in realization or better in seeking than a good hadith for a great sin."
36263,"(36263) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Imran bin Hudayr told us, on the authority of Qasamah bin Zuhair, He said: Entertain the hearts with the remembrance."
36264,"(36244) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ghaylan, who said: Mutarrif bin Al-Shakhir used to say: O God, I seek refuge in You from... The evil of authority, and from the evil of what their pens create, and I seek refuge in You if I speak with the truth that I demand other than your obedience, and I seek refuge in I seek refuge in You if I adorn myself to people with something that will disgrace me before You, and I seek refuge in You if I seek help from any of Your disobedience against a calamity that has befallen me. By me, and I seek refuge in You lest you make me an example to any of your creation, and I seek refuge in You lest you make anyone happier with what you have taught me than me, O God. Do not disgrace me, for You know me. Oh God, do not torture me, for You have power over me."
36265,"(36245) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi ibn Maimun, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jarir, who said: I heard Mutarrif say: As if the hearts were not from us, and as if the hadith meant something other than us."
36266,"(36246) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi, he said: Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: I heard Mutarrif saying: If only someone would come to me From my Lord, so He gave me a choice: In Paradise or in Hell, or should I become dust? I chose to become dust."
36267,"(36267) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid al-Rishk, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: {Indeed, those who recite the Book of God And they established the prayer, until the end of the verse. He said: This is the verse of the Qur’an."
36268,"(36268) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, who said: Mutarrif said: There is no one among the people who is not He is foolish in what is between him and his Lord, but some fools are more foolish than others."
36269,"(36269) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, who said: A mutarrif used to say: Oh God, accept. My daily prayers, O God, accept my daily fast, O God, write for me my good deeds. Then he says: {Allah only accepts my The righteous}"
36270,"(34270) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, that Mutarrif bin Abdullah said: If it had been I have two souls, one of them would have priority before the other, so if it attacks something good, the other will follow, otherwise I will catch it, but it is only... One soul, I do not know whether you are attacking, good or evil."
36271,"(34271) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, that Mutarrif, he said: If the believer’s hopes were weighed And his fear is that neither of them will overpower his companion."
36272,"(34272) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Wasi’ al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: I was in Al-Hasan and Mutarrif, and so-and-so and so-and-so, mentioned some people, and Sa’id bin Abi Al-Hassan spoke, saying: Then he called, and he said: His supplication: O Allah, be pleased with us, O Allah, be pleased with us, twice or three times. He said: Mutarrif says while he is in the direction of the throat: Oh God, if You are not pleased with us, then pardon us. He said: So the people made you cry with these words."
36273,"(34273) Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Ghailan bin Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, he said: The concern of the people and them Nasnas, and people dipped in people’s water."
36274,"(34274) Shadhaan narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: People’s minds are according to the extent of their time."
36275,"(34275) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn al-Shakhir, in his saying: {They were a few of By night, they will not be hungry."
36276,"(34276) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: The best of matters are the middle ones."
36277,"(34277) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Mutarrif, that he came from his beginning, he said, so he made it easy. At night, his whip lit up for him."
36278,"(34278) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, that Mutarrif said: If I had the world, God would take it away. He gave me a drink of water that He would give me to drink with on the Day of Resurrection. He had given me a price for it for it."
36279,"(34279) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: We were at a turning point, so we remembered God and called upon Him. He said: By God, if this is from what has been mentioned before you, then God has intended good for you, even if it is from what is happening in Night and day, God intended good for you, so whatever that is, thank God for it."
36280,"(34280) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, that Mutarraf used to say: The hadith is, and the oath is by Allah."
36281,"(36281) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, that Mutarraf used to say: If goodness were in the hand of one of us He could not empty it in his heart until God is the one who empty it in his heart."
36282,"(36282) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, that Mutarraf used to say: If a man saw a hunter and the game He does not see it, and the pain that is about to take him overwhelms him. They said: Yes. He said: For Satan sees us and we do not see him, and he It befalls us."
36283,"(34283) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, Mutarrif said: I considered the beginning of this matter from whoever it was, so if It is from God, and I looked at who it was perfected by, and lo, it was perfected by God, and I looked at what it was made of, and lo, supplication took possession of it."
36284,"(34284) Shababah bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Thabit, that Mutarrif bin Al-Shakhir said: May the majesty of God be great in Him. Your chests, so God is not mentioned in such a situation. One of you says to the dog: May God disgrace him, and to the donkey, or the sheep."
36285,"(34285) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: We were talking about him not loving each other. There are two men for the sake of Allah, except that the best of them is the one who loves his companion the most. He said: When he walked, Ma’qur and Aamir bin Abdullah said: A terrified man met Mutarrif and started to remember him. Mutarrif said: Then I started saying: O brother, why are you imprisoning me when the stars are shining? And the night has passed, and he says: Oh God, for you, then he remembers the hour and says: O my brother, why do you imprison me when I have become foolish? The stars, and the night went, and he said: Oh God, in you, and when we morning, I was informed that he had gone, so I knew his night’s favor over me."
36286,"(34286) Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun narrated to us, he said: Ghaylan bin Jarir narrated to me, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: What A widow sitting on her tail is more in need of company than you."
36287,"(36287) Affan narrated to us, he said: Suleiman narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Mutarrif used to say: No one among the people has been given better than The mind"
36288,"(34288) Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Ghaylan bin Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: I saw in a dream It is as if I went out to go to the congregation, and I came to some graveyards in the neighborhood, and behold, the people of the graves were sitting, so I began to say my salutations and go on. They said: “O Abdullah, where do you want?” He said: I said: I want to combine. He said: Then I said: Do you know what the combined is? They said: Yes, and we know what it is. The bird will say that day. He said: I said: What will the bird say that day? They said: It will say: Peace, peace, a good day."
36289,"(34289) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ Yazeed bin Abdullah, on the authority of his brother Mutarrif, who said: God May He have mercy on the bird."
36290,"(34290) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, he said: I heard Mutarrif say: I did not pass. In a gathering, I heard someone praising me well, saying: So take that into account."
36291,"(34291) Ishaq al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: This death has ruined my life. The people of bliss are their bliss, so seek bliss in which there is no death."
36292,"(36292) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu’alli bin Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Muwarriq Al-Ijli said: “It is something I have been seeking for ten years that I have not been able to do, and I will never abandon its request.” He said, “And that is not the case, Father.” Al-Mu`tamir said: Silence about what does not concern me."
36293,"(34293) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, she said: Muwarriq was visiting us. He visited us one day and greeted him, and I returned peace to him. She said: Then he asked me and I asked him. I said: How? How is your child? He said: They are not available. I said: So praise your Lord. He said: By God, I feared that they would imprison me for your destruction."
36294,"(34294) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Some of our companions narrated to us, he said: He was a murriq. Al-Ijlili is a merchant and makes money, so do not come to him while he has something of it. He said: He used to meet his brother from Brothers, he gives you four hundred, five hundred, or three hundred, and says: Leave it for us until we need it. Then he meets him after that and says: What is your business with her? And the other says: I have no need for her, so he says: By God, we are not. Never take it, it's up to you."
36295,"(36295) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, he said: Muwarriq al-Ijlili said: I have not found anything for the believer in This world is an example, except like the example of a man on a piece of wood in the sea, and he says: O Lord, O Lord, perhaps God will save him."
36296,"(34296) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Tayyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muwarriq, he said: Al-Mutamisik By obeying God when people are cowardly, like a deserter after a deserter."
36297,"(34297) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, he said: I heard Muwarriq Al-Ajli say: What I saw a man more knowledgeable in his piety, and none more pious in his jurisprudence than Muhammad."
36298,"(34298) Affan told us, he said: Thabit bin Yazid Abu Zayd told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muwarriq, he said: It was only Their hadith is an exposition."
36299,"(34299) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He said Safwan bin Mahrez: If I eat a loaf of bread, I will strengthen my back, and drink a cup of water, and I will benefit from the world and its chaste people."
36300,"(36300) Affan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun narrated to us, he said: Ghailan bin Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Safwan bin Mahrez, he said: He and his brothers used to gather and talk, but they did not see that kindness. He said: Then they would say: Oh Safwan, tell your friends. He said: Then he says: Praise be to God. He said: Then the people will shed tears and their tears will flow as if they were from their mouths. Auction"
36301,"(36301) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rabah, on the authority of Safwan ibn Mahrez, that if He recited this verse and wept, until I saw that the test of his falsehood had been broken: {And those who have wronged will know to what turn they will turn}"
36302,"(36302) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, that Safwan bin Mahrez had a private chamber in which he had a trunk. Then the log broke, and it was said to him: Won’t you fix it? He said: Leave him, for I will die tomorrow."
36303,"(36303) Affan narrated to us, he said: Zayd bin Zuray’ narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, he said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Safwan Ibn Mahrez, in his saying: {Indeed, We created them by creation and made them virgins, Arabs, like-minded.} He said: By God, among them is the incapacity and the creeping God has shaped them as you hear."
36304,"(36304) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Al-Mu’alla bin Ziyad, he said: It was for Safwan bin Mahrez Al-Mazini is a flock in which he weeps, and he used to say: I may see the place of the martyr if you wish, meaning himself."
36305,"(36305) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: He said: Mas’ar narrated to us, saying: Utba bin Qays narrated to me, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, he said: Four Whoever has been given will be given the best of this world and the hereafter: He who has been given a remembering tongue, a thankful heart, and a patient body in the face of trials. And a believing wife who does not desire a traitor in herself. (Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 34. Al-Tabarani 11275)"
36306,"(36306) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, he said : The rights of God are too heavy for the servants to perform them, and the blessings of God are too great for the servants to count them, but they became They repented, and they turned repentant yesterday."
36307,"(36307) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abdul-Hamid bin Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yasar narrated to us, saying: He informed us Kulthum ibn Jabr said: The one wishing for insight used to say: His slaves are Talaq ibn Habib, and Helm is Muslim ibn Yasari."
36308,"(36308) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, he said: We said to Talq bin Habib: Describe for us piety. He said: Piety is an act of obedience to God, hoping for God’s mercy, with a light from God, and piety is abandoning disobedience to God, fearing God, with a light from God."
36309,"(36309) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Manyal, he said: Safwan bin Mahrez told me, he said: Jundub said: : The parable of one who preaches but forgets himself is the parable of a lamp that shines for someone else but burns itself, so that one of you may see what It will be placed in its belly, for when an animal dies, the first thing to burst from its belly is, and let one of you beware lest it be traversed. Between him and Paradise is a handful of Muslim blood. (Abdul Razzaq 18250)"
36310,"(36310) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Aban bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: A man from Arinah narrated to me, saying: He came out Jundub Al-Bajlili was on his journey, and some of his people went out with him until they were in the place where they were bidding each other farewell. Some, he said: Don't you see, the war is the one whose religion is at war, and the plundered is the one whose religion is robbed, no, there is no poverty after heaven, There is no sufficiency after the Fire, for the Fire does not free its captive, nor does its poor free it. Then he got on the road and set off."
36311,"(36311) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ghalib bin Ajrad, who said: A man from among the jurists of the people of Syria told me about A mosque in Minna. He said: God created the earth and created the trees on it, and none of the children of Adam would bring a tree from That tree unless good befalls it, or good is for it, and the tree did not remain like that until it spoke and the children Adam with the great word, “God has taken a son,” and the earth quaked and the trees shook."
36312,"(36312) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Qahdham, who said: Ibn Ziyad was brought a bundle containing wheat. Examples of palm trees were found in some of the homes of the Kasra family, with the words: This grew for such and such a time, meaning: It grew for a long time. It was done in obedience to God."
36313,"(36313) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Khaled Al-Ruba’i, who said: There was a man among the Children of Israel, and he was unknown. In knowledge, and that he invented an innovation, so he called the people and it was followed, and that he remembered one night, so he said: Oh, these people They do not know what you have invented. Doesn’t God know what you have invented? He said: He reached the point of his repentance that he burned his collarbone and put it in it. He chained it and tied it to one of the bracelets of the mosque. He said: I will not remove it until he repents to me. He said: So God revealed it to me. A prophet from among the prophets of the Children of Israel, and he did not deplore the revelation: Say to so-and-so: If only your sin had been in Between you and me, I would have forgiven you, but how about who of My servants I led astray, and he entered the Fire?"
36314,"(36314) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Marwan, who said: I heard Salih Aba Al-Khalil saying regarding the word of God: {Only those who fear Allah among His servants are scholars} He said: The most knowledgeable of them is the greatest in their fear of Him."
36315,"(36315) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: A man from the people of Sana’i told us, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Munabbih, he said: He passed A man with a monk, and he said: O Rahib, how is your remembrance of death? He said: I never raise one foot, nor lower the last, unless I see that I am Dead. He said: How have you been so active? He said: I never saw that anyone had heard of the mention of Jannah and Hell coming upon you quickly. He does not pray, so the man said: I will pray and cry until the grass grows from my tears, so the monk said: If you laugh while you Confessing your sin to God is better than crying while complaining about your deeds. The prayer of the one who is mourning does not rise above him, so the man said “Advise me,” and the monk said: “You must abstain from this world, and do not dispute with its people, and be like a bee if you eat.” It is eaten with good things, and if it is put in it, it is put in good things, and if it falls on anything, it will not harm it or break it, and be sincere to God as one is sincere. The dog is his family. They starve him and beat him, and he refuses to do anything except to be sincere and to protect them."
36316,"(36316) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I was informed that Ibn Munabbih used to say: I help morals. On the eternal religion in this world, and the verge of destruction is the following of desires, and from following desires is the desire for this world, Among the desires for this world is the love of money and honor, and from the love of money and honor is the permissibility of incest, and among the permissibility of incest is the wrath of God. And the wrath of God is a disease for which there is no cure except God’s pleasure, and God’s pleasure is a cure for which no disease is harmed, and who wants to He who pleases his Lord makes his soul displeased, and whoever does not displease himself does not please his Lord. Whenever something is heavy on a person, Of his religion he has abandoned, and he is on the verge of not having anything left of it."
36317,"(36317) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, who said: I heard Ibn An alarmist who says: We find in the Scripture that God says: O son of Adam, as long as you worship Me and hope in Me, then I will forgive you for what you have done. It was, and it is my right not to mislead my servant while he is eager for guidance, and I am the judge."
36318,"(36318) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Simak bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Ibn Munabbih, who said: The example of He who supplicates without action is like one who throws stones without Witr."
36319,"(36319) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Sulaiman Al-Daba’i, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ibn Munabbih, He said: God revealed to Uzair: O Uzair, do not swear by me falsely, for I do not accept someone who swears by me falsely. Uzair was dutiful to your parents, for whoever is dutiful to his parents, you are satisfied, and when you are satisfied, you are blessed, and if you are blessed, you reach the fourth line. O Uzair, do not disobey your parents, for whoever disobeys his parents, she becomes angry, and when she becomes angry, she is cursed, and if she is cursed, she reaches the lineage. Fourth"
36320,"(36320) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Saleh al-Fazari informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Maimun, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Alarming, he said: David said: O Lord, the son of Adam does not have hair except that underneath it are a blessing from you, and above it is a blessing from you. So, from where will he reward you for what you have given him? He said: Then God revealed to him: O David, I have been given much and I am satisfied. With ease, he expressed his gratitude, so that he would know that whatever blessings he had were from me."
36321,"(36321) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Wahhab bin An alarmist. He said: God gave Moses a light that would be fire for others. He said: So Moses called Aaron, and he said: God has given him light. It will be a fire for someone other than Me, and indeed, Moses was a gift to me, and I am a fan of you. He said: So the sons of Aaron used to offer sacrifices. The offering to the Children of Israel. He said: Then they made something and the fire came down and they were burned. He said: Then it was said to them: O Moses and Aaron, this is what I will do. Whoever disobeys me from among the people of my obedience, so what should I do with the one who disobeys me among the people of my disobedience?"
36322,"(36322) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abdul Hamid, the companion of Al-Zayadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Alarming, he said: Among those before you was a man who served God for a period of time, then he asked God for a pilgrimage and fasted seventy Sabbaths for God. He eats eleven times every Saturday. He said: He asked God for what he needed and He did not give it to him, so he turned to himself and said: O soul, I came before you. If you had any good, you would have given what you needed, but there is no good with you. He said: Then an angel descended to him at that time and said to him: O son of Adam, this hour of yours which you have made easy for yourself is better than All of your acts of worship that have passed, and God has given you the need you asked for."
36323,"(36323) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, saying: He who does not follow them narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Munbih, that he sat with a peacock. And some of the people of that time mentioned which of God’s commands is quickest, and some of them said: The word of God is like the twinkling of an eye, and he said Some of them: The bed when it was brought to Solomon, and he said: Ibn Munabbih: God’s command hastened, that Yunus was on the edge of the ship when God revealed to Nun about the Nile to Egypt, saying: And nothing fell from its edge except into its belly."
36324,"(36324) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sulaiman Al-Absi, on the authority of Idris bin Sinan, on the authority of his grandfather Wahhab bin Alarming, he said: On the day Moses spoke to his Lord by the tree, he was wearing a cloak of wool, a garment of wool, and a hood of wool."
36325,"(36325) Affan told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: Ibn Munbih said: One of the characteristics of a hypocrite is that he loves praise. And he hates slander."
36326,"(36326) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalababi’s book, he said: The likeness of the scholars is like the stars. Which he is guided by, and the signs by which he is followed. If they are absent from them, they become confused, and if they abandon them, they go astray."
36327,"(36327) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, that he said in his supplication: Oh God! I ask you to do good things, to abandon evil deeds, and to love the poor, and to turn to me in repentance. And if you intend to tempt your servants, You will leave me without being fascinated."
36328,"(36328) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: When God cursed Iblis, he asked him to look at it. Then he looked at him until the Day of Judgment, and said: By Your glory, I will not come out of the stomach or from the heart of the son of Adam as long as the spirit is in him. He said: By Your glory, I will not withhold repentance from him as long as the spirit is in him."
36329,"(36329) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Ayyub told us, he said: Muslim bin Yasar said: If Abu Your qalaba from the non-Arabs was Mobz Mobzan."
36330,"(36330) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: I heard Ayyub and he mentioned Abu Qalabahi, and he said: It was, by God. From the jurists and people of understanding."
36331,"(36331) Omar told us, he said: Ibn Mubarak told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, he said: The best of your affairs are the middle ones. (Abu Naim 286)"
36332,"(36332) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Wahhab bin Munabbih, he said: What The creation is in God’s possession, except as mustard greens from one of you."
36333,"(36333) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, on the authority of His father, he said: He was the best of them with them, meaning those of the past who were most peaceful in their hearts and the least of them in their absence."
36334,"(36334) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Uqba ibn Abi Yazid al-Qurashi narrated to me, saying: I heard Zayd ibn He became a Muslim. It is mentioned in the words of God: {And those who seek forgiveness by the pre-dawn prayers} He said: He who attends the morning prayer."
36335,"(36335) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: May God have mercy on a servant who stood When he is concerned, for no servant does anything until he is concerned. If it is good, he will accept it, and if it is evil, he will suppress it. about him"
36336,"(34336) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran Al-Qusayr, he said: I asked Al-Hasan about something, and I said: The jurists They say such-and-such. He said: Have you seen a jurist with your own eyes? The jurist is only the one who is ascetic in this world, the insightful one. With his religion, he who perseveres in worshiping his Lord."
36337,"(36337) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Al-Hasan said: The servant will never cease to exist. He is well - he does not know what will spoil his deeds. Yunus said: Among them are those who think that he is right, and among them are those who You overcome your lust."
36338,"(36338) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaid, and Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It used to be said: The heart of the believer is behind His tongue, so if one of you is thinking about a matter, he ponders it, and if it is good, he speaks about it, and if it is other than that, he keeps silent, and his heart The hypocrite is on the tip of his tongue, so if he is up to something, he speaks of it and makes it go away."
36339,"(36339) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Indeed, the believer has the best suspicions. In his Lord, he did good deeds, and the hypocrite has bad thoughts about his Lord, so he did evil deeds."
36340,"(34340) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Seek knowledge in a way that will not cause harm. of my servants, and I seek my servants in a way that does not harm knowledge, for whoever acts without knowledge will cause more corruption than He will fix it."
36341,"(36341) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, who said: Al-Hasan was a sad man."
36342,"(36342) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I have encountered people who cannot They make anything of work secret except they make it secret."
36343,"(36343) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hassan, he said: A man does good deeds and it is... Light in his heart and strength in his body, and indeed a man does evil and it becomes injustice in his heart and weakness in his body."
36344,"(36344) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. When they meet, the man says to his companion: Has it come to you that you are coming? He says: Yes, then he says: Has it occurred to you that you are leaving it? He says: No, then he says: So what is the reason for the laughter?"
36345,"(36345) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, he said: Dawud, the companion of Al-Basri, told me that Al-Hasan said: By God There is no servant to whom the provision of one day is apportioned and he does not know that it has been given to him, except one who is helpless, or of foolish mind."
36346,"(36346) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: By God, this is not the worst of days. The believer has days in which he will be brought near to him for his sake, and he will be reminded of what he had forgotten about his hostility, and his sins will be expiated thereby."
36347,"(34347) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I did not see No one is more loyal than Qari when he turns to you."
36348,"(34348) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid, Thabit, and Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, He said: On the path there will be a thorn and a thorn; there will be plenty of slippers and slippers on that day."
36349,"(34349) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man seeks the door of knowledge. So he works with it, and it will be better for him than if this world was his, and he would have it in the Hereafter."
36350,"(36350) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah ibn Shamit ibn Ajlan informed me, he said: My father informed me, He heard Al-Hasan say: The believer is sad in the morning and sad in the evening, and what suffices with suffering is sufficient for him."
36351,"(36351) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Ayoub told us, he said I heard Al-Hasan say: If you see a man He competes in this world and competes with him in the hereafter."
36352,"(36352) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {Indeed, her torment was love} He said: They knew that Every debtor separates from his creditor, except the debtors of Hell."
36353,"(36353) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Qurayh, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: {Corruption has appeared on land and sea, including The hands of the people have wrought. He said: God has corrupted them because of their sins on the land and sea of the earth, because of their evil deeds, so that they may They will return, and those after them will return."
36354,"(36354) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It has informed me that in the Book of God: The son of Adam are two You made them yours and they were not yours: a bequest of your property in a kind manner, and the property has become the property of someone else, and the claim of the Muslims While you are in a house in which you do not find fault with anything bad, and you do not add to what is good."
36355,"(36355) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, and he said: When Sa`id ibn Abi Al-Hassan died, Al-Hassan found him very sad. Severe, so he spoke about that, and he said: I have not heard God criticize sorrow for Jacob."
36356,"(36356) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Muhammad Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Whoever enters the graves, and he said: O God, Lord of the worn out bodies and the rotten bones that came out of this world while believing in You: enter upon them a soul. From You and peace from me. Every believer who has died since God created Adam has asked forgiveness for him."
36357,"(36357) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The believer is the sturdy one. He will hold himself accountable to God, but the reckoning will only be lightened on the Day of Resurrection for a people who will hold themselves accountable in this world. Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, the reckoning will be difficult for a people who took this matter from someone who was not held accountable. Indeed, the believer will be surprised by this matter. He is amazed and says: By God, I long for you and you are one of my needs, but by God, there is no way to reach you. There is a dispute between you and me, and something slips away from him and he returns to himself and says: I did not want this, what is wrong with me? For this reason, I have no number other than this, and by God, I will never return to this, God willing. Indeed, the believers are a people to whom the Qur’an has strengthened and its circumstances Between them and their destruction, the believer is a prisoner in this world, running to free his neck, and is not safe at anything. Until he meets God, he knows that he will be taken into account in all of that."
36358,"(36358) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Abd Rabbuh Abu Ka’b say: I heard Al-Hasan He says: The believer in this world is like a stranger. He does not compete in its glory, nor is he dismayed by its humiliation. People have a state and a different state. Direct this curiosity where God has directed it.
 Abu Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:"
36359,"(36359) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said Zakaria told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: Faith It is not by showing off, nor by wishful thinking. Faith is what is established in the heart and confirmed by action."
36360,"(36360) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Muhammad bin Juhada, he said, pass by Al-Hasan Bardhun turned to Hamlij and said: Oh, I know that when the Hour comes, it comes with grief."
36361,"(36361) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The believers hastened fear in this world. So God made them safe on the Day of Resurrection, and the hypocrites delayed fear in this world, so God made them fearful on the Day of Resurrection."
36362,"(36362) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The people did what they wished for."
36363,"(36363) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Mubarak, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say: There are people whose eyes cried but did not cry. Their hearts, so whoever’s eyes weep, let his heart weep."
36364,"(36364) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The worst of them is he who weeps."
36365,"(36365) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I encountered people who were wasting their papers. And they stored their tongues, then after them I found people who stored their letters and spread their tongues."
36366,"(36366) Yahya bin Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They are prudent, and if they are ignorant, they will not be fooled. This is their day, but how good is their night? The best night is when they ran their tears down their cheeks and lined up their feet seeking us. To God to free their slaves."
36367,"(36367) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I have not heard Al-Hasan reciting any verse of poetry except this verse: He who dies does not rest in a dead person, but rather a dead person is the dead of the living.
 Then he said: He spoke the truth, by God, he was alive even though he was dead in heart."
36368,"(36368) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Al-Hasan continued seeking wisdom until he uttered it."
36369,"(36369) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In his saying: {Woe to you from what you describe} He said: By God, every describer is a lie until the Day of Resurrection. Woe to you."
36370,"(34370) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Shahid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When God created Adam And your offspring. The angels said: The earth cannot contain them. He said: Indeed, I will bring death. He said: Then there will be no comfort in life. He said: Indeed, I am full of hope."
36371,"(34371) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Contemplating an hour of prayer is better than staying up all night."
36372,"(36372) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan Al-Saadi, who said: I heard Al-Hasan reciting this verse: 
The young man would be pleased with his pious self when he knew the pest that killed him."
36373,"(34373) Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. To his companions: You are to people like salt in food. He said: Then Al-Hasan says: Is food good except with salt? Al-Hasan says: How about a people whose salt has gone?"
36374,"(34374) Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I have overtaken them, by God, if it is Someone will live his life without ever having a garment folded for him, nor commanding his family to make food for him, nor is there any way in between him. And between the earth there is nothing at all."
36375,"(36375) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When his descendants were presented to Adam, he saw He preferred some of them over others. He said: My Lord, if You were to equalize them. He said: O Adam, I love to be thanked. His grace and they praise Me and thank Me. (Abdul Razzaq 19576)"
36376,"(34376) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, he said: What He entered a house in ruins, unless he entered it dusty."
36377,"(34377) Abu Asama told us, he said: Omar bin Hamza told us, he said: Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi told me Dhu’ayb, who said: Aisha said: I do not know of a man whom God has kept safe from people’s affairs and who has been upright in the ways of those before him. The integrity of Abdullah bin Omar."
36378,"(34378) Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: A man said to Muhammad bin Wasi’: Indeed, I love you for the sake of God. He said: The one for whom you loved me loved you."
36379,"(34379) Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Mujahid {That is the Day of Defeat}. He said : When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hell enter Hell."
36380,"(34380) Qubaysah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amara ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibn Shubramah, he said, I have never seen a living person. He is the most devout and jurisprudential sheikh of the Banu Thawr."
36381,"(36381) Qubaysah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Ali, he said: It was among us. Thirty men, none of them is smaller than Rabi’ bin Khathim."
36382,"(36382) Qubaysah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Utbah Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he was brought with a treacherous person. He did not eat it and said: This is the food of boys."
36383,"(36383) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’ al-Asadi, on the authority of Ibn Munabbih, he said: Faith is naked, its garment is piety, its wealth is jurisprudence, and its adornment is modesty."
36384,"(36384) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, he said: Amr bin Maymun was When he enters the mosque, he mentions God."
36385,"(36385) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If you learn, learn for yourself, for people have Their trustworthiness vanished. He said: He used to count the hadith, letter by letter."
36386,"(36386) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a sheikh of theirs, that Whenever he heard the questioner say: Whoever gives God a good loan, he would say: Glory be to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God and God. Greater, this is a good loan."
36387,"(36387) Qubaysah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Suriyat al-Rabi`, he said: al-Rabi’ ibn Khathim used to love And he says to us: Make food for me, and we prepare a lot of food for him. Then he calls a chick and so-and-so, and Rabih feeds them with his hand. And he gives them something to drink, and he drinks what is left over from what you drink, and it is said to him: These two would not know what you feed them, and he says: But God knows best"
36388,"(36388) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Bakhtari al-Ta’i, he said: He used to say: Make the living creatures miserable. Because of what you envy the dead, and know that your servants are not good except with asceticism and humiliation when obedient and difficult when you disobey. And he loved people as much as they were pious."
36389,"(36389) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Ishaq saying: Read. Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami The Qur’an has been in the mosque for forty years."
36390,"(36390) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Qais, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, who said: If the believer were On his reed in the sea, may God protect him from those who hurt him."
36391,"(36391) Ghandar Muhammad bin Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beware of injustice, for injustice is oppression. On the Day of Resurrection"
36392,"(36392) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Injustice will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection. (Bukhari 2447. Muslim 1996)"
36393,"(36393) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Jarir, he said: Salman said to me: Do you know what The injustices on the Day of Resurrection are the injustices done by people to themselves in this world."
36394,"(36394) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: God revealed to David, peace be upon him: Say to the oppressors: They do not remember me, for it is my right to remember those who remember me. And his remembrance of them means that I curse them."
36395,"(36395) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Thumama bin Bijad, he said: I warned you, I will get up, I will pray, I will fast."
36396,"(36396) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Do not postpone today’s work until tomorrow, for you do not know what tomorrow will do."
36397,"(36397) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: No If someone hears a hadith from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he will be among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He took it, neither more nor less than it, nor from Abdullah bin Umar."
36398,"(36398) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qais narrated to us, saying: Zurr said to me: Take us to this. We praise the mosque, meaning we pray."
36399,"(36399) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl {If he does not end Hypocrites and those in whose hearts is a disease} He said: those who commit immoral acts."
36400,"(36400) Al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Qais Al-Kindi (So when the rain comes Al-Kubra) said: When it is said: Take him to the Fire."
36401,"(34401) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, he said: Ibn Masoud passed by Those who blow the fury and fall."
36402,"(34402) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hakim ibn Jabir, who said: A man said to another man: Advise me, and he said: I will follow. A good deed erases it away, and create good manners with people."
36403,"(34403) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Mirdas al-Aslami, who said: The first righteous will go, so the first. Until there remain scum like the scum of dates and barley, God will not care about them at all. (Bukhari 4156)"
36404,"(36404) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard Zayd bin Aslam saying in these verses: {Do not be afraid, nor Be sad. He said: Do not fear what is before you, and do not be sad about what is behind you, and give good tidings of the Paradise that you were promised. He said: Good news comes in three situations: at death, in the grave, and at resurrection."
36405,"(36405) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: If God intends good for His servant He taught him the religion, increased it in this world, and made him see its faults. And whoever is given it has been given the best of this world and the hereafter."
36406,"(34406) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of a man from Ja`fi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Hatim, who said: The prayer never came except when I was in it. With longings, and they never came unless I was ready."
36407,"(34407) Qutayba bin Saeed narrated to us, saying: Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, that he said: See The one whom you would like to be with you in the Hereafter, give it to him today, and look for the one you hate to be with you and then leave him. Today"
36408,"(34408) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Sa’ib bin Baraka, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, who heard Abu Dharr say: I was walking behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Shall I not direct you to one of the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, he said: No. There is no power nor strength except with Allah. (Ibn Majah 3825. Ahmed 145)"
36409,"(34409) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he heard me while I was behind him, and I said: There is no power nor strength except in God. So he said: O Abdullah bin Qais: Shall I not guide you to this? One of the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, he said: There is no power nor strength except with God."
36410,"(34410) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd al-Madini, who said: Al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn narrated to me Hantab, on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, who said: I met Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, and he said to me: Shall I not order you to do what he ordered me to do? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to say many times: There is no power nor strength except with God, for it is one of the treasures. Heaven (Tabarani 3900)"
36411,"(36411) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir Al-Aslami, on the authority of Abul Zinad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Suleiman, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Shall I not direct you to a treasure of You will multiply the treasures of Paradise, and there is no might or strength except with Allah. (Tabarani 4885. Abdul bin Hamid 249)"
36412,"(36412) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Kumail ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no power nor strength except with God, one of the treasures of Paradise. (Nasa’i 10190. Ahmad 520)"
36413,"(34413) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: There is no power nor strength except with God, one of the treasures of Paradise.
(Ahmad 228. Tabarani 371)"
36414,"(34414) Qutayba bin Saeed narrated to us, saying: Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: Look at every deed. You hated death because of him, so leave him, and he will not harm you as long as he dies."
36415,"(34415) Qutaybah bin Sa’id narrated to us, saying: Ya’qub bin Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, that he said: He walks. This world distracts much from the hereafter. Then he said: You find a man occupying himself with other concerns, even more severely. Out of concern on the part of the person concerned for himself."
36416,"(34416) Qutaybah bin Sa’id narrated to us, saying: Ya’qub narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, that he said: You find a man working With sins, if it is said to him: Do you love death? He says: No, and that is it, and I have what I have. Then it is said to him: Will you not abandon what you You are committing sins, so he said: I do not want to leave it, and I do not like to die until I leave it."
36417,"(34417) Qutaybah bin Sa’id narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sahl, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In his saying: {Indeed, Hell is a lookout}. He said: They are waiting for you, by God. He said: While a man was passing by, another met him. He said: Did he inform you that there is a watch on the road? He said: Yes, he said: So be careful."
36418,"(34418) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I saw Abu Sinan on the day of Friday prayer, and his eyes were flowing and his lips were moving."
36419,"(34419) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: A man cannot be pious until he holds himself accountable more severely than A man will be held accountable to his partner until he sees where his food, drink, and earnings come from."
36420,"(34420) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, in his saying: {Whoever wants The life of this world and its adornments. We will repay to them their deeds in it, and they will not be deprived therein. He said: Whoever works for the world. He was fulfilled in this world."
36421,"(34421) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, he said: They said to Ibn Al-Munkadir: Which job is most beloved to you? He said: Bringing pleasure to the believer. They said: What remains of what you find pleasure in? He said: Showing kindness to the brothers."
36422,"(34422) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umayr, who said: Qays bin Al-Sakan entered the mosque and began to look. And he says: The most deserted of the mosque. The most deserted of the mosque."
36423,"(34423) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: He said to me: If you saw a people If you saw them, your heart would be cut off for them."
36424,"(34424) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: Hide your good deeds more than you conceal your bad deeds."
36425,"(34425) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qais, who said: Whoever recites two hundred verses while looking at the Qur’an No one came on that day better than him."
36426,"(34426) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: I have never seen anyone more knowledgeable about fatwa than Jabir bin Zayd, and I heard him. He says: I do not own anything in this world except a donkey."
36427,"(34427) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, in his saying: {Except that The friends of God, there is no fear upon them, nor do they grieve. He said: They are the ones who, when they see God, remember God."
36428,"(34428) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, he said: Abdullah said: Who would please him to know? Whatever he has with God, let him see what the people have."
36429,"(34429) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid: {Unless it is cut off. Their hearts} He said: Death."
36430,"(34430) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Salim: {And worship your Lord until certainty comes to you} He said: Certainty: death."
36431,"(34431) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim came to him. With sand, or sand was bought for him and placed in his house, or in his house, meaning he sits on it."
36432,"(34432) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sariyyat al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym, who said: Rabi’i’s work was secret."
36433,"(34433) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Malik narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Al-Shakhir, On the authority of Ibn Abbas {of purulent water}, he said: What flows between the skin and flesh of an infidel."
36434,"(34434) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {And on that day man will remember, and that The remembrance says, “I wish I had given my life.” He said: He knew, by God, that it would happen that there would be a long life and no death. It is the last thing on it."
36435,"(34435) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that one of those kings died. Then the people of his kingdom went around him and said: To whom will you leave the people and the land after you? He said: O people, do not be ignorant, for you are in the possession of one who does not care if the smallest thing is taken from his possession, or Big"
36436,"(34436) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The servant is still fine when he says to God and when he does For God's sake"
36437,"(34437) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: O son of Adam, indeed you have a secret, and indeed Your publicity, I am more in control of you than your publicness, and if you have action, and if you have speech, then your action is more in control of you than your speech."
36438,"(34438) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: O son of Adam, you will see the speckle in the eye. Your brother and leave the sadness in your eyes."
36439,"(34439) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, that Abu Al-Bakhtari And his companions used to bend his shoulders when he heard one of them praising him, or when a feeling of astonishment entered him, he would bend his shoulders and say: I submit to God."
36440,"(34440) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, it was said to Al-Hasan: O Abu Sa’id, shall I sleep? Satan said: Had he been heedless, every believer would have found it from his heart."
36441,"(34441) Affan told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, that he said: Evil has a family and good has a family. And whoever neglects anything, it will be sufficient for him."
36442,"(34442) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hisham informed us, on the authority of Hafsiya, on the authority of Ar-Rabi’ ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ka’b He said: By God, no double is settled for a servant on earth until he is settled for him in the people of heaven."
36443,"(34443) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa: Now that the strength in action is that you do not postpone today’s work until tomorrow, for if you do that, you will recover. There are deeds upon you, and you did not know which ones to take, but you neglected them. So, if you were given the choice between two matters, one for this world and the other... For the Hereafter, so choose the matter of the Hereafter over the matter of this world, for the world will perish, but the Hereafter will remain. Be of the presence of God Almighty. And learn the Book of God, for it is the spring of knowledge and the spring of hearts."
36444,"(36444) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever sees, may God bless him."
36445,"(34445) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Zakariya, who said: I have heard that when a man sees off any of his work, whatever he did before is nullified."
36446,"(34446) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kulayl, who said: I heard Jundub al-Alaqi say: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever listens, God will hear through him, and whoever dissents, God will dissatisfy through him. (Bukhari 6499 and Muslim 2289)"
36447,"(34447) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim ibn Badl, who said: I heard Abu Razin, he said: Abdullah said: Who He hears, God hears through him, and whoever dissents to God’s opinions, and whoever humbles himself out of humility, God will exalt him, and whoever is arrogant out of arrogance. God placed it."
36448,"(34448) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of a sheikh whose nickname was Abu Zaid, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who makes people listen to his actions will hear. Through Him, God will hear His creation on the Day of Resurrection, and He will despise them and belittle them. (Ahmed 223)"
36449,"(34449) Bakr bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Al-Mukhtar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Awfi, on the authority of Abu Saeed, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever hears, God will hear of him, and whoever sees, God will see. God bless him (Tirmidhi 2381 and Ibn Majah 4206)"
36450,"(34450) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I have realized people who they were. They will be so satisfied, if any of them were to eat, that when he regains his breath, he will be left with a shriveled, slimy mass, coming to his own devices."
36451,"(34451) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Whenever we entered upon Al-Hasan, we would leave, and we did not consider this world to be anything."
36452,"(34452) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {And there will be a distance between them and what they desire} He said: From faith."
36453,"(34453) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Al-Hasan said: From the signs, or the approaching of the Hour, that Death comes to choose you and picks them up just as one of you picks up fresh food from a plate."
36454,"(34454) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Salam bin Miskin, who said: Al-Hasan said: Indignize the world, by God. She would not be like that if she insulted her."
36455,"(34455) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The hermitages of the believers are their homes."
36456,"(34456) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In his saying: {So a wall was placed between them, with a door inside of which is the womb} He said: The jinn {and the torment appearing before it} He said: Fire."
36457,"(34457) Dhudha bin Khalifa narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan {And on that day man will remember, and indeed The remembrance says, “I wish I had given my life.” He said: “By God, he knows that there will be a long life and no death.” It is the last thing on it."
36458,"(34458) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He comes upon the people. For a time when speaking to them in their mosques is a matter of their world, and God has no need for it, so do not sit with them."
36459,"(34459) Jarir told us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In His saying: {But He will not bring you out of Paradise and cause you to be miserable} He said: He meant by it the miseries of this world, so do not meet the son of Adam except in wretchedness. Nasib"
36460,"(36460) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Al-Hasan recited this verse {And their father was righteous} He said: I have never heard him say anything good about their children. May God protect them as they protected their father."
36461,"(34461) Ibn Aliyah and Muhammad bin Abi Adiy told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no god but Allah. The price of heaven"
36462,"(34462) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, that Al-Hasan used to say: Beware of what God has forbidden. upon them and do good in what He has provided for them."
36463,"(34463) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan {Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter} He said In this world there is knowledge and worship, and in the afterlife there is Paradise."
36464,"(36464) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: {And do not forget your share of the world} He said: Give grace. And hold on to what they convey to you."
36465,"(34465) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan: On the Day of Resurrection"
36466,"(34466) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, who said: Al-Hasan recited until he reached the message: {And they do not remember Allah except a little} He said: It was only small because it was for other than God."
36467,"(34467) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, he said: Al-Hasan recited: {The repentant and worshipers} He said: They repented from polytheism and were exonerated. Of hypocrisy."
36468,"(34468) Affan told us, he said: Abu Aqeel Bashir bin Uqba told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: The scholars are three: Among them is a scholar of himself and of others. That is the best of them and the best of them. Among them is a scholar of himself and is good, and among them is a scholar who does not For himself, nor for anyone else, that is their evil."
36469,"(34469) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Who among you is able to To be an imam for his family, an imam for his life, an imam for whoever is after that, let him do it, for there is nothing that can be taken from you unless it is yours. There is a share in it."
36470,"(34470) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I have encountered people who are intent on O God, do not turn away a beggar."
36471,"(34471) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he recited: {And ask them about the village that was By the sea when they transgressed on the Sabbath, when their whales came to them on the day of their Sabbath lawfully. God be upon them on a day and made lawful for them other than that, so he used to come to them on the day that was forbidden to them. It was as if it was labor, and no one could stop it, so they began to worry and worry until they took him and ate, by God. The most shameful food that Lot’s people ate, the most disgraceful in this world and the most severe his punishment in the hereafter, and God’s oath is greater for the believer. Sacred to God than a fish, but God has made the appointed time for your people the hour, and the hour is His best and most commanding."
36472,"(34472) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: We used to talk about it, that if the servant wants it, I think it will be done to him. He said good, and made him a rebuke of himself, enjoining him to do good, and forbidding him from evil."
36473,"(34473) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abdul-Hamid bin Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yasar narrated to us, saying: He informed us Kulthum ibn Jabr said: The one wishing for insight used to say: The good jurisprudence and piety of Muhammad ibn Sirin and his servants was Talq ibn Habib and dream of Ibn Yassar."
36474,"(34474) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Asim, he said: I heard Muwarriq al-Ijali saying: I did not see No one is more learned in his piety, and none is more pious in his jurisprudence than Muhammad, and Abu Qalabab said: Spend him wherever you wish, and you will find him. The most pious of you and the most faithful of you to himself."
36475,"(34475) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I do not know anything about religion."
36476,"(34476) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Salam bin Miskin narrated to us, he said: Imran bin Abdullah bin Talha narrated to us. Al-Khuza’i said: The soul of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab was easier for him in the presence of God than the soul of a fly."
36477,"(34477) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that Saeed bin Al-Musayyab was He often says in his meetings: O God, grant us peace, grant us peace."
36478,"(34478) Affan told us, he said: Abu Awana told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: Ka’b said: God never looked at Paradise except that He said: It was good for your family, and it became more good than it was until they entered it. Welcome (Tabarani 75)"
36479,"(34479) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Imran al-Juniy told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Ka’b, said: Abraham said: O Lord, it saddens me not to see anyone on earth worshiping You. Other than him, so God sent angels to pray with him and be with him."
36480,"(34480) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, On the authority of Ka`b, he said: The world is cursed. Cursed is it. Nothing is in it except a good learner, or a teacher."
36481,"(34481) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told me, on the authority of Mutarrif, that Ka’b said in His saying: {And raised furniture} He said: On a journey of forty years."
36482,"(34482) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Zayd bin Aslam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: The ruler will be brought in goodness on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: Answer your Lord. Then he will be taken to his Lord, but no It will be hidden from him, then he will be taken to Paradise and he will see his abode and the abode of his companions who used to agree with him on it. And they will help him with it, and it will be said to him: This is the abode of so-and-so and this is the abode of so-and-so, and he will see what he has prepared. God will grant him some honor in Paradise, and He will see your status as better than theirs, and He will clothe you with the garments of Paradise and will be placed in On his head is a crown, and he is enveloped in the scent of Paradise, and his face shines until it is like the moon. Hammam said: I think so. He said: For the night of the full moon. He said: Then he will go out and no people will see him except that they will say: Oh God, make him one of them, until he comes. His companions who used to agree with him on goodness and help him with it, and he would say: Give good news, O so-and-so, for God has He has prepared such-and-such for you in Paradise, and He has prepared such-and-such for you in Paradise, and He continues to inform them of what God has prepared for them in it. Paradise is so honorable that their faces will be covered in white like the white on his faces, so people will recognize them by their whiteness. their faces, and they will say: These are the people of Paradise. And the ruler of evil will be brought and it will be said to him: Answer your Lord, and he will depart. He will be brought to his Lord, and he will be withheld from him and will be commanded to the Fire, and he will see his position and the positions of his companions, and it will be said: This is The house of so-and-so and this is the house of so-and-so, so he saw what God had prepared for him in it of humiliation, and he saw your house as worse than Their homes. He said: Then his face would be blackened and his eyes would be blue, and a hood of fire would be placed on his head. Then he would go out, but no He saw a family of people except that they sought refuge in God from him, so his companions who used to agree with him against evil would come to him. And they help him. He said: Then they say: We seek refuge in God from you. He said: Then he says: God has not protected you from me. Then he says to them: Do you not remember, O so-and-so, such-and-such? He reminds them of the evil they used to deal with and help them against, so what? He will continue to inform them of what God has prepared for them in the Fire until their faces become as black as his face. Then people will recognize them by the blackness of their faces, and they will say: These are the people of Hell."
36483,"(34483) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, he said: My father told us: If one of you sees any of her adornment, This world and its afflictions, let it come to its family, let it command them to pray, and let it be patient over it, for it is God, he said To his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: {And do not direct your eyes to that with which We have entertained a couple of them} Then he recited to another. The verse"
36484,"(34484) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: If you see a man doing good deeds, Know that she has sisters, so good deeds indicate her sister, and if you see him doing evil, know that She has no sisters, for the bad deed indicates her sister."
36485,"(34485) Yahya bin Bukair told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: The sweetness of this world is the bitterness of the hereafter, and the bitterness of this world is the bitterness of the hereafter."
36486,"(34486) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The believer does not attain His religion except its pit."
36487,"(34487) Abu Asama told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Omar told me, on the authority of Bishr bin Asim, he said: Tawoos said: I have not seen anyone like him. He believed in himself: I saw a man who, if it were said to me: Who is the best person you know, I would say: So-and-so to that man, and he remained like that. Then a pain in his stomach took hold of him, and something happened to him, so he wiped his stomach over him and lusted after him, so she revealed himself and saw him in a state of pain. I don't know what kind of energy he had faster until he died of sweating."
36488,"(34488) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: It was his shirt. Over the garment and the robe over the shirt."
36489,"(34489) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Is there a man who performs ten days of prayer during the night, and in the morning he A hundred good deeds and more were recorded for him."
36490,"(36490) Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: Trusting in God is all Faith"
36491,"(36491) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he used to say: Oh God, I I ask you to sincerely trust in You and have good faith in You."
36492,"(36492) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Atiq, who said: I gave Saeed bin Jubayr a drink of honey in He took a cup and drank it, then said: By God, I will ask about this, so I said: Why? He said: I drank it while I enjoyed it."
36493,"(36493) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, who said: I read the letter of Saeed bin Jubayr to my father: O Abu Omar, eat A day on which the Muslim will live and become a spoil of war."
36494,"(34494) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr: {Rather, the deception of the night and the day} He said the night and the day passed."
36495,"(36495) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The remembrance of God in The heedless are like the protectors of those who seek reward."
36496,"(34496) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr {And it is not in jest} He said: It is not a game."
36497,"(36497) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr {so curse be upon the inmates of the burning fire} he said: Wadi In Hell"
36498,"(34498) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: {O My servants who have believed, indeed My earth is spacious} He said: Whoever is commanded to disobey you, let him flee."
36499,"(36499) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Al-Asbagh bin Zayd informed us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, that Sa’id bin Jubayr repeated these verses: {And fear a Day in which you will be returned to Allah} twenty times."
36500,"(36500) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, regarding his saying: {Indeed, We have guided you}. He said: Repent."
36501,"(36501) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zubayri narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Sa’id bin Mighty {Rather, man is a watcher over himself} He said: He is a witness to himself, even if he excuses himself."
36502,"(36502) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr {It is no doubt that theirs is the Fire and that they Neglected} He said: Forgotten and lost."
36503,"(36503) Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr {And We write down what they put forward and their traces} He said: They have not forgotten."
36504,"(36504) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: He says, meaning God, Blessed be He. And God Almighty: What is the matter with people who pursue understanding other than My worship? They wear the saddle of sheep, and their hearts are more bitter than patience. My Father. Are they deceived or are they deceiving Me? I have sworn by Me that I will give them temptation in this world, leaving the wise among them bewildered. (Ibn Al-Mubarak 50)"
36505,"(36505) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, that a tyrant is among the tyrants. He said: Do not stop until I look at whoever is in the heavens. He said: So God gave power to the weakest of His creation over him, and a residue entered his nose. Then death took hold of him, and he said: Strike my head, so they struck him until they scattered his brains."
36506,"(34506) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Rabi’, who said: I heard Abu Ubaidah say: The just ruling To silence voices from God, and indeed, an unjust ruling leads to many complaints to God."
36507,"(36507) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah: {Indeed, these are a group of people.} A few} He said: They were six hundred thousand and seventy thousand."
36508,"(34508) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: I heard Abd al-A’la al-Taymimi say: He who is given knowledge that does not It is a cry for a person not to have been given knowledge that would benefit him, because God described the scholars, then he read to his statement. {They cry}"
36509,"(36509) Abu Usama told us, he said: Abd al-A’la al-Taimiy said: There is no dweller except the angel of death who visits them twice a day."
36510,"(36510) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abd al-A’la al-Taymi, who said: The jinn and hell are the ones who hear Children of Adam, when a man asks the jinn, she says: O God, let him enter it, and when he seeks refuge from the Fire, she says: O God, grant him protection. From me"
36511,"(36511) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Abu Salih used to lead us in prayer, but he did not explain the recitation of ruqyahs."
36512,"(36512) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: The people will be gathered in this way. He placed his head and held his right hand over his left, at his chest."
36513,"(36513) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih: They see that the torment is lightened for the people of the graves between the two blows, so when the second blow comes, they say: {Ya Woe to us who has been resurrected from our resting place."
36514,"(36514) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: Blessed is a tree in Paradise if it rides. He rode his hip, or his trunk, and circumambulated it until he reached the place where he rode, until the old man killed him."
36515,"(36515) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, he said: Abu Sinan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murah, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: On the Day of Resurrection, those to whom He sent the messengers will be judged, and whoever disobeys him will enter Paradise, and whoever disobeys him will enter Hell: And there will remain a people of the children and those who perished during the period and those whose reason has been defeated, and the Lord, Blessed and Most High, will say to them. You have seen that I only admit to Paradise those who obey me, and I admit to Hell those who disobey me, and I command you to enter this Fire. Then a neck from it will emerge for them. Whoever enters it will be saved, and whoever turns away and does not enter it will be destroyed."
36516,"(36516) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Salih {faces that day will be radiant}. He said: Beautiful {to Her Lord is the Watcher} He said: She awaits reward from her Lord."
36517,"(36517) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya, that when he prayed, it was as if he was speaking to a man of Iqbal’s rank. May his prayers be upon him."
36518,"(36518) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya, who said: If there was a funeral among them, that would be known. In their faces for days."
36519,"(36519) Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-A’mash, who said: When Yahya had finished the prayer, he would stay there. Soon you will learn about the burden of prayer."
36520,"(34520) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Dirar bin Murra, who said: I met Al-Dahhak in Khurasan, and I was wearing a fur coat of good character, so he said Al-Dahak: Abu Idris said: A pure heart in dirty clothes is better than a dirty heart in pure clothes."
36521,"(34521) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha Al-Yami, on the authority of Abu Idris, a man from the people of Yemen, he said: He was saying: O God, make my sight a lesson, my silence a reflection, and my reason a remembrance."
36522,"(34522) Abu Asama told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, he said: Abu Muslim said Al-Khawlani: People used to be paper without thorns, but today they are thorns without leaves. If you insult them, they will insult you. You criticize them, they will criticize you, and if you leave them, they will not leave you."
36523,"(34523) Sa’id bin Shurahbil told us, he said: Laith bin Sa’d told us, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: I sat One day, Al-Khawlani came to Abu Idris while he was storytelling, and he said: Shall I not tell you who was the best of people to eat? So when He saw that people were looking at him, and he said: Yahya bin Zakariya was the best of people to eat, but he used to eat with the beast. He hates mixing with people in their daily lives."
36524,"(34524) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Abu Muslim said Al-Khawlani: I have not done anything that would make me care who saw me except my need for my family and my need for excrement."
36525,"(34525) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Idris, he said: No, he will not destroy you. May God cover a servant with an atom’s weight of goodness in his heart."
36526,"(34526) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Abu Muslim al-Khawlani, who said: Four shall not be accepted in Four: the property of an orphan, deceit, betrayal, and theft are not accepted in Hajj, Umrah, or Jihad, and he mentioned one letter. Another"
36527,"(34527) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Abu Uthman al-Naddi said: I know when My Lord reminds me. They said: How is that? He said: God says: {So remember me, I will remember you} so when I remember God He reminded me."
36528,"(34528) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Zainab told us, he said: I heard Abu Uthman say: What In the Qur’an, there is a verse that I consider more hopeful for this nation than its saying: {And others confessed their sins, mixing one good deed with another. Bad}"
36529,"(34529) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah: {They were not sleepy during the night}. He said: They sleep little at night until the morning."
36530,"(34530) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah: “None shall touch it except the purified.” He said: No. You, you are the ones who commit sins."
36531,"(36531) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Manyal, that Abu Al-Aali saw a man performing ablution, and when he finished, he said: Oh God, make me among those who repent and make me among those who purify themselves. He said: Purifying oneself with water is good, but they are the ones who have been cleansed of sins."
36532,"(36532) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, that if he wanted To complete the Qur’an at the end of the day, he delayed it until evening, and if he wanted to complete it at the end of the night, he delayed it until evening. In the morning"
36533,"(36533) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: The companions of Muhammad said to me, “Pray May God bless him and grant him peace: Do not work for anyone other than God, for God will leave you to whomever you work for."
36534,"(36534) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: I heard an old man being told: “Zufr” mentions, on the authority of Qays ibn Habtar, He said: The shock is from Satan."
36535,"(34535) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, on the authority of some of his companions, he said: The night did not come upon a servant. Not at all. She said: Son of Adam, do something good to me, for I will never do evil to you."
36536,"(36536) Abu Osama narrated to us that Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam narrated to him, saying: I heard Hammad saying: I heard Ibrahim saying: If Indeed, a servant who conceals himself with worship just as you conceal yourself with immorality - God will make that clear from him."
36537,"(36537) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were ashamed to increase. And they hate decrease, and He says: It is a permanent thing."
36538,"(36538) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, he said: They claimed that Abraham used to say: We were when we were present. A funeral, or we heard of a dead person, and this will be known to us within days, because we have known that a matter has befallen him that has become a matter of fate. Heaven, or Hell, and that you speak at your funerals the conversation of your world."
36539,"(36539) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Among us was a man who was a worshipper with a woman when he was baptized. So he struck her thigh with his hand. He said: Then he took it with his hand and put it in the fire until it became hot."
36540,"(36540) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Hawshab, he said: Abraham said: I rarely read these verses except I mentioned the coldness of the drink: {And there will be a barrier between them and what they desire}"
36541,"(36541) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zakaria al-Abdi, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he wept during his illness, So they said to him: O Abu Imran, what makes you cry? He said: How can I not cry when I am waiting for a messenger from my Lord to bring me good tidings? Either with this or with that."
36542,"(36542) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, who said: Ibrahim saw Amir Helwan passing by with his animals. He planted a plant, and he said: Being unjust in a way is better than being unjust in religion."
36543,"(34543) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding his saying: {hot and dark}. He said: Al-Ghasaq: what is cut off from Their skins, and what flows from their skin."
36544,"(34544) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid: {Man will be informed that Day of what he has put forward and what will come back} They said: With his first and last deeds."
36545,"(36545) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim: {And We will surely make them taste the lesser punishment, apart from the greater punishment} He said: Things they are afflicted with in this world."
36546,"(36546) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, saying: Abraham was reading from the Qur’an, and when a person entered upon him, He covered it and said: I do not see me reciting it every hour."
36547,"(36547) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Abraham mentioned that Al-Mukhtar bin Abi was sent to him. Ubaid, he said: He painted his face with paint and drank medicine but did not come to them, so they left him."
36548,"(34548) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Whoever seeks Anything of knowledge that God seeks. God has given him of it what is sufficient for him."
36549,"(36549) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Humility is in the heart."
36550,"(36550) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There were those before you who wore shatter clothes. And He has compassion for hearts."
36551,"(36551) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Suqi, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a man says in the morning: I seek refuge in the Hearer The All-Knowing One is protected from Satan, the accursed, ten times. He is protected from Satan until the evening, and when he says it in the evening, he is protected from Satan. Until morning."
36552,"(36552) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awanan, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Abraham’s shirt was on the back of The foot"
36553,"(36553) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abraham, “that they may return.” He said: They will repent."
36554,"(34554) Ali bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He honors a people In Paradise, a people will be in Hell, and they will say: What is the matter with you in Hell? But we were only working according to what you taught us. They said: We were teaching you. And we do not work with it."
36555,"(36555) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi {and ascents upon which they appear} He said: stairs."
36556,"(36556) Ja’far ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi {And ascens upon which they emerge} He said: Stairs, and a roof, he said: logs, and decoration, he said: gold."
36557,"(36557) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: I heard Ubaid Allah bin Al-Ezar, who said: The Day of Resurrection will be The Resurrection is like a nobility in a horn, and the happy one is he who finds a place for his feet to place them, and at the scales there is an angel calling out. Indeed, so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, had heavy scales, so he was so happy that he would never be miserable after it. Indeed, so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, was light. His scales are so miserable that he will never be happy again."
36558,"(36558) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, who said: He used to say: God’s blessings upon me in what He took away from me from this world is greater than His blessings upon me in what He gave me from it."
36559,(36559) Abdullah bin Idris told us that he heard his father and uncle mentioning this. They said: Abdul-Malik bin Iyas was one of those who heard it. Then he remained silent.
36560,"(36560) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The most impressed people of Kufa to me are four: Talhah. Zubaid, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, and Yahya bin Abbad."
36561,"(36561) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: I said to Talhah: Indeed, Tawoos hated groaning, so he said: So what His groaning was heard until he died."
36562,"(36562) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, who said: The blind Zaid gave me a letter in which it was written that a man had bequeathed His son, he said: O my son, be one of those who distanced yourself from him with enrichment and purity, and be close to those who approached him softly. And His mercy, His disavowal is neither arrogance nor greatness, nor is His closeness deceitful, nor is it treachery. He does not hasten in what He has deceived, and He pardons. From what has become clear to him, let no one be deceived by his ignorance, and let him not forget to take stock of what he has done. If he mentions it, he fears what they say. And ask forgiveness for what they do not know. He says, “My Lord knows me better than I know myself, and I know myself better than others.” He asks to know. He speaks for sheep, is silent to greet them, and mixes with those who understand them. If he is among the heedless, he is written among those who remember. He was among those who remember. He was not written among the heedless, because He remembers when they neglect, and does not forget when they remember. Hussein said: Ibn Uyaynah added to it: He mixes knowledge with the dream of his increase in what vanishes and his desire in what remains."
36563,"(34563) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Manhal, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: If God wanted the people of Hell to forget me, He would make for every one of them a coffin of fire. On its level, then it was closed with padlocks of fire, so that no vein would be struck from it unless there was a nail of fire in it. Then that was made The coffin is in another coffin of fire, then it is closed with locks of fire, then a fire is lit between them, so that none of them can see it. That there is someone in the Fire other than Him, that is the saying of God Almighty: {For them in Hell is a resting place, and above them is a covering of clouds. And thus We recompense the wrongdoers.}"
36564,"(36564) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, who said: Indeed, God will make peace with goodness. The servant begot him, and he begot his child, and the people of his city, and the people of the cities around him, and they will continue to be under the protection of God as long as Between them."
36565,"(36545) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Hamran bin Ayan, on the authority of Abi Harb bin Abi Al-Aswad Al-Daili said: A man will be imprisoned at the gate of Paradise for a sin he has committed for a hundred years, and he will see his wives. And he served you"
36566,"(36546) Mu’awiyah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bakhtari al-Ta’i, who said: It used to be said: Living beings are blessed with what is blessed. By Him the dead, and know that the servants are not righteous except through abstinence and humility when obedient, and difficult when disobeying, and love People are as pious as they are."
36567,"(34567) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughul, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn al-Walid {So when the great catastrophe comes} he said: When the people of Paradise are driven to Paradise and the people of Hell to Hell."
36568,"(36568) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, I think, on the authority of Uthman, who said: Whoever does a job, God will cover him with a robe. His work"
36569,"(36569) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: Othman bin Affan said: Whoever does a good deed God covered him with his robe. If it is good, it is good, and if it is bad, then evil."
36570,"(34570) Waki’ and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Yahya bin Rafi’, who said: I heard Othman say: {And every soul came with it a driver and a witness} He said: A driver drives it to the command of God, and a witness. He bears witness to what she did."
36571,"(34571) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythama, on the authority of Adiy bin Hatim, who said: Ayman A man and his hair is what is between his beard."
36572,"(36572) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: You are in a time that is known and denied, a time that has passed, and what is denied is known, a time that has yet to come."
36573,"(34573) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abu Mansour, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, who said: I went out to the grave and sat there next to the wall, then a man came to a grave and leveled it, then he came and sat next to me, so I said: Who is this? He said: My brother. He said: I said: A brother to you. He said: A brother to me in Islam. I saw him yesterday in what the sleeper sees, so I said: So-and-so has lived, praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. He said: I have said it, because being able to say it is more beloved to me than the fullness of the earth. And what is in it? Did you not see that when they were burying me, so-and-so got up and prayed two rak’ahs so that I would be able to I pray whatever is dearer to me than the world and what is in it."
36574,"(34574) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, who said: For those who are masked Imprisonment will cause people to stomp on their faces on the Day of Resurrection."
36575,"(34575) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, he said: Muawiyah bin Bashir told me, he said: I see it, on the authority of his father, he said: Khabab said: She will be screaming, so listen to her."
36576,"(36576) Affan narrated to us, he said: Suleiman narrated to us on the authority of Thabit, he said: Ibn Abi Layla said: I roamed these places, but what I saw someone who was more diligent and was not early in remembering Allah than the people of Basra."
36577,"(34577) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Salami, he said : The angel comes to one of you every morning with a white scroll, and let him fill it with good things. When the sun rises Let him fulfill his need, then when he prays the afternoon prayer, let him fill it with goodness, for when he dictates the first and last of his prayers, It was good, perhaps what was between them would be enough."
36578,"(34578) Ibn Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, who said: They will pass through the Fire while... It is extinguished, and they say: Where is the fire that We were promised? He said: You passed by it while it is extinguished."
36579,"(34579) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Musa bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, he said: He was Saeed. Ibn Aamir Ibn Hudhaym was the Emir of Egypt, and he informed Omar Ibn Al-Khattab that there would come a time when he would not smoke in his oven. So he sent money to him and he bought what was good for him and his family, then he said to his wife: If only We had given it to a merchant, perhaps he would It will be a blessing for us. She said: So do it. He said: So the man gave it in charity and gave it until there was nothing left of it. Then they were in need. Then his wife said to him: If you had only looked at those dirhams and taken them, we would have needed them, so he turned away from them, then She came back, and she said again, so he turned away from her until he made it clear to her that he had fulfilled it. He said: So she started blaming him. He said: So he sought help. Ali approached Khalid bin Al-Walid, so he spoke to her and said: You have harmed him, so it was as if he had tempted her with him, so she said to him also, so when That man saw blessings on his knees and said: I would not be pleased if I were withheld from the first neck on the Day of Resurrection, nor would I be He would not have appeared on the earth, and if He had chosen one of the good things and pointed out its fingers to the people of the earth from above the heavens, it would have been found. Their fragrance, so I invite you to them, because I invite you to them is better than to invite them to you, but when she saw that, she stopped it. (Abu Naim 244)"
36580,"(36580) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: A man passed by Rabi’ bin Abi Rashid and he was sitting. On one of the shoe boxes, and he said: If you enter the mosque and sit with your brothers, then Rabi’ said to him: If a male leaves Death was in my heart quickly, I was afraid that my heart would be corrupted."
36581,"(36581) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Shuaib, who said: Abu Zumail Rabi’ bin Abi Rashid was To Mecca, and one day he said: If I only knew the work I love most dear to my Lord, perhaps I would be able to do it for Him. He said: Then he saw it in a dream. Thanks and remembrance."
36582,"(36582) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, he said: Rabi’ bin Abi Rashid met me at the gate in the market. So he took my hand and shook it with me, and said: O Abu Dharr, whoever asks God for His pleasure has asked Him for a great matter."
36583,"(34583) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Aoun bin Shaddad, that when Haram bin Hayyan Al-Abdi died, they said: He said: O Haram, advise me. He said: I advise you to fulfill my debt. They said: What do you recommend? He said: So he recited the last Surah An-Nahl {Call To the way of your Lord with wisdom and beautiful exhortation, until he reaches the word: “Indeed, Allah is with those who fear Him, and those who are doers of good.”"
36584,"(36584) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: Harim said: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of a time. The young of them will rebel in it, and the great of them will hope in it, and their ages will draw near in it."
36585,"(36585) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Asbagh al-Warraq, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, that Umar sent Haram bin Hayyan to The horse became angry with a man, so he commanded it, and its neck was surprised. Then he turned to his companions and said: No, may God reward you well. You advised me when I said: And do not restrain me from my anger, and by God, I have no right for you. Then he wrote to Omar: O Amir. Believers, I cannot bear to herd, so send me your work."
36586,"(36586) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Haram bin Hayyan used to say: I have not seen anything like fire. Its fugitive slept, and its seeker did not sleep like heaven."
36587,"(36587) Abu Asama told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told me, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: He was old. Ibn Hayyan was working on some of the offices of Ahwaz, and one of his friends asked permission to go to his family, but he refused to give him permission. He said: Then Haram bin Hayyan stood up to deliver the Friday sermon. When the man said this to his nose, he held it to his nose and pointed. Haram in his hand: Go, so the man went until he came to his family and fulfilled his needs, then he came back, and Haram said to him: Where? I was, so he said: Did you not see when I got up and touched my nose and motioned to me with your hand to go? So Hürrem said: Leave the bad men behind. For the bad time."
36588,"(36588) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ghalib al-Qattan told me, on the authority of Bakr, he said: If On the Day of Resurrection, God will not leave any need for a believer without fulfilling it, and He will not ask of him except what agrees with His satisfaction."
36589,"(36589) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Saeed Al-Jariri narrated to us, he said: Muwarriq Al-Ajli passed by. At the meeting of the neighborhood, he greeted them, and they returned his greetings to him and asked him, and a man from the neighborhood said: I think you are doing well. He said: We are welcome. The tenth part of it is suitable."
36590,"(36590) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Bakr, who said: A man is not pious until he is pious of anger. Piousness of greed."
36591,"(36591) Yahya bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid {so for their souls they will strive}. He said: In The grave"
36592,"(36592) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid: {And for whoever fears the position of his Lord there will be two gardens} He said: Whoever fears God His standing over sin in this world."
36593,"(36593) Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Whenever I saw a Mujahid, I thought that he was Kharbandiah, had gone astray. He is a donkey, so he is concerned."
36594,"(36594) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbă bin Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: What Not one day has he departed from this world except that he said: Praise be to God who has taken me out of this world so that I will never return to it."
36595,"(36595) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid: {We will bring the earth to reduce it from its edges} He said: Death"
36596,"(36596) Abu Usama told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: There were in Medina the people of a household who had a need. They had a sheep’s head, so they noticed something and said: If only we had sent this head to someone who is more in need of it than us. He said: So they sent for him, and he did not stop wandering around Medina until he returned to his companions from whom he had left."
36597,"(36597) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The scholars have gone, and only the learned remain. The diligent person among you today is just like the player among those who were before you."
36598,"(36598) Abdullah bin Numir told us, he said: Malik bin Mughul told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: If he meets The man, the man, made you laugh in your face, and sins fell away from them, just as the wind scatters dried leaves from a tree. He said: Then a man said: This is easy work. He said: He said: I have not heard the words of God Almighty: {If you were to spend all that is on the earth, you would not have reunited their hearts}"
36599,"(36599) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The people of Kufa impressed me with four things: Talha, Zubaid, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, and Yahya bin Abbad."
36600,"(36600) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a Muslim is not afflicted by his brother, he His modesty prevents him from sin."
36601,"(36401) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The jurist is the one who fears God."
36602,"(36602) Affan narrated to us, saying: Abdul-Wahid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding the Almighty’s saying: {Repent to Allah with complete repentance. Sincere} He said: It means to repent and then not do it again."
36603,"(36403) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, in the Almighty’s saying: {And to Him submits whoever is in the heavens and the earth. Willingly or unwillingly} He said: The obedient and faithful one."
36604,"(36404) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {They were not hungry during the night}. He said: They did not sleep all night."
36605,"(36605) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, Their hearts, their eyes, and their souls are over their wives. They are in tents of pearls, and they do not want anyone but them."
36606,"(36606) Fudayl bin Ayyad told us, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Mujahid {and a beautiful eye} who said: They are dazzling to see."
36607,"(36407) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid: {And ask God of His bounty} He said: It is not as small as the world."
36608,"(36408) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid {And seek Him with complete devotion} He said: Be sincerely sincere to Him."
36609,"(36609) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no dead person who dies without the earth weeping for him. Forty in the morning."
36610,"(36610) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid: {And for whoever fears the position of his Lord there will be two gardens} He said: He is the man He remembers God when committing sins, and He will withhold them from them."
36611,"(36611) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, in his saying: {He will circumambulate over them a vessel of silver. And the cups were flasks, flasks of silver, which they measured with a precise estimate. He said: The vessels: the cups, and the cups: the constellations. And in recognition: It is not full of overflowing, nor lacking in destiny."
36612,"(36612) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, in the Almighty’s saying: {For those who do evil With glory, then they repent from near. He said: The whole world is near, all of it is glory."
36613,"(36413) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ikrimah {their marks are in their faces} who said: Staying awake"
36614,"(36614) Hakam al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Ikrimah: {And remember your Lord when you forget} He said: Then You disobeyed, and some of them said: If you became angry."
36615,"(36415) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah {And the hearts reached Throats} He said: If the hearts moved, or were to move away, his soul would go out, but it is only fear."
36616,"(36616) Yahya bin Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shu’ba informed us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, “As the disbelievers despaired.” From the dwellers of the graves} He said: When the unbelievers enter the graves and see what God has prepared for them of disgrace, they despair of God’s mercy."
36617,"(36617) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Amr Baya’ al-Mala’, on the authority of Ikrimah, “Indeed, we have ungulates.” He said: fetters."
36618,"(36618) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: We entered upon Muhammad bin Suqi, and he said: I will narrate to you a hadith that may It will benefit you, for it has benefited me. He said: Ata’ bin Abi Rabah said to us: O son of my brother, those who were before you were He hates frivolous speech except for the Book of God Almighty that you read it, or enjoining what is right, or forbidding what is wrong, and You express your need in your livelihood which is necessary for you. Do you deny that {over you are guardians, honorable and recorded} and that {He is restrained on the right and on the left. He does not utter a word except with Him is a watcher, ever present.} Would not one of you be ashamed if he were spread? His page that filled the beginning of his day, and most of what was in it was not related to matters of his religion or the world."
36619,"(36419) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Al-Rudaini, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, he said: The wind did not blow. Except with punishment and mercy."
36620,"(36420) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Shabib, on the authority of Muqatil bin Hayyan {or did he take a covenant with the Most Gracious?} He said: the covenant. Prayer"
36621,"(36621) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, he said: They were good people when they met each other. They entrust one another with three things, and if they are absent, they write to one another with three things: Whoever does good deeds for the hereafter, God will suffice him. This world, and whoever improves what is between him and God, Allah will suffice him with the people, and whoever improves his secrets, Allah will improve his openness."
36622,"(36422) Saeed bin Shurahbil narrated to us, on the authority of Khallad bin Sulaiman Al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Khalid bin Abi Imran say: Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr would not break his fast during the month for more than three days. Khaled said: He stayed for forty years and did not stop. His garment, from his back."
36623,"(36423) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun and Hisham told us all, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: We were with Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhayfah in his apartment, when a man came to him and sat with him on his bed, and he asked him something. I did not understand him, so Abu Ubaidah said to him: I ask you to put your finger in this fire, and be between There was fire in their hands, and the man said: Glory be to God, and Abu Ubaidah said to him: You are being miserly to me with one of your fingers. The fire of this world and you ask me to put my whole body in the fire of hell. He said: So we thought that he called him to judgment."
36624,"(36424) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that Ubaid Allah bin Adiy bin Al-Khayyar said: Oh God, protect us and those who believe among us."
36625,"(36425) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith say: Al-Zabaniyya. Their heads are in the heavens and their feet are on the earth."
36626,"(36426) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas? It is written from his words good and evil."
36627,"(36427) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He will write down what he has and his wealth."
36628,"(36428) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Al-Hassan, “They were for a little while during the night. They will be hungry. He said: Say, “When a night has come upon them, they will be hungry.”"
36629,"(36629) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: While a man was riding on a donkey When he stumbled upon it, he said: I am miserable. Then the one with the right hand said: What is your good deed, so write it down. And the one with the left hand said: What is wrong with you? If the companion of the right has left, write it down. The companion of the left is called. If the companion of the right has left, write it down."
36630,"(36430) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: Whoever is hostile to the friends of God has lost God has given permission to wage war, and whoever’s intercession prevents him from going beyond one of God’s limits has deviated from God in His command, and whoever helps his opponents against him has not He who has knowledge of it will be in the wrath of God until it is removed, and whoever stands by believing in something of which he has no knowledge, God will stand him in reproach. What is wrong until a way out comes from it, and whoever disputes with a weak person until his right is established, God will make his feet firm on the Day The feet slipped, and God said: I do not hesitate about anything I want. My hesitation about taking the soul of My faithful servant hates death. And I hate to be with him, but he has no choice but to do so. (Bukhari 6502)"
36631,"(36431) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Zaytoun, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, that he said: Speech in the mosque is idle talk, except for one who is praying, or remembering his Lord, or asking for good, or giving it."
36632,"(36432) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Abi Salamah, who said: It has reached me that Ibn Muhayriz entered upon a man from So he bought something from him, and a man said to the butcher, do you know who this is? Ibn Muhayriz. So he got up and said: It’s just We came to buy with our money, not with our debt."
36633,"(36433) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, who said: I heard Ibn Muhayriz while we were with him. With sand, and he says: It overtook the people, and when among them a dead Muslim died, they said: Praise be to God who caused so-and-so to die. upon Islam, then that stopped, and no one today says that."
36634,"(36434) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Mujja’ bin Yahya, who said: Muja’ bin Jariyah used to say: Oh God, I I ask you for a happy death."
36635,"(36435) Yahya bin Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of his father, regarding his saying: (Khafidiya) is one who lowered On that day it will never rise, and whoever rises on that day will never fall."
36636,"(36436) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Aws, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, he said: The doers of good are those who are not unjust, and if they are wronged they are not victorious."
36637,"(36437) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Al-Shakhir, he said: So-and-so said: You walk on Your graves. I said: Yes. He said: How do you get rain?"
36638,"(36438) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {Then the fish ate it up.} He said: When it ate it up, it took it until it placed it on the seventh earth, then it heard the earth singing, so it rejoiced. On the glorification, and he said: {There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, you have been of the wrongdoers} He said: So he took him out until he threw him on the ground without There is no hair or fingernails like a child who was killed, so God caused trees to grow on him to shade him, and beneath them the insects of the earth would eat. While he was sleeping under it, some dried leaves fell on him, so he complained about that to his Lord, and it was said to him: Do you grieve over a tree, and do not grieve over a hundred thousand, or more will they torment you?"
36639,"(36439) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Abu Hilal Muhammad ibn Sulaym al-Rasibi informed us, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: Abu Al-Sabai: I asked for money from his wealth, but it provided me with only one day’s sustenance, then I knew that it had been better for me: God knows what Whoever is a servant who has been given daily sustenance and does not think that it has been better for him, unless he is helpless, or is of foolish mind."
36640,"(36440) Affan narrated to us, he said: Bukair bin Abi Al-Sumait narrated to us, he said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mutrif, He used to say: You will meet between two men, one of whom fasts and prays more, and the other is more generous to God. Far away, they said: How can that be, O Abu Jazir? He said: He will be the more pious of the two of them regarding his mahrams."
36641,"(36441) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, regarding his saying: {And give good news to those who are hidden.} He said: the humble."
36642,"(36442) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak {And they were humble to Us} He said: Submissiveness is to God."
36643,"(36443) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak {It will melt with it what is in their bellies and skins} He said: He is melted by it."
36644,"(36444) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Al-Dahhak {And when they pass by idle talk, they pass by it with honor} He said: Idle talk was not part of their condition, nor was it their concern."
36645,"(36445) Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Had it not been for the recitation of the Qur’an, it would have pleased me. That I am sick."
36646,"(36446) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak {in a trustworthy position}. He said: They are safe from dying. And protect the old age, lest they grow old and not go hungry or become naked."
36647,"(36447) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak {Indeed, you are toiling to your Lord, toiling.} He said: A worker to your Lord. work"
36648,"(36448) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bastam, on the authority of Al-Dahhak (for them is good news in the life of this world) he said: He knows where he was before death."
36649,"(36449) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abu Sinan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim saying in his statement: {So race ahead of good deeds; to Allah is your return.} He said: The mother of Muhammad, the righteous and the ungodly."
36650,"(36450) Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: I heard Aba al-Fayd saying on the authority of al-Dahhak, he said: {Allah only accepts from the righteous} He said: those who fear polytheism."
36651,"(36451) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Dawud bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Safiyya, he said: Tell me Ashras bin Hassan Al-Kufi said: I heard Wahhab bin Munabbih say: Aaron was the one who consecrated the churches."
36652,"(36452) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, that he said: What Do you know what is sufficient for the faith of a servant who does not abandon anything that God hates?"
36653,"(36453) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Muslim bin Yasar, he said: If one of them was acquitted, it would be said To him: to him there is purity."
36654,"(36454) Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Thabit told us, that Abu Bakr used to imitate this verse:
You will continue to mourn a beloved until you are no more. The young man may hope for a hope that he will die without him."
36655,"(36455) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Malik bin Dinar, he said: I asked Jabir bin Zaid, I said: God Almighty says: {And had We not made you firm, you would have almost abandoned them a little. Then We would have made you taste the weakness of life and the weakness of life. Death and then you will not find you any helper over Us} What is the weakness of life and the weakness of death? Jabir said: Double the torment of this world and double the torment of the Hereafter, then you will not find any helper against us."
36656,"(36456) Affan told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: I heard Thabit, he said: We were with Jabir bin Zaid. He saw a camel and said: If I had told you: I do not worship this camel, I would not have believed that I would worship it."
36657,"(36457) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: How are people like one another? Somehow, how similar the night was to yesterday."
36658,"(36458) Affan narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: Most of the scents of Paradise Henna"
36659,"(36459) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Rabi’ narrated to us. Ibn Khuthaym said: Abu Ubaidah Ibn Abdullah told us, he said: When Ar-Rabi’ Ibn Khuthaym entered upon Abdullah, he did not On that day there will be permission until each one of them has finished with its companion. He said: And Abdullah said to him, O father Yazid, if the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw you, he would love you, and I did not see you except that I mentioned those who were hidden. (Ahmad 408, Abu Naim 106)"
36660,"(36460) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Talha, he said: It was said: Who is the one who gets fat? In fertility and barrenness, and who is the one who laughs in fertility and barrenness, and who is sweeter than honey and never ceases, He said: As for the one who thrives in fertility and barrenness, he is the believer who, if given, is grateful, and if he is tested is patient. He is mocking about fertility and barrenness. For the disbeliever, or the ungodly one, if he is given something, he is not grateful, and if he is tested, he is not patient, and as for the one who It is sweeter than honey, and it will not be cut off, for it is the bond of God that He has joined between the hearts of the believers."
36661,"(36461) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Thamer, and he was a devout man who would go to The mosque, and he saw in a dream as if the people had been brought before God, and a woman was brought to her wearing thin clothes, and a wind came. Then she revealed her clothes, and God turned away from her and said: Take her to the Fire, for she was one of the adornments to the point of The matter came to me, and he said: Call him, for he was fulfilling the right of the people."
36662,"(36462) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Thamer who claimed that a woman, she said: By God, no May God never punish me. I have not stolen, nor committed adultery, nor killed my children, nor come up with a slander that you will invent. Their hands and feet. She saw in a dream that she was told: Arise to your seat in the Fire, O you who neglect The much is the greater of the little, and he ate the meat of a strange neighbor in the unseen. She said: O Lord, but I repent, but I repent."
36663,"(36463) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, that Abu Thamer saw what a sleeper sees: Woe. For fat women from a period in the bones on the Day of Resurrection."
36664,"(36464) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, that Abu Thamir was a man of worship, so he slept one night. One night before he prayed the evening prayer, two angels or two men came to him in his dream, and one of them sat at his head and the other At his feet, and he said: The one at his head to the one at his feet: Prayer before sleep pleases the Most Gracious and displeases Him. Satan, and the one at his feet said to the one at his head: Sleeping before prayer pleases Satan and displeases the Most Gracious."
36665,"(36665) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit Al-Bunani narrated to us, on the authority of Salah bin Ashaim, that He said: By God, I do not know which day I am most happy about: the day on which I rise early to remember God, or the day I went out. It was for some of my needs, so he offered me the remembrance of God."
36666,"(36466) Affan narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: It was Abu Rifa’ Al-Adawiyy says: Surah Al-Baqarah has not been withheld from me since the Messenger of God taught it to me. I have taken with it what I have taken from the Qur’an, and what My back hurts from standing up all night."
36667,"(۳۶۶۶۷) حَدَّثَنَا عَفَّانُ ، قَالَ : حدَّثَنَا سُلَیْمَانُ عَنْ حُمَیْدُ بْنُ ہِلاَلٍ ، قَالَ : قَالَ صِلَۃٌ رَأَیْتُ أَبَا رِفَاعَۃَ بَعْدَ مَا He was afflicted while sleeping on a fast camel while I was on a heavy camel, and I found its tracks. He said: So he limps it to me. So I say, “Now I will make him hear the voice and he will make it go away, and I will follow in her footsteps.” So your visions were interpreted to be that I would follow the path of Abu Rifa’ah, so I I will work harder after that."
36668,"(36668) Affan narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Humaid bin Hilal narrated to us, he said: Abu Rifaa’i, or a man from among them who, while traveling, brings hot water to his companions and goes to the cold one and performs ablution with it, then he says: Feel. From this, I will feel from this."
36669,"(36669) Affan told us, he said: Sulayman told us, he said: Thabit said, Mutarrif said: If anyone from this nation has been tested. The heart was terrified because of the one who tests the heart."
36670,"(36470) Affan told us, he said: Sulayman told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: Mutarrif said: A man saw me and I was terrified, so he said: Who? He was pleased to look at two men from the people of Paradise, so let him look at these two, and he heard them terrified, so I saw The hate in his face, then he said: Oh God, you know us and we do not know them."
36671,"(36471) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abi Raji, who said: This place was among the Ibn Abbas: The duct of tears is like a curtain worn out from tears."
36672,"(36672) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shimr ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Sa’d ibn Al-Akhram, He said: When Abdullah went out to the market and passed by the blacksmiths and saw them not coming out of the fire, it made his eyes water."
36673,"(36673) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: When the people of Yemen came in the time of Abu Bakr When they heard the Qur’an, they began to cry, so Abu Bakr said: This is how we were, then the hearts became hardened."
36674,"(36474) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Nadhru, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, the client of Abu Usayd, who said: When Omar prayed, he would take the people out of the mosque and go to us. When he saw his companions, he threw down his pearls and sat down, and said: Pray. So they prayed. He said: So he started calling and calling until the call came to an end, so I called while I was a slave, and I saw him praying and crying, crying for no reason. The bereaved woman cried, so I said to myself: This is what you say is harsh."
36675,"(36475) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Dawud, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: On you. By the Way and the Sunnah, for there is no servant who follows the Way and the Sunnah who mentions the Most Gracious and whose eyes overflow from the fear of God. So the Fire will never touch him, and there is not a servant who follows the path and Sunnah of God and makes his skin tremble out of fear of God but he will be like him. Like a tree whose leaves wither, so it is, when a wind strikes it, and its leaves are blown away, and its sins are erased as I will shed its leaves from this tree, and being frugal according to a Sunnah and a path is better than striving in a way other than a Sunnah and a path. So consider your deeds. If they are economical and diligent, they should be on the method of the prophets and their Sunnah. (Abu Naim 252)"
36676,"(36476) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: I heard Omar sobbing while I was at the end of the class, and he was reciting Surah Yusuf: {I only complain of my grief and my grief to God}"
36677,"(36477) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah. That Ibn Umar recited: {And whether you reveal what is within yourselves, or conceal it, Allah will call to account you for it}, and it brought tears to his eyes, so he reached What Ibn Abbas did, and he said: May God have mercy on Abu Abdul Rahman, he did just as the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. And he greeted when it was revealed, and the verses after it abrogated it. {To her is what she has earned, and upon her is what she has earned}"
36678,"(36478) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Ibn Awn, on the authority of Arfaja al-Salami, who said: Abu Bakr said: Cry even if you do not They cried and they cried."
36679,"(36679) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Malika informed me, he said: Alqamiya informed me Ibn Waqqas said: Omar used to recite Surah Yusuf in the last evening prayer while I was at the back of the rows until he was mentioned. Youssef heard his sobbing."
36680,"(36480) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Shaqiq ibn Salamah, who said: We entered upon Khabbab to return to him. He said, “In this coffin, there are eighty thousand whom you did not bind with a thread, nor did you protect them from a liquid.” They said, “Why are you weeping?” He went on. My companions, the world did not diminish them in the slightest, and we remained until we found no place for it except dust."
36681,"(36481) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of his brother Abdullah bin Ubaidah, he said: She saw Safiya, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A people recited “Prostration” and prostrated, so she called to them: “This is the prostration and the supplications, so where is it?” Crying"
36682,"(36482) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud Al-Laythi, he said: Al-Bakhtari bin Zayd bin Kharijiya narrated to us, that a man from Al-Abbad passed by an open blacksmith's furrow, so he stood up to look at it and stayed as long as God wished for him to stay, then he gasped. Then he died."
36683,"(36483) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: I saw Abdullah Ibn Amr was crying, and I looked at him and he said: I am amazed that they cried out of fear of God. If they did not cry, then they would cry until One of you says: Oh, oh, this moon is crying out of fear of God Almighty."
36684,"(36484) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Alqamiya bin Marthad narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, he said: If the crying of the people of the earth were to be compared to the crying of David, it would not be equal to it. If the crying of David and the crying of the people of the earth were to be compared to the crying of Adam at He was brought down to the earth without equal."
36685,"(36485) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Abu Salih used to lead us in prayer, but he did not allow the Qur’an to be recited from Raqqa"
36686,"(36486) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, who said: So-and-so narrated to me: He said: I came. Rabia and he was crying over the prayer."
36687,"(36487) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rabah, on the authority of Safwan ibn Mahrez, that if He recited this verse and wept until he saw that his false stories would be crushed: {And those who have wronged will know what a reversal it is. They turn."
36688,"(36488) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of his mother, and she used to crush the kohl. According to Abdullah bin Amr, he used to put out the lamp and cry until his eyes watered."
36689,"(36489) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Recite the Qur’an to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, recite it to you and to you it was revealed. He said: I long to hear it from someone else. He said: So the women recited until when they reached the news: {How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness? And We brought you as a witness against these.} I raised my head, or a man nudged me beside me, and I saw his tears flowing."
36690,"(36690) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abdullah He raised it in a similar way."
36691,"(36691) A lecturer narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, who said: I met sixty of Abdullah’s companions. In this mosque of ours, the youngest of them was Al-Harith bin Suwayd, and I heard him reciting: {When it is shaken} until it reaches {then who can make a weight A seed of goodness that he will see} He said: Then he cried, then he said: This is a severe experience."
36692,"(36692) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Salam bin Miskin told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, he said: A man passed by The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man recite a verse and make you cry and repeat it. He said: Did you not listen to me? God Almighty says: {And recite the Qur’an in a recitation} He said: This recitation."
36693,"(36693) Shadhan narrated to us, saying: Mahdi bin Maimun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq. Al-Uqaili said: I heard Ka’b say: Because I cry out of fear of God Almighty until my tears run down my cheeks, I love I have to give my weight in gold in charity, and by the one in whose hand is the soul of a heel, not a single Muslim servant will cry out of fear of God. Until a drop of his tears drops to the earth, and the fire will never touch it, until the drop of the sky that fell returns to the earth from where it came, and it will not He will never come back."
36694,"(36694) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Mahdi bin Maymun narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad saying: The man was one of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, three days will come to him and he will not find anything to eat, then he will find the skin. So he roasted it and made use of it, and if he did not find anything, he went to a stone and tightened his stomach with it."
36695,"(36695) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abu al-Ward bin Thumama, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, He said: There were among the Children of Israel men of young teeth, and they were overwhelmed. They had read the Scripture and had knowledge, and indeed they sought By granting them honor and wealth, and they invented heresies by which they took honor and wealth in this world, they went astray and misled many."
36696,"(36696) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Khaled bin Salih, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, he said:"
36697,"(36697) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair told me, he said: It was for the Prophet Job, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Two brothers came together and were not able to get close to him because of his scent. So one of them said to the other: If only God were He knew that this was a good thing for Ayoub, so Ayoub was greatly alarmed by what they said, as he had never been alarmed by anything before, so he said: Job: Oh God, if You know that I have never spent a night full and I know a hungry place, then believe me. So believe me, and they are both. Simon then said: Oh God, if you know that I have never worn a shirt and I know a naked place, then believe me. So he was believed, and they... Simon, then he fell down prostrating, then said: Oh God, I will not raise my head until you uncover it. He said: He did not raise his head until it uncovered it. May God protect him"
36698,"(36698) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: It was narrated that Jesus, the son of Mary, peace be upon them both. He used to say: When one of you gives charity, let him give with his right hand and let him give with his left hand, and when it is a day for one of you to fast Let him use his hands and wipe his lips of grease so that the observer looks at him and does not see that he is fasting, and if he prays in In his house, let him take cover over himself, for he divides the couple just as he divides sustenance."
36699,"(36699) Saeed bin Abdullah bin Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir bin Dhu’luq, on the authority of Bakr bin Ma’iz, He said: Whenever Abdullah bin Masoud saw Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym coming, he would say: {Give good tidings to those who are hidden.} But by God, if a messenger saw you May God bless him and grant him peace, I love you."
36700,"(36700) Sa’id bin Abdullah bin Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr bin Ma’iz, who said: A girl came. Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, and he had some of his friends with him, so she said: Father, I will go play. He said: No, so his friends said to him: O Abu Yazid, leave her. He said: It is not found in my manuscript that I said to her: Take the slave, but go. So say good and do good."
36701,"(36701) Sa’id bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Al-Rabi’ used to say: O Bakr bin Ma’iz. O virgin, beware of your tongue except what is yours, and do not blame the people. Indeed, I have accused the people of my religion. Obey God in what you know, and do not He was preferred over you, so leave it all to his world, because we are more afraid of intentionality than I am of you making mistakes. How good you are today. With its goodness, but it is better than the last evil of it. You have not understood everything that God revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And you do not know what they are about everything you read. The secrets that they hide from people, and they are to Him are valleys. Seek their medicine. Then He says For himself: And what is the cure for her to repent to God and then not come back?"
36702,"(36702) Saeed bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Nasir bin Dhuluq, on the authority of Bakr, who said: When Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthim finished To the mosque of his people, they said: To him: O Rabi’, if you sit, tell us today. He said: So he sat, then a stone came and struck him, and he said: {So whoever has come to him an exhortation from his Lord and he refrains from it, he will have what was previously given}"
36703,"(36703) Saeed bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim used to say: There is no good in Speech except in nine things: God’s praise, God’s glorification, God’s greatness, God’s glory, God’s praise, God’s request for good, and God’s refuge from evil. I command you to do what is right and forbid what is wrong and to recite the Qur’an."
36704,"(36704) Saeed bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: It was spring when it was said to him: How is this morning? O Abu Yazid, he says: We have become weak and sinful, devouring our livelihood and waiting for our time."
36705,"(36705) Sa’id bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Ibn al-Kawa’i said to Rabi’ bin Khathim: What We see you disparaging someone, but do not blame him. He said: Woe to you, O son of Al-Kawa’i. I am not pleased with myself so I can relieve myself of my blame. Slandering people. Indeed, people feared God for the sins of His servants and believed in their sins."
36706,"(36706) Saeed bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Al-Rabi’ used to say: The people are two men: a believer and an ignorant person. As for the believer; Do not harm him. As for the ignorant person, Don't ignore him."
36707,"(36707) Saeed bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: When Rabi’ was told, “Don’t you seek treatment?” he said: She wanted that, then she mentioned Ad, Thamud, and the Companions of the Land, and many centuries between that, so I knew that it had been among them. Pains, and they had doctors, so the healer and the healed died."
36708,"(36708) Sa’id bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Al-Rabi’ used to say in the morning: Do good. And speak good and always do what is righteous, and if you do evil, repent, and when you do good, add more. Whatever you know, maintain it, and whatever you doubt. So eat it to God. The believer, so do not harm him. And the ignorant, do not ignore him. And do not let a long period of time pass, lest your hearts harden. And do not be like those who said: We hear them, but they do not listen."
36709,"(36709) Saeed bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr, who said: Al-Rabi’ used to say: Mention this frequently. A death the likes of which you have never tasted before."
36710,"(36710) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: I realized that he was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, more than those who came before me. I have never seen a people more lenient in conduct, nor less strict than them."
36711,"(36711) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Ali, who said: When the elephants tend And the souls have come to rest, so seek your needs from God, for He is the One who seeks those who will come to Him. And He recited: {For indeed, He is Forgiving of those who will return}"
36712,"(36712) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Mughul, on the authority of Ukil, who said: It was between a man from the neighborhood and a slave. Al-Rahman bin Yazid said something, and Alqamah said to him: Would you curse me if I cursed you? He said: No. He said: He is better than you, and he is more jihad than you."
36713,"(36713) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Bahdaliya, he said: Abu Wael had a private servant. He is in it and his animal, so if he wants to invade, he breaks the line, and when he returns, he builds it."
36714,"(36714) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza’: {Indeed, Hell It was a lookout. He said: it became."
36715,"(36715) Sa’id bin Khathim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, who said: We entered upon Suwayd, meaning Ibn He was terrified and complaining about you, so we said to him: How do you find yourself? He said: I am in recovery from my Lord."
36716,"(36716) A lecturer told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: There is no A small tree, nor a large one, nor one planted with a fresh needle, nor a dry one, except an angel entrusted with it. God will bring it to you. By working with it every day with its moisture when it is wet, and with its moisture when it is dry."
36717,"(36717) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, who said: If the man were from the neighborhood, he would come Then Al-Harith bin Suwayd cursed, but he remained silent. When he remained silent, he stood up, shook off his cloak, and entered."
36718,"(36718) Al-Ahwas bin Jawab narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar Al-Dhani, on the authority of Wahhab bin Alarming, he said: God revealed to some of his friends: Indeed, I have never permitted My pleasure to the people of a household, nor to the people of a house, nor To the people of a town, I will never turn away from them My pleasure until they turn from My pleasure to My displeasure, and indeed, I have not permitted My displeasure. To any family at all, nor to the family of a house at all, nor to the family of a town at all. So I will turn away from them My wrath until they turn away from My wrath. To Ridvaniyah."
36719,"(36719) Muhammad b? Ibn Abi Layla said: What is the duty of any of you if he does not say to his companion: Listen, may God have mercy on you, then he dictates? May good be upon them."
36720,"(36720) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whenever he recited: {Your deity is multiplication} He said regarding wealth and children, “until you visit the graves. No, you will know.” He said: promise after promise, knowledge of certainty."
36721,"(36721) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When he recites this verse {Indeed, Allah He bought from the believers their souls and their wealth. He said: souls He created and wealth He provided for, so they kill them. And they kill {a promise made true in the Torah and the Gospel}."
36722,"(36722) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, who said: {Ya O man, what has deceived you about your Lord, the Most Generous? He said: Ignorance."
36723,"(36723) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, who said: He was Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman. Ibn Yazid took his servant to the market and recited verse after verse to her from the Qur’an, teaching her. He rises from the night until his end and finds it there."
36724,"(36724) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who used to say: Forbearance, modesty, and conscience are the signs of the tongue, not the conscience of the heart, and jurisprudence is part of faith, and they are of what takes away from the world and increases it. In the Hereafter, and nothing increases in the Hereafter more than what decreases in this world, except that indecency, obscenity, and statements are part of hypocrisy. And they are among those that increase in this world and detract from the Hereafter, and they are among those that increase in the Hereafter more than what they increase in this world."
36725,"(36725) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Masruq, on the authority of Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khuthaym {And behold, the tax collector It was disrupted. He said: Her family abandoned her, so she did not milk and did not insist."
36726,"(36726) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, on the authority of Tarif, who said: I saw Rabi’ bin Khuthaym. He carries a piece of clothing to his aunt's house."
36727,"(36727) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, he said: : Unless the face of God is desired, it vanishes."
36728,"(36728) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abu Kuddin narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr said, when Ibn Omar was injured, he said: I did not leave anything of this world behind me that I would regret except thirst. Hajj and other than walking to prayer."
36729,"(36729) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Adam ibn Ali, he said: I heard Bilal’s brother, the muezzin. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: People are in three: the peaceful person, the spoiler, and the one who withdraws. He said: The peaceful person who is silent, and the spoiler. He who enjoins good and forbids evil, that is an increase from God, and the one who denounces: the one who speaks treacherously. And the one who helps against injustice."
36730,"(36730) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: Ibrahim informed me on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Abi Rashid, he said: It was my father. He was impressed by Khalaf bin Hawshab. He said: I said to him: Father, you admire this man. He said: My son, he was brought up with His way was beautiful, and it did not fail on her. He said: And Abu Marzuq used to call me: Then Rabi’ said to him: Turn it around. He said: Then Khalaf said: So call me, he said: You are Abu Abd al-Rahman."
36731,"(36731) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He said Islam, and what is Islam? He said: Islam is the secret. And revelation in it is equal to your heart being submitted to God, and every Muslim and every covenant being submitted to you."
36732,"(36732) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, he said: I have heard that work on the Day of Decree is like work on His night"
36733,"(36733) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Khaythami, he said: Issa ibn Maryam: Do not hide today’s provision for tomorrow, for He who brought it to you today will bring it to you tomorrow. If you say: How will it be? So look at the birds. They neither plow nor sow. They go in the morning and go to God’s provision. If you say: What is enough for the birds? So look at the donkeys of the wild beast and the oxen of the wild beast. They go in the morning with God’s provision and go away full."
36734,"(36734) Al-Muharabi narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul, he said: Abu Yafur narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: The holder of the Qur’an should be known by its night when the people are sleeping, and by its day when the people are asleep. They break their fast, and with his sadness when people rejoice, and with his crying when people laugh, and with his silence when people are confused, And with humility when people are conceiting, and the bearer of the Qur’an should be weeping, sad, forbearing, wise, and calm. It is not appropriate for the person carrying the Qur’an to be, as Abu Bakr mentioned, a word, neither loud, nor shouting, nor sharpening."
36735,"(36735) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Abu Sinan told us, he said: Amr bin Murah told us, he said: Abu Wael came. Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym returned and said: I did not come to you unless I heard the voice of the mourner. Al-Rabi’ said: I am only for a month. Therein are written for me fifty and a hundred prayers."
36736,"(36736) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja`far Al-Khattimi narrated to us, that his grandfather Umair bin Habib used to get up at night and say, “Leave, O people. You have raced to the water, the deluge, the deluge.” He who races to the water becomes thirsty, and he who races to the sun becomes thirsty."
36737,"(36737) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Al-Khattimi, that Umair bin Habib had a master who taught him the structure of the Qur’an and the Book, so he made their memories of women and the world, he said: Then he said to him: O Ziyad, Satan has cast a shadow over the people of Quba, destroy it."
36738,"(36738) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muslim bin Yassar said: If you narrate a hadith on the authority of God, then withhold it. So know what came before it, and what comes after it."
36739,"(36739) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Asim, who said: His people were the words of Al-Hasan, Glory be to God. The Great, Glory be to God and praise be to Him."
36740,"(36740) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir said: Whoever purifies, it will be pure for him, and whoever mixes, it will be mixed for him."
36741,"(36741) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: A man gave a will to his son, and he said: O my son, show your despair with what is in people’s hands, for it is wealth, and beware of asking for what you need, for it is present poverty. And beware of what is excused from him in speech, and when you pray, pray a farewell prayer, you will not see that you will return, even if you are able to Today is better than yesterday, and tomorrow is better than today, so do it."
36742,"(36742) Shazan narrated to us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabab, he said: Mujahid said to me: No I inform you of the Most Merciful, the Protector. I said: Yes. He said: He is the one who remembers his sin when it is free and seeks forgiveness from God."
36743,"(36743) Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: I heard Zuhayr Abu Khaythama, saying: Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani narrated to us, saying: It was Al-Hassan, which means the best-looking one, is likened to the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
36744,"(36744) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid and Yunus bin Ubaid, that they said: They We have seen the jurists, but we have not seen from them anyone who is more complete than the good."
36745,"(36745) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, saying: Khalid bin Rabah narrated to us, that Anas bin Malik was asked about He asked him, and he said: You should ask us about our Master Al-Hasan, so ask him. They said: We ask you, O Abu Hamza, and you say: Ask our Master Al-Hasan. He said: We heard, and he heard, but we forgot and memorized."
36746,"(36746) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Musa Al-Qaari, on the authority of Talha bin Abdullah, who said: It was Zazan teaches without anything."
36747,"(36747) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Faraj bin Fadalah narrated to us, on the authority of Asad bin Wada’i, he said: Shaddad bin When Aws goes to bed as if he were a grain of wheat on a frying pan, then he says: Oh God, the fire has prevented me from sleeping: Then He stands up for prayer."
36748,"(36748) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amara ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’i, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab, he said The most generous of people is he who is generous to someone who does not hope for his reward, and the most forgiving of people is he who pardons after destiny, and the most stingy of people is he who is stingy. With peace, and the most incapable of people is the one who is unable to supplicate to God."
36749,"(36749) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Salam ibn Miskin informed us: He said: I heard Al-Hasan say: If the servant sleeps in His prostration, by the name of God, by the angels, says: Look at My servant, he is worshiping Me, and his soul is with You."
36750,"(36750) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Al-Sumait narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: For the virtue of knowledge, I love To me is the bounty of worship, and the piety of your religion."
36751,"(36751) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of a man from Al-Nakh’, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: The people of The affliction on the Day of Resurrection is that their skins were cut off with scissors."
36752,"(36752) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Othman has been appointed successor, and all they have been faced with is coldness, and nothing I wear them except the tiger. One of them used to say to his friend: My tiger is better than yours."
36753,"(36753) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, he said: Abu Qatada al-Adawi told us: You should take care of this Sheikh, meaning Al-Hasan, for I have never seen anyone with an opinion more similar to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab than him."
36754,"(36754) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, who said: Mutarrif bin Abdullah said: I was not. I do not believe in anyone’s supplication until I hear nothing he says except the good ones."
36755,"(36755) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, that Abu Barza used to pray, and he used to Aid bin Amr Al-Muzani was wearing good clothes. He said: Then a man came to one of them and said: Have you not seen your brother wearing such-and-such? And so and so, and he desires, about your clothing, he said: And who can be like so-and-so, thanks to such-and-such and such-and-such. So-and-so, from the bounty of such-and-such, he said: And the other came and said: Like that."
36756,"(36756) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Asma Bint Zaid, she said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The greatest name of God in these two verses: {And your God is God. One - there is no god but Him, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."
36757,"(36757) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of his father, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man saying: Oh God, I ask you that you are the one God, the eternal, the eternal, who does not give birth and does not give birth. He was born and there was no one equal to Him, so he said: I have asked God by His greatest name, by which when He is called, He answers, and when He is asked With Him He gave you"
36758,"(36758) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khuzaymah, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he heard the Prophet pray May God bless him and grant him peace, a man says: Oh God, I ask you that to you is praise, there is no god but you alone, you have no partner, Al-Mannan, the Splendor of the heavens and the earth, the Possessor of majesty and honor. He said: I have asked God in His greatest name, which when asked, He gives. And when he is called upon with it, he responds."
36759,"(36759) Abu Usama told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, that a caller called During the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: I ask of you in your name, to whom there is no god but You, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Creator of the heavens. And the earth, and when you want something, you just say to it, “Be,” and it is. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: You have struggled, or he almost To call upon God by His greatest name."
36760,"(36760) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Al-Hasan bin Thawban narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Ruqayya, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’ and Ibn Abbas, that they used to say: The greatest name of God is Lord, Lord."
36761,"(36761) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: A man recited Al-Baqarah and the family of Imran, Ka'b said: He recited two surahs containing the name by which when he is called, he responds."
36762,"(36762) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Hayyan Al-Araj, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: The greatest name of God is God."
36763,"(36743) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of someone who heard Al-Sha’bi say: The greatest name of God is God, then he recited, or I recited to him {He is Allah, the Creator, the Creator, the Creator} until the end."
36764,"(36744) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Damra, that Abu Rayhani passed by Hums. Its people were dividing it among themselves, so he heard a noise and said: What is this noise? He said: Homs, divide it with its people among them. Then he said: Oh God, do not make it a trial for them. So he continued repeating it until... He knows when his voice has stopped."
36765,"(36745) Muhammad ibn Mus’ab narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Dhamra, that Abu Rayhani was a marabout. On the island in Miyafareqin, he bought Rastan from a Nabataean, one of its people, for penniless money. When it was settled, and they were in Rastan, he descended from His animal, and he said to his servant: Has Nabati settled his bankruptcy? He said: No. He said: So he took out some of his expenses and paid them to her. His servant, and he said to his companions: Help him well with his animals until he informs his family. They said: O Abu Rayhani, and what Do you want? He said: I want to go to my adversary and fulfill my trust. He said: So he set off until he came to a distance, then he came to his family. After he paid off his fine."
36766,"(36766) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan {No, but they do not fear the Hereafter} He said: This is the one He exposed them."
36767,"(36767) Affan told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Malik bin Dinar told us, he said: I asked Ikrimah, I said: God’s saying {Unless the hypocrites and those in whose hearts is a disease} He said: They are the ones who commit adultery."
36768,"(36768) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the words of God Almighty: {And He knows best of you when He created you from the earth and when you were fetuses in the wombs of your mothers} He said: God knew who Every soul has its own doer, whatever its maker, and what it will do."
36769,"(36769) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, who said: Omar said: Be careful in everything. It is better, except for the matter of the Hereafter."
36770,"(36770) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Qays, who said: If you are in any of The affairs of this world are open, and if you are in any matter of the hereafter, stay as long as you can, and if Satan comes to you while you are praying, He said: You are showing off, so increase and prolong it."
36771,"(36771) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, that he came to him. He asked, and he said: Feed him sugar, and he said: His family: He doesn’t do this with sugar, so he said: But I do with it."
36772,"(36772) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, he said: Maymun bin Abi Jarir narrated to me, he said he informed me, That a man from Banu Ibn Umar put a garment on him. He said: They mentioned a garment. He said: Cut it off. Then he put it on himself. He said: So he disliked that. The boy, and Ibn Umar said to him: Woe to you, see that you are not one of the people who put what God has provided for them in their bellies and on Their backs"
36773,"(36773) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Maimun, that Abu Al-Darda’ said: Woe to the one who does not He knows sometimes, and woe to him who knows, and then does not do it six times."
36774,"(36774) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub bin Rashid narrated to me, on the authority of Wahhab. Ibn Munabbih said: We find in the revealed Book of God: people who follow religions other than worship, who distort this world with the work of the hereafter. They are dressed like sheep’s combs, their hearts are like the hearts of wolves, their tongues are sweeter than honey, and their souls are bitterer than patience. He said: Why are they deceived, and Me, are they deceiving? I have sworn that I will send against them a trial in which the wise will return in confusion."
36775,"(36775) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: A man cannot be pious until he is called to account. His own soul is more severe than holding your partner to account until he knows what he eats, what he eats, what he drinks and what he wears."
36776,"(36776) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Musa Al-Ansari, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of His father, he said: He was the most devout of people in prayer and he would not fast except on the day of Ashura."
36777,"(36777) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Nubait, he said: He said: O my son, get up and pray the magic, if not If you are able, do not skip the two rak’ahs of dawn."
36778,"(36778) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, who said: If Anbas bin Following the Taymiyyah, he followed the ropes, to prostrate until the birds would fall on his back and come down, they do not think so. Except for a wall."
36779,"(36779) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of The Almighty’s saying: {And whoever fears Allah - He will make for him a way out} He said: From every matter that is difficult for people."
36780,"(36780) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr: {He believed and was obedient at times. He prostrated and stood at night, warning of the Hereafter."
36781,"(36781) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, or on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the words of God Almighty: {Let not the greatest terror grieve them} He said: When the Fire closes upon them."
36782,"(36782) Qubaisa told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr al-Zubaidi, on the authority of his father, he said: I did not see He is more likely to sit in mosques than the revolutionaries and Arabs."
36783,"(36783) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, he said: Al-Hasan said: O son of Adam, do you see the speckle in your brother’s eye? And let joy appear in your eyes."
36784,"(36784) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: They used to say: The tongue of the wise is behind his heart, and if he wants to speak, he returns to his heart, and if he wants to say it, and if he wants to say it, he holds it back, and the ignorant person is His heart is on the tip of his tongue and does not return to his heart. What comes on his tongue is spoken by him."
36785,"(36785) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: He who follows himself entirely What he sees in people causes his sadness to cease and his anger not to be alleviated."
36786,"(36786) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, who said: I said to Ibrahim: The raw sabkhahi is not eaten. Meat, and he should not eat such-and-such. He said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, were better than him. They used to eat meat. And ghee and such and such."
36787,"(36787) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: O son of Adam, you will not be held accountable except for what you have committed. Ali baptized."
36788,"(36788) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The people of the village were more generous, may God bless them. To the point that they were seeking cleansing themselves with bread, then God sent upon them hunger to the point that they were eating what They sit with it."
36789,"(36789) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There was a man who often cheated at the gate of Omar. He said: Then Omar said to him: Go and learn the Book of God Almighty. He said: So the man went and Omar missed him, then he met him again, and it was as if he had blamed him. He said: I found in the Book of God what sufficed me on the subject of Omar."
36790,"(36790) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The servant is still fine as long as he is not afflicted. It is a great sin that corrupts his heart and mind. He said: And Al-Hasan said: Faith is faith, for whoever is a believer has God is the intercessor, those who intercede."
36791,"(36791) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever says a good word and does a good deed, then take. On his behalf, and whoever says a good word and does an evil deed, do not punish him."
36792,"(36792) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, he said: Al-Hasan said: Among hypocrisy is disagreement between tongue and heart, and disagreement in secrets. And publicity, and the difference in entry and exit."
36793,"(36793) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, he said: Hafs al-Dab’i told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abi said: Your kingdom: Omar said: O Ka’b, tell us about death. He said: Yes, O Commander of the Faithful, a branch with many thorns was inserted into He entered a man's stomach, and all his thorns were covered with sweat. Then a man pulled him with great force, so he took what he took and left what he left behind."
36794,"(36794) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, saying: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, he said: He informed me that God Blessed and Most High will say on the Day of Resurrection: O children of Adam, indeed We have listened to you since We created you until your day. So, listen to us as we read your deeds to you. Whoever finds good, let him praise God, and whoever finds evil, let him blame no one but me. It is your deeds that We will return to you."
36795,"(36795) Muhammad ibn Mus’ab narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Dhamra, that Abu Rayhani asked permission from the companion of I armed him so that his family would come, so he said: O Abu Rayhani, how much do you want me to postpone it to you? He said: Night, so when he came He came to the mosque and continued praying until morning, then he called for his animal, heading towards his armed ones, and they said: O father Rayhana, did you not ask permission to go to your family? He said: My prince only delayed me for the night, so I will not lie, nor will I differ. He said: So he departed to his armed group and did not come to his family. Abu Rayhani’s house was Bayt al-Maqdis."
36796,"(36796) Muhammad ibn Mus’ab narrated to us, saying: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abdullah ibn Peace be upon him. A boy made a note for him, and he started crying and saying: Take revenge on me, and the boy says: I will not take revenge on you, my master. He said Ibn Salam: Every sin will be forgiven by God except one’s face."
36797,"(36797) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ka`b, he said: There is no servant who does not have wisdom in his head, so if he humbles himself, God will exalt him, and if he is arrogant, God will humble him."
36798,"(36798) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the words of God Almighty: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it} He said: Al-Hasan said: That is for whom God intended to humiliate, so as for he who God intended His honor, for He overlooks His evil deeds among the companions of the jinn. {He promised truthfulness which they used to promise}"
36799,"(36799) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, he said: Abu Salih Al-Uqaili told us, he said: It was Abu Al-Alaa Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir reads from the Qur’an until he faints."
36800,"(36800) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, he said: He was Abu Al-Ala’ He was reading from the Qur’an, and Mutarrif would sometimes say to him: “Your reading of the Qur’an will do us no good for the rest of the day.”"
36801,"(36801) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas: Which work is best? He said: The remembrance of Allah is the greatest. He said: And whoever is slowed down by his deeds will not be hastened by them. Sufficient for him is sufficient for him."
36802,"(36802) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hussein, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Shall I not guide you to the best morals of the people of this world and the hereafter, the one who pardons those who wronged him and gives to whom he deprives him and maintains ties with him? Whoever breaks it off, and whoever would like to have an increase in his life and an increase in his wealth, let him fear God, his Lord, and maintain his mercy. (Tabarani 343. Abd al-Razzaq 20237)"
36803,"(36803) Affan told us, Hammad bin Zaid said, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawzai {The day they will be upon the Fire They will be put to trial. He said: They will be tortured."
36804,"(36804) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza’: “And they fear an evil reckoning.” He said: Discussion in business."
36805,"(36805) Affan told us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid told us, he said: Amr bin Malik told us, he said: I heard Abu Al-Jawzai. He says: Moving the stones is easier for the hypocrite than reciting the Qur’an, and Sa’id said: It is easier for the hypocrite."
36806,"(36806) Affan told us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Amr bin Malik, he said: I heard Abu Al-Jawzai saying in These are the verses: {And I did not create the jinn and mankind except to worship Me. I do not desire from them of provision, nor do I desire that they should be given food.} He said: I I provide for them and I feed them. I created them only to worship Me."
36807,"(36807) Affan told us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid told us, he said: Amr bin Malik told us, he said: I heard Abu Al-Jawzai. He says: They have no food except from the Shrine of Peace. How can one get fat who eats thorns?"
36808,"(36808) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, he said: Abu Ayyub invaded Al-Medina. He said: I said: Constantinople. He said: Yes. He said: He passed by a storyteller who was cutting, and he said: If the slave does the work in... At the beginning of the day, it is presented to the people of his acquaintances from the people of the afterlife at the end of the day, and if he does the work at the end of the day, it is presented to his family. Your acquaintances with the people of the Hereafter in the middle of the day. He said: Then Abu Ayyub said: See what you say? He said: So he said: By God, I say it to you both. He said: Then Abu Ayyub said: O God, I seek refuge in You lest you expose me to My servants. The silent one, and Saad bin Ubadah was pleased with what I did after them. He said: Then the storyteller said: By God, God does not write His commandments to a servant except that He conceals them. His private parts and praised him for his best deeds."
36809,"(36809) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Hammam informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Muslim ibn Yasar, he said: Wadyan Two broad and unfathomable depths, people walk in them, so do deeds that you know that only good deeds will save you, and trust in them. Trust in a man whom you know will not befall you except what God has decreed for you."
36810,"(36810) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, he said: I heard Abu Ma’shar narrating, on the authority of Abraham, narrating, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no town but in it is someone who defends its people, and I hope that he will be Abu Wael. Some of them"
36811,"(36811) Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Sharia, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar {When they throw it in a narrow place} He said: like the narrowness of being thrown into a spear."
36812,"(36812) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Thabit bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalababi, he said: He said: Muslim bin Yassar: If you were among a king requesting a need, it would please you to submit to him."
36813,"(36813) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Ziyad Al-Adawi said: In my sleep, I saw as if I was seeing a one-eyed old man with one big eye and the other was almost closed. There was something amazing adorning it of aquamarines and jewels, so I said: What are you? She said: I am the world, so I said: I seek refuge in God from your evil. She said: If it pleases you for God to protect you from evil, then hate dirhams."
36814,"(?? 6814) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was a Muslim. At the Dirham."
36815,"(36815) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abd Rabbah, on the authority of Abi Ayyad. {And We turn them over to the right and to the left} He said twice every year."
36816,"(36816) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saad bin Ma’abad, he said: Asmaa narrated to me. Ibn Umays, that Ja'far came to her while he was in Abyssinia and he was crying. She said: What is the matter with you? He said: I saw a young man. He passed by a woman and threw out some fine flour that she had, and the wind blew it away. She said: I will eat it for a day. The king sits on the throne and takes possession of the oppressed from the oppressor."
36817,"(36817) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad. He said: When I smell basil, I am reminded of Paradise."
36818,"(36818) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: A man said to Al-Sha’bi: Give us a fatwa, O scholar, He said: The scholar is the one who fears God."
36819,"(36819) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, who said: They hated for a man to give away his son. He takes it out, and the poor sees it and weeps for his family, and the orphan sees it and weeps for his family."
36820,"(36820) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: No servant will understand until he counts calamities as blessings and ease. Misfortune"
36821,"(36821) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: It was astonishing for them to make themselves happy."
36822,"(36822) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, saying: I heard Malik bin Dinar say: A heart that does not There is sadness in it like a ruined house."
36823,"(36823) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Shumayt narrated to us, on the authority of Badil bin Misra Al-Uqaili, Or the rain of abundant rain, for He said: Whoever knows his Lord will love Him, and whoever sees the world will abstain from it, and let not the believing man neglect. Until he has fun, but when he thinks about it, he becomes sad."
36824,"(36824) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sayyar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: The example of one who plunders. The orphan and the widow’s clothing is like the one who earns money from something other than what is lawful and spends on it in something other than what is lawful."
36825,"(36825) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qays, who said: God will command the people of the earth to be punished, so you say The angels: O Lord, among them are children. (Dharmi 3345)"
36826,"(36826) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: It used to be said: No one often mentions death. Unless this is seen in his work."
36827,"(36827) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit used to say: Oh God, if you have granted anyone the prayer In his grave, so give me the prayer in my grave."
36828,"(36828) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Humayd told us, he said: We used to bring people and with us was Thabit. Whenever he passed by a mosque he prayed in it, we would come to a man and he would say: Where is Thabit? Where is Thabit? Where is Thabit? Indeed, he is Thabit. I love her."
36829,"(36829) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Anas said: And he did not say “Shahadat”: Indeed, for every Something is a key, and indeed it is one of the keys to goodness."
36830,"(36830) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: A famine struck the children of Israel. Then a man passed by another man and said: I wish I had this fine sand so that I could feed it to the Children of Israel. He said: So give it to me. His intention"
36831,"(36831) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, who said: It was said: Al-Hakimah is misguided. The believer takes it when he finds it."
36832,"(36832) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: {Their account has drawn near to the people} He said: What they are promised."
36833,"(36833) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who said: Abstinence in this world means shortening hope, and it is not wearing wool, and he mentioned that Al-Awza’i used to say: Asceticism in this world is abandoning Muhammad. He said: You do deeds without wanting people to praise you for them. It was mentioned that Al-Zuhri used to say: Abstinence in this world is as long as the forbidden does not outweigh your patience, and unless the lawful outweighs the lawful. Thank you"
36834,"(36834) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: The scholar should have put the dirt On his head in humility before God."
36835,"(36835) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he said: I have some concessions that I wish I could narrate to you. Do not trust me"
36836,"(36836) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Thabit, who said: There were men from Banu Adiy, some of whom I met if they were One of them prays until he reaches his bed while crawling."
36837,"(36837) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Malik, who said: Indeed, to Allah there is no end on earth. Only steel that is fine and pure is accepted from it. He said: Solid in obedience to God, delicate when remembering God, pure and free from dirt."
36838,"(36838) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Aws, who said: He was a prophet. Among the prophets says: Oh God, protect me with what You protect a child with. He said: So He made me cry."
36839,"(36839) Sa’id bin Shurahbil narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Sa’d informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ayyub. He said: Whoever wants to be more forgiving and increase his knowledge should sit in a gathering other than that of his clan."
36840,"(36840) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: If we were to attend the funeral, we would not know whom to offer our condolences to. He found the people."
36841,"(36841) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ashras Abu Shayban told us, he said: Thabit Al-Bunani told us, he said: We used to follow the funeral procession, and we would see nothing around the bed except someone masked and crying, or thinking, as if there were birds on their heads."
36842,"(36842) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: Two men met in the market, and he said: One of them. To his companion: O my brother, come, let us pray to God and ask His forgiveness for people’s negligence, perhaps He will forgive us. So they did, and it was decided for one of them. He died before his companion, so he came to him in a dream and said: O brother, I sense that God has forgiven us on the eve we met. The market"
36843,"(36843) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Zainab, who said: Whoever comes to the market does not come there except to remember. May God forgive him as many times as he did."
36844,"(36844) Muadh bin Maqil narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, who said: The pilgrims made me cry in this mosque of yours. He was delivering a sermon, and I heard him say: A man who exhorted himself, a man who exhorted himself, a man who did not trust himself to himself, a man who did not entrust himself to himself. He took from himself for himself, a man who had a rebuke to his tongue and heart from God Almighty. He said: So he made me cry."
36845,"(36845) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from the Levant, nicknamed Abu Abdullah, who said: I brought a peacock. So I asked her permission, and an old old man came out to me. I thought he was a peacock. I said: Are you a peacock? He said: No, I am his son. I said: If you are his son, then your father has become senile. He said: He says: The world is not senile. He said: I said: Ask permission for me to come to your father. He said: So he asked permission for me, so I entered upon him. The Sheikh said: Ask and be brief. I said: If you brief me. I summarized for you, so he said: Do not ask, I will teach you in your assembly this Qur’an and the Torah and the Gospel: Fear God for fear until No one is more afraid of you than him, and your hope for him is stronger than your fear of him, and love for people what you love for yourself."
36846,"(36846) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurriyah, who said: Al-Hasan loved to keep up with work. He said: Muhammad said: What do you think if he was active and lazy all night, and you did not see any harm in him?"
36847,"(36847) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, who said: Abu Sa’id narrated to me, on the authority of Zaid. Ibn Arqam said: Worship God as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then He sees you, and consider yourself in death. And beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it will be answered."
36848,"(36848) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Khawlani, he said: There are three scholars: a man who lived by his knowledge and people lived by it, and a man who lived by his knowledge but did not live by it. No one other than him, and a man who made people live with his knowledge and who destroyed himself with it."
36849,"(36849) Affan told us, he said: Zurayk bin Abi Zurayk told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: O son of Adam, put your foot down. On your land and know that after a little while it will be your grave."
36850,"(36850) Affan told us, he said: Zurayk bin Abi Zurayk told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan saying: O son of Adam, You look at your deeds and weigh the good and the bad, and do not despise any of the good, even if it is small, for when you see it it pleases you. its place, and do not despise any evil, for if you see it wandering its place, may God have mercy on a servant who earns well and spends intentionally. And they placed them in virtue, and they placed these ransoms where God directed them, and they placed them where God commanded them to be placed. Before you, they used to sell their souls for the bounty from God, and this death has harmed the world and exposed it, so God does not He was found to have a joyful heart."
36851,"(36851) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Dhudhail, on the authority of Abu Al-Ubaidin He said: If they attack you with the mutilate, then take your loaf of bread, restore your fire, and keep your religion."
36852,"(36852) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Al-Manhal, he said: Ali said: It is forbidden for every soul. To leave this world until you know where your destination is."
36853,"(36853) Affan narrated to us, he said: Mubarak bin Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Adi bin Arta, on the authority of a man He was from the beginning of this nation. He said: When they praised him, he heard that. He said: Oh God, do not hold me accountable for what they say. And forgive me what they do not know."
36854,"(36854) Affan told us, he said: Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali Ibn al-Hanafiyyah said: He is not wise who does not treat people with kindness, who does not find a way to find relief for him. And a way out."
36855,"(36855) Affan narrated to us, Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Ammar bin Ghaziyya narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, On the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If God loves a servant, he protects him in this world as it always does. One of you protects his sick water."
36856,"(36856) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: There is nothing more secret for a believer than that He is alone."
36857,"(36857) Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, he said: Abdullah said: The world is the home of one who has no home, and money. He who has no money, and he who has no mind has work."
36858,"(36858) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidullah bin Saeed Al-Ja’fi, who said: Issa bin Maryam, peace be upon them, said: My home is the mosque, my source of water, my quencher of hunger, my emblem of fear, the beast of my feet, and my resting place in the winter. The summer sunshine, and my lamp in the moonlit night, and my servants of time and the poor, and my evening and I have nothing, and the morning and I have nothing. I have something, and I am fine, so who is better off than me?"
36859,"(36859) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, that some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him. They said: O Messenger of God, we do things in secret, and we hear people talking about them, so we like to be mentioned. He was fine, so he said: You have two rewards: the reward of secretness and the reward of publicity. (Tayalisi 2430. Ibn Hibban 375)"
36860,"(36860) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Ubaid informed us, saying: Al-Hasan narrated to us, that two men from the companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of them died before his companion, so they preferred the one who died and was better in themselves. Of the last, so that was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Didn’t the last remain after the first, all together, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And so he prayed. He said: It is as if he preferred the second."
36861,"(36861) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Dhabi narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’. He said: “Seek refuge in God from the humility of hypocrisy.” He said: It was said: “O Abu Darda’, and what is the humility of hypocrisy?” He said: “To see the body.” Humbled, but the heart is not humble."
36862,"(36862) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, he said: When it was said To David: You have been forgiven. He said: So how about the man? He said: It was said to him: We seek you from him and he grants you to us. To hope for this world."
36863,"(36863) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban bin Zaid Al-Attar narrated to us, he said: His qatadah narrated to us: He said Abu Al-Aliyah narrated to us. Al-Rihihi, on the authority of the hadith of Sahl ibn Hanzala al-Abashami, that he said: No people gathered together to remember God except that a herald called out from among them. Heavens: Arise, and you will be forgiven. Your evil deeds have been changed into good deeds."
36864,"(36864) Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, saying: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, he said: It was. It is said: Knowledge is the desire of a believer. He begins his search for it, so if he attains something from it Hawwa"
36865,"(36865) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Rawwad narrated to us, that the Companions of the Prophet prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. Joking and laughter appeared among them, so God Almighty revealed: {Has not the time come for those who believe that you should submit to humility? Their hearts are for the remembrance of God} until the end of the verses."
36866,"(36866) Muhammad bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, that a people accompanied Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he said: You must fear God alone, with no partner, and beware of joking, for it removes evil and causes grudges. And sit with the Qur’an and converse with it. If it is burdensome for you, then it is a hadith from the hadith of men. Walk in the name of God."
36867,"(36867) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that I wrote to Muawiyah: I advise you to fear God, for if you fear God, people are sufficient for you. If you fear people, they will not be of use to you. anything from God, so you must fear God. As for what comes after that."
36868,"(36868) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: No servant has ever taken a better dose. There is a reward from God for a dose that one suppressed for the sake of God, seeking the face of God. (Bukhari 1318)"
36869,"(36869) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Musa, who said: Do not learn for this world, do not understand hypocrisy, and do not You will laugh without ambiguity, and you will not walk without ambiguity."
36870,"(36870) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Rustum, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiah, who said: I accompanied Ibn Abbas from... He went from Mecca to Medina and from Medina to Mecca. Whenever he came down to a certain place, he would stand up for half the night and do that more often. Sobbing. I said: What is sobbing? He said: Weeping and crying. And it is recited: {And the intoxication of death has come in truth. That is what I was. What do you deviate from?"
36871,"(36871) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, he said: It was Jesus is the son of Mary, peace be upon them both, and Yahya is my cousin. Jesus used to wear wool, and Yahya used to wear And there was not for any of them a dinar, nor a dirham, nor a manservant, nor a maidservant, nor any shelter to shelter him. Wherever the night covered them, they were sheltered. When they wanted to separate, Yahya said to him: Advise me. He said: Do not get angry. He said: No. I can't help but get angry. He said: Don't acquire money. He said: As for this, it's okay."
36872,"(36872) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, regarding the words of God Almighty: {And a cup of fresh water} He said: A cup of the wine of a slave girl."
36873,"(36873) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Sa’id bin Zaid told us, he said: Sa’id bin Iyas Al-Jariri told us, he said: Abu Al-Alaa told us that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was overcome by death, so he started saying: By the way. And he was anxious. It was said to him: Why were you anxious? He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: The world is not enough for me. He said: A servant and a coachman, so I am not. I was silent and did not ask him. When I asked him, I concluded what he said, and I attained from the world while in my hand what was in my hand. And death came to me."
36874,"(36874) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: A verse revealed about This nation: {Say: Shall I inform you of something better than that?} Omar said: Now, O Lord."
36875,"(36875) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Zaid, brother of Hammad bin Zaid, narrated to us, saying: Othman Al-Shaham narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Wasi’ narrated to us, saying: I came from Mecca and saw a bridge over the ditch, so I took it and was taken to Marwan ibn Al-Muhallab, who is the prince of Basra, welcomed me and said: I need you, O Abu Abdullah. I said: I need you if you are able to Should I be as the brother of Banu Adi said? He said: Who is the brother of Banu Adi? He said: Al-Ala’ ibn Ziyad. He said: A friend of his hired someone for work, so he wrote to her: As for what follows, if you are able not to spend the night Unless your back is light, your stomach is swollen, and your palms are clean from the blood and property of Muslims, then if you do that, you will not May there be a way upon you. {Indeed, the way is upon those who oppress people and transgress in the land} the verses. Marwan said: He has spoken the truth, by God. He gave advice, then said: I need you, O Abu Abdullah. I said: I need you to join me with my family. He said: So he said: Yes."
36876,"(36876) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Yasa, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, who said: Indeed, in the jinn. For a tree, God did not create a beautiful voice except that within its trunk was your pleasure and enjoyment."
36877,"(36877) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Three scholars They gathered together and said to one of them: What is your hope? He said: Not a month passes without me thinking that I will die during it. They said: This is hope. They said to the other: What do I have? He said: What? A group of people came to me, but I thought I would die there. They said to the third: What is the matter with you? He said: No one trusts himself in the hands of anyone else."
36878,"(36878) Affan narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He was striking like the son of Adam. Like a man who was about to die, and his family attended him and his deeds, and he said to his family: Prevent me. They said: We were only preventing you from doing something. This world, as for this, we cannot prevent you from it, so he said to his money: Are you preventing me? He said: I have been adorned for you in this world, but as for this, I cannot prevent you from it. He said: Then his deed was rewarded, and he said: I am your companion who will enter your grave with you and will stay with you wherever you stay. He said: By God, if I had felt it, I would have preferred the three with me. He said: Al-Hasan said: Now, choose it over everything else."
36879,"(36879) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Kardous al-Talabi, who said: It is written in the Torah: Beware of fearing him, but fear is only With piety, have mercy and you will be shown mercy, repent and you will be forgiven."
36880,"(36880) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Abu Nazrih, that a man entered Paradise. He saw his angel above him like a star, and he said: By God, O Lord, this is your angel in this world, so he did not send it down. This is the revelation. He said: This was the best deed on your part."
36881,"(36881) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: If you had seen the I saw that your liver would be burned for them, and Abraham said: If the night were to be long for me until I came in the morning and I would see it."
36882,"(36882) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Musa al-Tamimi told us, he said: An-Nawwar, the wife of Al-Farazdaq, died. At her funeral, the faces of the people of Basra came out, and Al-Hasan came out, so Al-Hasan said to Al-Farazdaq: You have not prepared for this. Today, Abu Firas, he said: He bore witness that there is no god but Allah eighty years ago. He said: When she was buried, he rose over her grave. And he said:
I fear beyond the grave if he does not heal me.
When a leader comes to me on the Day of Resurrection
He who walked has been disappointed by the sons of Dharm.
More troubling and narrower than the grave
Violent and violent driver
To Hell, the chain of the necklace is blue."
36883,"I read to Muslimah bin Al-Qasim. Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Jahm, known as Ibn Al-Warraq Al-Maliki, spoke to you in Baghdad. In Rabi` al-Awwal, of the year one hundred and twenty-four, he said: It was recited to Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Abdoos bin Kamil al-Siraj, And I hear from him. He was ninety years old. He said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah Al-Kufi told us, he said:
(36883) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of his father and Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: He was the first to judge. In Kufa, here is Salman bin Rabi’a Al-Bahili. He sat for forty days without any adversary coming to him."
36884,"(36884) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: The first to take out the pulpit during the two Eids was Bishr bin Marwan, and the first to give the call to prayer for the two Eids was Ziyad."
36885,"(36885) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: The first one to deliver the sermon sitting with Mu’awiyah when he grew old and multiplied His fat and abdominal bones."
36886,"(36886) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Uthman bin Yassar, on the authority of Tamim bin Hudhalam, he said: The first He greeted Amir with Al-Kufi with the word Al-Amirah. He said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba came out of the palace and a man from Canada came to him and greeted him. He asked him about the woman, and he said: What is this? I am but one of them. I left it for a while, then he continued it after that."
36887,"(36887) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Othman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, He said: The first person to deliver a sermon on the pulpit was Ibrahim, the friend of God Almighty."
36888,"(36888) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: Ibrahim was the first of the people to add The guest, and the first of people to be circumcised, and the first of people to trim his nails, trim his mustache, and use the sunshade."
36889,"(36889) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, that Abraham was the first to see gray hair. He said: O Lord, what is this? He said: Dignity. He said: Oh God, increase me in dignity."
36890,"(36890) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Fire was shown to me, and in it I saw Amr ibn Luhayy ibn Qama’i ibn Khandaf dragging his reed through it. Fire, and he was the first to change the covenant of Abraham, peace be upon him, and to leave the impurities free. (Abu Yali 6095. Ibn Hibban 7490)"
36891,"(36891) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, who said: The first to introduce the greeting in Mecca Abd al-Rahman bin Abza."
36892,"(36892) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The first person to decrease the takbeer was Ziyad."
36893,"(36893) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Khalid ibn Arfatah, he said: The first thing I saw was the disagreement between Muhammad’s companions when Othman called for Hajj and Ali called for Hajj and Umar."
36894,"(36894) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, he said, He was the first to take the two sticks, Ziyad spoke while sitting and the call to prayer was given in front of him during the Eid."
36895,"(36895) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: He was the first to take an increased wage from the market."
36896,"(36896) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, who said: I was my father’s guide when he lost his sight, and whenever I went out with him to the congregational prayers and he heard the call to prayer, I would ask forgiveness for my father in front of him. Asaad bin Zurarah and prayed for him, so I said to him: Father, what is the matter with you if you hear the call to prayer on Friday, ask forgiveness for my father? Imam of him, and I prayed for him and prayed for him. He said: Yes, my son. He was the first to join the prayer for us before the arrival of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “And how were you that day?” He said: We were forty men.
(Abu Dawud 1062; Ibn Majah 1082)"
36897,"(36897) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: The first thing I heard at a funeral was, “Ask forgiveness for him, he will forgive him.” May God bless you in the funeral of Saeed bin Aws."
36898,"(36898) Abu Usamah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Hakim, who said: The first to institute zakat was four days. One hundred dinars Omar bin Abdul Aziz."
36899,"(36899) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, that Umm Ayman ordered the coffin for the women."
36900,"(36900) Abu Asama told us, he said: Sufyan told me, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: Umm More reliable than the Abyssinians, and she ordered the casket to be given to the women."
36901,"(36901) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Abd Khayr, who said: I heard Ali saying: May God have mercy on him. Abu Bakr was the first to combine the two tablets."
36902,"(36902) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abd Khair, who said: I heard Ali saying: May God have mercy on him. May God bless Abu Bakr, he was the first to combine what was between the two tablets."
36903,"(36903) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The first to start With the sermon on the day of Eid before the prayer, Marwan."
36904,"(36904) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first to speak out loud, and the first to announce the salutation during prayer, was Omar bin Al-Khattab."
36905,"(36905) Waki` narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The first to narrate The Adhan on the two Eids, Muawiyah."
36906,"(36906) Waki’ narrated to us, my father narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, he said: The first to narrate the call to prayer In Al-Aidin Ibn Al-Zubayr."
36907,"(36907) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Imamah, He said: The first person to pray the Duha prayer was Dhul-Zawa’id, a man who used to come to the market for needs and pray."
36908,"(36908) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The first person to give the horse two arrows was Omar bin Al-Khattab, he referred to it. Ali was a man from Banu Tamim."
36909,"(36909) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The first to pronounce the Mu’awwidhatin loudly in prayer. Ubaid Allah bin Ziyad."
36910,"(36910) Qutaybah bin Sa’id narrated to us, Laith bin Sa’d narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: We were informed that Khadija bint Khuwaylid, wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the first to believe in God and His Messenger, and she died before Prayer is made obligatory."
36911,"(36911) Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: It was among the character of the ancients to look at the Qur’an."
36912,"(36912) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abu Umair told me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The first of the Arab women to do the hadith to drag their tails was Umm Ismail, who said: When she ran away from Sara, she let down her tail. So that her traces may be spared, and the first to circumambulate between Safa and Marwah was Umm Ismail."
36913,"(36913) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first to demonstrate Islam were seven: the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and Abu Bakr, Bilal, Khabbab, Sahayb, and Ammar, and she was named Umm Ammar."
36914,"(36914) Hammad Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Aamir told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abza told me, he said: I prayed. With Omar Ali Zainab, and she was the first of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to die after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
36915,"(36915) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abu Hamza, the client of the Ansar, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Arqam, he said: The first to convert to Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali. I mentioned it to Abraham but he denied it. He said: Abu Bakr."
36916,"(36916) Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Protectors were given to a man to kill the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, so God informed him of that, so he ordered that he be crucified, and he was the first to be crucified in Islam. (Abu Dawud 298)"
36917,"(36917) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that he heard Abd Allah bin Al-Harith bin Jazi’ Al-Zubaidi says: I am the first to hear the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: None of you will be ignorant. The future of the qibla, and I will be the first to tell people about it."
36918,"(36918) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Zakariya, who said: He was the first of the tribes to unite with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him."
36919,"(36919) Waki’ told us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The first to pledge allegiance to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. Al-Ridwan was sold to Abu Sinan Al-Asadi."
36920,"(36920) Waki’ told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first martyr to be martyred in Islam. Umm Ammar, Abu Jahl stabbed her in the forehead with a spear."
36921,"(36921) Waki’ told us, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman: He said: The first among the Muslims to be martyred On the day of Badr, the refuge of Omar's family."
36922,"(36922) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed She is a grandfather with a sixth son, and she was the first grandmother to inherit an inheritance in Islam."
36923,"(36923) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the right with the witness: an innovation, and the first Whoever Mu'awiyah ruled on it."
36924,"(36924) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The first to leave one of his fingers in his ears Ibn Al-Asam"
36925,"(36925) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Raising the hands on the day of Friday prayer is modern, and the first to Marwan introduced the raising of hands on Friday."
36926,"(36926) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The first to raise his hands in congregation. Ubaidullah bin Muammar."
36927,"(36927) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The first person to be crucified in Islam was a man from Bani Layth, for whom the Quraysh appointed guardians to kill the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Gabriel came to him and informed him. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to him and he was ordered to be crucified."
36928,"(36928) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The first kid that was fed in Islam was one-sixth of the kid that was fed. And her son is alive."
36929,"(36929) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, on the authority of a boy of Salman’s He was also called Suwayd, and he praised him well, saying: When the people conquered the cities and went out in pursuit of the enemy, I was struck, and he said: Salman: Do you have any food? So I said: I brought it to you. He said: Bring it. If it is money, We raise it to those. It was food that we ate. He said: So we opened it and behold, loaves of bread, cheese, and knives. It was the first thing the Arabs saw. Dialogue"
36930,"(36930) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: They were making bets on the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Al-Zuhri said: The first one to give it to him was Omar bin Al-Khattab."
36931,"(36931) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far: I said to Al-Zuhri: Who was the first of the Arabs to inherit from the slaves? He said: Omar. Ibn Al-Khattab"
36932,"(36932) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man who narrated to him that Abu Bakr circumambulated With Abdullah bin Al-Zubair in a rag, and he was the first child born in Islam."
36933,"(36933) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Utbah, meaning Al Masoudi, on the authority of Al Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, He said: The first to reveal the Qur’an in Mecca was Ibn Masoud, and the first to build a mosque. Ammar bin Yasser prayed there, and the first to call the call to prayer was Bilal, and the first to shoot an arrow in the way of God was Saad bin Malik, and the first Whoever of the Muslims is killed is a place of refuge, and the first to gallop his horse in the way of God is Miqdad, and the first alive to give alms from Before themselves, the Banu Uthrah, and the first living people to unite with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Jahaina."
36934,"(36934) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ismail, Aamir told us, he said: The first to pledge allegiance under the tree, was it Sinan ibn Wahhab? Al-Asadi, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: What do you pledge allegiance to? He said, “For what is in your mind,” so he pledged allegiance to him, then People followed one another and pledged allegiance to him."
36935,"(36935) Abu Usama told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Amir, who said: The first one who indicated the making of the coffin was to raise the names of Ibn Umays: When she came from the land of Abyssinia, she saw them doing this to their land."
36936,"(36936) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyyah Al-Jarami, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about Al-Badhaq, and he said: Muhammad Al-Badhik preceded me. I was the first Arab to ask Ibn Abbas about that."
36937,"(36937) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Ghanam, who said: The first grandfather to inherit In Islam, Omar bin Al-Khattab wanted to take possession of all the money, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, they are trees below you. That means his children."
36938,"(36938) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When Omar bin The disputing speaker imposed the duties, wrote down the collections of books, and introduced the diviners."
36939,"(36939) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, Harim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaidullah. Al-Thaqafi, he said: Omar, a man from Thaqif called Nafi’ ibn Al-Harith, came and he was the first to conquer the fleets in Basra."
36940,"(36940) Affan narrated to us, Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, I heard Al-Baraa’ say: The first of the companions to come to us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Musab bin Umair and Ibn Umm Maktum, and they started reciting the Qur’an to the people. He said: Then Ammar came. And Bilal and Saad, then Omar bin Al-Khattab came with twenty passengers, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and I did not see The people of Medina were happy with something that made them happy with it. (Bukhari 3924, Ahmed 284)"
36941,"(36941) Waki’ narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not interrupt Nor Abu Bakr, nor Omar, nor Ali, and the first to seize the herds was Othman, and the lands were sold during the emirate of Othman."
36942,"(36942) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The first person to sit on the pulpit in the assembly was Muawiyah."
36943,"(36943) Shababah told us, Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Habib al-Urani, on the authority of Ali, he said: I The first man to pray with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
36944,"(36944) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abi Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, who said: I told Ibn Hanafi: Abu Bakr was the first of the people to convert to Islam. He said: No."
36945,"(36945) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Zayed bin Qadamah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The first to demonstrate his Islam was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Ammar, and his mother was named Wasiyb. And Bilal and Al-Miqdad."
36946,"(36946) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Shabi, who said: Shurayh Omar passed judgment on the Kufa in A case, and Ka'b bin Sur ruled against Basra in a case."
36947,"(36947) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The first living people to unite with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him."
36948,"(36948) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shaiban narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu Layla said: I was sitting close to Ka’b ibn Ajra on Friday, and Al-Dahhak ibn Qais addressed us and he sat down. He said: Don't you see, by God, I have not seen the imam of a Muslim people giving a sermon sitting down."
36949,"(36949) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Arara, on the authority of Ali, a man said to him: Tell me, Regarding the House, was it the first House established for the people? He said: No, but it was the first House in which the blessing was placed in place of Abraham. Whoever enters it is safe."
36950,"(36950) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Amir, who said: The first to make the tithe was Omar bin Al-Khattab"
36951,"(36951) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: The first one I saw. Walking between the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone was Urwah ibn al-Zubayr."
36952,"(36952) Abu Osama narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, he said: It was said to Al-Hasan: Who is the first to free the mothers of his children? Omar said, I said: So... He will curse them if they commit adultery. He said: No, by God, then."
36953,"(36953) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, met a people There was a sharp man among them, and when they saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the sharp one remained silent, and he said: From the people. They said: From Mudar. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am from Mudar. He said: What is the matter with one of you who does not attack? They said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: We are the first of the Arabs to wear camels. He said: And what is that? They said: A man from among us, whom they called, fought among his camels in the days of Spring, so he sent a boy of his with the camels, and the boy slowed down, then he came and started hitting them with a stick on his hand, so the boy set off. And he said: And his hands, his hands, and his hands, he said: Then the camels moved and became active, so he said to him: Hold you, hold you, he said: So the people opened The shoe"
36954,"(36954) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Shu’bi, and al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Indeed, the father of the one who made an obligation The gift was given to Omar bin Al-Khattab and he imposed a full blood money on it."
36955,"(36955) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Al-Ala bin Al-Hadrami to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for eight hundred thousand from the tax of Bahrain, and it was the first tax he submitted. to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he ordered it to be spread on mats in the mosque, and the muezzin called the call to prayer and he went out to pray. So he prayed, then he came to the money and appeared standing over it, but he did not give silently and did not prevent a beggar, so he made the man come and say: Give me, and he says: Take a handful, then the man comes and says: Give me, and he says: Take two handfuls, and the man comes So he says: Give it to me. So he says: Take three handfuls. Then Al-Abbas came and said: O Messenger of God, give me some of this money. I gave a ransom and the ransom of Aqil on the day of Badr, and Aqil had no money. He said: So he began to spread out his khamisah, which was Ali, and he made a load of money, so he searched it, then he got up with it, but he could not bear to carry it, so he said: O Messenger of God, carry it. Ali, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at him and smiled until he seemed to laugh at him, and said: Save money and do as much as you can. Tattiq, then when Al-Abbas took charge, he said: As for one of the two things that God promised us, He has fulfilled one of them for us, and we are waiting for the other. His saying God Almighty: {O Prophet, say to those of the prisoners in your hands, “Indeed, God knows that there is good in your hearts” until the end of the verses. God has accomplished it for us while we await the afterlife."
36956,"(36956) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The first to Satan measured, but the sun and the moon were worshiped according to standards."
36957,"(36957) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, who said: The first time people spoke about fate, a man came. He said: It was by God’s will that sparks flew and burned the house. A man said: This is God’s will, and another said: It is not by God’s will. God"
36958,"(36958) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amer, who said: The first to pledge allegiance under the tree was Abu Sinan ibn Wahhab. Al-Asadi came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I pledge allegiance to you. He said: Why do you pledge allegiance to me? He said: I pledge allegiance to you for what is in it. yourself, then people pledged allegiance to him after that."
36959,"(36959) Abu Asama told us, Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais who heard Saad bin Abi Waqqas say: I, by God, am the first man. From the Arabs, he shot an arrow for the sake of God Almighty."
36960,"(36960) Hussein narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil narrated to us, he said: Anas said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated to us. He said: I am the first intercessor in Paradise."
36961,"(36961) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Sa’d, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah, who said: The first to emigrate from this nation were two men from Quraysh."
36962,"(36962) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ya’qub bin Mujma’ informed me, on the authority of his father, he said: The first person I saw praying on his sandals was Utba bin Awaim bin Sa`id."
36963,"(36963) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, he said: The first surah. It was revealed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: {Recite in the name of your Lord who created}"
36964,"(36964) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bai, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Ubaid ibn Umair saying: The first thing that was revealed was From the Qur’an {Read in the name of your Lord who created} then Nun."
36965,"(36965) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I learned from Abu Musa: {Recite in the name of your Lord who created} It is the first surah that was revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
36966,"(36966) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: This is the first surah that was revealed: (Read in the name of your Lord who created) then (N)"
36967,"(36967) A sheikh of ours narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, who said: The first person to porridge porridge was Abraham, peace be upon him."
36968,"(36968) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Rabah, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The first one to dye his hair black was Pharaoh."
36969,"(36969) Othman bin Matar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, who said: The first man to dye his hair in Islam was Abu Quhafiya. He was shown to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his head like a mole, and he said: Change it with something and keep it from blackness."
36970,"(36970) Waki` narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, he said: I asked Mujahid about the two muezzins performing the call to prayer one by one, and he said: That is something that the princes underestimated."
36971,"(36971) Waki’ narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Who The first one to call it Al-Atama, he said: Satan."
36972,"(36972) Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Samaan bin Mujma’, on the authority of Ya’qub bin Mujma’, on the authority of his father Muja’im bin Zaid said: The first person I saw praying in sandals was Utba bin Awaim bin Sa’id."
36973,"(36973) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He was the first to start the war. Othman bin Affan. The first person to ask the student for clear evidence that his rival died and his debt was owed by him was Othman bin Affan."
36974,"(36974) Malik told us, he said: Masoud bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The first to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, gathered the people to pray in Ramadan. He gathered them together with Ubayy Ibn Ka’b."
36975,"(36975) Malik narrated to us, Masoud bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The first of the Arabs to write, meaning In Arabic, Harb bin Umayyah bin Abd Shams. It was said: From those who learned that. He said: From the people of Al-Hira. He said: From those who learned it. The people of Al-Hira, he said: from the people of Al-Anbar."
36976,"(36976) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Rabah bin Abi Marouf narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Abi Tawaf Rabi’a was with Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan until, when he was on the seventh circumambulation of the House, he would adhere to it, then Al-Harith took him by the hand. So he turned to him and said: What is the matter with you, Harith? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, do you know who was the first to do this? An old man. The old women of your people. He said: He stopped and did not adhere to it."
36977,"(36977) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The first word, This was said by Abraham, peace be upon him, when he was thrown into the Fire. God is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs."
36978,"(36978) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Al-Harith bin Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata’, he said: The first mountain made on earth was Abu Qubays."
36979,"(36979) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said: The first On the day I knew the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I was walking with Abu Jahl in Mecca, and we met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So he said to him: O Abu Al-Hakam, come to God, to His Messenger, and to His Book, I invite you to God. He said: O Muhammad, you are not abstaining from cursing our gods. Do you only want us to bear witness that you have conveyed the message? We bear witness that you have conveyed it. I have conveyed it. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him and came to me and said: By God, I know best that what he says True, but the Banu Qusayy said: Among us is the veil, so we said: Yes, then they said: Among us are the villages, so we said: Yes, then they said: Among us The prayer, so we said: Yes, then they said among us is the watering, so we said yes, then they fed and we fed until when the knees rubbed together, they said : Among us is a prophet, by God, I will not do it."
36980,"(36980) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: The first people I knew of Bahr al-Bahair was a man from Banu Mudlij who had two she-camels, so he cut off their ears and deprived them of their milk. And their backs, and I saw him and them in the Fire, flopping around in their socks and biting it with their mouths, and indeed I knew the first people to remove the Ḥaībīb, set up the ṣābīb, and change the covenant of Abraham, Amr ibn Luhi, and I saw him dragging his reed in Fire hurts the people of Hell by dragging their reeds. (Abdul Razzaq 197)"
36981,"(36981) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Jarir, that he said: The beginning of the earth will be desolation and its plains. Then it will be followed by its right hand, and the gathering will be here, and I will follow it."
36982,"(36982) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majid Al-Hanafi, who said: I was sitting at Abdullah, narrating to us, stated that the first person to cut off a wound in Islam, or among the Muslims, was a man from the Ansar.
(Ahmad 391, Abu Ali 5133)"
36983,"(36983) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The first one to name it Al-Atam: Satan"
36984,"(36984) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Shaddad bin Maqil, he said: Abdullah said: The first thing You will lose trust in your religion, and the last thing you will lose is prayer."
36985,"(36985) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of his father, he said: The first words that Omar spoke were If he said: Oh God, I am weak, so strengthen me, and I am strong, so soften me, and I am stingy, so make me hot."
36986,"(36986) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Hudayr, who said: I am the first to He tithed in Islam."
36987,"(36987) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The first person to cut a man was Abu Bakr."
36988,"(36988) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman Al-A’shi, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah. Or on the authority of his brother Husain, one of them on the authority of the other, he said: Salman mentioned the emergence of some of the mothers of the believers, and he said: It was a The First Book of God, or in the First Psalms."
36989,"(36989) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Murra, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Who If he wants knowledge, let him spread the Qur’an, for in it is information for the ancients and the last."
36990,"(36990) Ibn Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, that Omar, may God have mercy on him, was the first to impose The gifts"
36991,"(36991) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Abu Idris, that Daniel was the first to separate the witnesses."
36992,"(36992) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The first person to know about insight was Ibn Abbas."
36993,"(36993) Hammad bin Masada and Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The first person to recite it was a king. Marwan"
36994,"(36994) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abu Kudayna told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, he said: The first person to sit on the pulpit during the two Eids and call the call to prayer during them was Ziyad, who is called Ibn Abi Sufyan."
36995,"(36995) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that a man narrated to him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The first banner to knock on the door of Paradise is my banner, and the first to whom the call to intercession is made is me, and no pride."
36996,"(36996) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar, he said: Anas said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said : I am the first intercessor in Paradise."
36997,"(36997) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, Abdullah bin Salam narrated to us, he said: When the Messenger of The people dispersed before him, and it was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came three times, so I came. among the people to look at him, and when I saw his face, I knew that his face was not like that of a liar, so that was the first thing. I heard him speaking about it when he said: O people, extend your greetings, provide food, maintain the ties of kinship, and pray with the people. Asleep, you will enter Paradise in peace."
36998,"(36998) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings be upon him: I will be the first to knock on the door of Paradise."
36999,"(36999) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am the master of the descendants of Adam, and the first from whom the earth will open, and the first Intercessor and the first to be interceded."
37000,"(37,000) Al-Fadl narrated to us, Al-Walid bin Juma’ narrated to us, he said: Your grandmother narrated to me, on the authority of Umm Warqa ibn Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Ansari, that a boy of hers and a maid of hers drowned her and killed her during the rule of Umar, and that they fled, so he was brought to them. Omar crucified them, and they were the first to be crucified in Medina."
37001,"(37001) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Ma’bad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Hudhayf ibn Asid, who said: The last of Two men from Quraysh will be gathered from this nation. (Muslim 1010, Hakim 566)"
37002,"(37002) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: I was informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The last to be gathered from this nation will be two men from Quraysh."
37003,"(37003) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, enjoyed it. Peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, Omar and Othman, and the first to be forbidden by Muawiyah."
37004,"(37004) Ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ka’b, He said: The first to take the door of Paradise by the throat and have it opened for him is Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
37005,"(37005) Shazan narrated to us, Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, he said: Zubaid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ka’b, he said The first verses in the Torah that were revealed in the Qur’an were ten verses, and these were the ten that were revealed in the last of the An’am."
37006,"(37006) Aswad bin Ali told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, who said: The first of the verses will be general and the last of them will be specific. He recited these verses: {And on the Day of Resurrection they will be returned to the severest of the torment, and what God is unaware of what you do."
37007,"(37007) His youth narrated to us, his people narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, he said: I heard Ibn Masoud says about the Children of Israel, Al-Kahf, Maryam, Watta, and the Prophets: They are from the first era and they are from your generation."
37008,"(37008) Ishaq ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: It is written in the first book: The example of Abu Bakr is the example of Dropping wherever it falls is beneficial."
37009,"(37009) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will be the first to breathe water. The earth and the first intercessor."
37010,"(37010) Ahwas bin Jawab narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Baja, who said: The first humiliation that entered upon me The Arabs killed Hussein bin Ali and claimed Ziyad."
37011,"(37011) Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaidah told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbi, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Samarra said: The first person to throw an arrow in the way of God Almighty was Saad."
37012,"(37012) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from Thaqif, who said: A man from Thaqif consulted Thaqif asked Omar to set up the mosque, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, it is gentler and more forgiving of the pituitary and mucus, so Omar said: They counted it from the blessed valley of Al-Aqiq. The first person to count the mosque was Omar, may God be pleased with him."
37013,"(37013) Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The first one to introduce the Qur’anic narration was after Imam Al-Mukhtar, and they were not They read."
37014,"(37014) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Omar was the first to make the blood money a tenth of the money given to fighters, not the people."
37015,"(37015) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, and Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, They said: The first to enact the prayer upon killing was Khubayb bin Adiyy."
37016,"(37016) Qubaysah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sa’sa’a, he said: The first to combine The Qur’an and Abu Bakr inherited the Quran."
37017,"(37017) Wakī’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The first thing that will be judged among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed."
37018,"(37018) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq ibn Salamah, on the authority of Amr ibn Shurahbil, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The first thing that will be judged on the Day of Resurrection among people will be bloodshed. (Nasa’i 3458)"
37019,"(37019) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, plotted on the day One of the polytheists, and that was the first day on which deception was planned."
37020,"(37020) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, Al-Sa’q bin Hazan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah Al-Dhabi’i, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The first The Arabs said: Quraysh and Rabi’ah will be destroyed. They said: Wakayf. He said: As for Quraysh, they will be destroyed by the king. As for Rabi’ Fever will destroy her."
37021,"(37021) Muhammad bin Al-Hassan narrated to us, Thabit bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The beginning of the earth is desolation. Armenia, then Egypt."
37022,"(37022) Muhammad bin Al-Hassan narrated to us, Zaid bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding his saying: {Sidrāḥ Al-Muntahi} He said: The first day of the Hereafter, and the last day of this world, so that is where it will end."
37023,"(37023) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The first thing that God created was the pen. Then He created the Nun. (Ibn Jarir 29)"
37024,"(37024) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of some of his companions. On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The first thing that God created was the pen, and the nun and the medicine were created for it."
37025,"(37025) Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered it. And peace be upon him, Al-Fadl, Asama bin Zaid, and Talha bin Uthman. Ibn Umar said: So I entered, and he was the first one I met Bilal, so I said: Where did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray? He said: Between these two pillars."
37026,"(37026) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Jabir Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Kindi, he said: Ali said to Ibn Al-Kawa’i: Do you know what the first one said: “Love your lover lightly, for he may one day be the one who hates you, and I hate the one who hates you.” Here he may be your lover one day."
37027,"(37027) Dhudha bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Abu Dharr, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The first to change your Sunnah will be a man from the Umayyads."
37028,"(37028) Ibn Numair narrated to us, Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’i, he said: He said: Abdullah: The first thing you will lose in your religion is trust, and the last thing you will lose is prayer."
37029,"(37029) Yahya bin Ali Al-Aslami told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mu’amil, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, He said: It was the first Islam of Omar. He said: Omar said: He struck my laboring sister. He said: So I was taken out of the house and entered into a shelter. The Ka'bah on a hot night. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and entered the Hijr with his sandals on. He said: So he prayed. God willing, then he left, and I heard something the likes of which I had never heard, so I went out and followed him. He said: Who is this? I said: Omar. He said: O Omar, do not leave me alone day or night. He said: I was afraid that he would pray for me, so I said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Messenger of God, and he said: O Umar, conceal him. He said: So I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will declare it just as you announced polytheism.
(Musnad 4329. Abu Nu’aym 39)"
37030,"(37030) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mahrez bin Salih, that Ali was the first to separate the witnesses."
37031,"(37031) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Urwah ibn Rumaym, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The first thing that my Lord forbade me was from worshiping idols, from drinking alcohol, and from men who walk with Him."
37032,"(37032) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a Bedouin. He sells something, and he says: You pay the first price, or the first price, for profit comes with tolerance."
37033,"(37033) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, he said: Ibn Abbas said to me: Do you know which is the last surah in which all of them were revealed? I said: {When the victory and conquest of God has come} He said: You have spoken the truth."
37034,"(37034) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, on the authority of Qubaisah Bin Dhu’ayb, that Abu Salamah was the cousin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was the first to emigrate with a large flock of sheep. To the land of Ethiopia, then to Medina."
37035,"(37035) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The last verse to be revealed In the Qur’an: {They ask you for a fatwa. Say, “Allah gives you a fatwa concerning the words}."
37036,"(37036) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of al-Suddi, who said: The last verse that was revealed was: {And fear the Day when you will be returned. In it to Allah} the verses."
37037,"(37037) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, on the authority of Atiyya Al-Awfi, he said: The last verse that was revealed: {And fear the Day in which you will be returned to Allah} the verses."
37038,"(37038) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Misra Abi Jamilah, who said: The first day she spoke about The Kharijites on the Day of Camel."
37039,"(۳۷۰۳۹) حَدَّثَنَا عَبْدُ الرَّحِیمِ ، عَنْ أَشْعَثَ بْنِ سَوَّارٍ ، عَنِ ابْنِ سِیرِینَ ، قَالَ : إنَّ أَوَّلَ مَنْ طَبَخَ الطِّلاَئَ حَتَّی Two-thirds of it was gone, and Omar bin Al-Khattab remained."
37040,"(۳۷۰۴۰) حَدَّثَنَا حُسَیْنٌ ، عَنْ زَائِدَۃَ ، عَنْ عَطَائِ بْنِ السَّائِبِ ، عَنِ الشَّعْبِیِّ ، قَالَ : أَوَّلُ مَا کَتَبَ النَّبِیُّ صَلَّی اللَّہُ It was written, “In Your Name, O God,” upon him and grant him peace. When it was revealed, “In the Name of God, its course and its anchorage,” it was written, “In the Name of God,” so when it was revealed: “Indeed, it is مِنْ سُلَیْمَانَ وَإِنَّہُ بِسْمِ اللہِ الرَّحْمَن الرَّحِیمِ} کَتَبَ بسم اللہ الرَّحْمَن الرحیم۔"
37041,"(37041) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghani, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Medina, who said: Muawiyah said: I The first of the kings."
37042,"(37042) Ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra’il bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: The first person to deliver the sermon while sitting was Muawiyah. He said: Then he apologized to the people, then he said: I complain about my feet."
37043,"(37043) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, he said: The first thing that begins Obsessiveness from ablution."
37044,"(37044) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi narrated to us, Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The beginning of creation is the Throne. And water and air, and the earth was created from water, and creation began on Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, and the plural of creation Friday, so the Jews converted to Judaism on the Sabbath, and one of the six days is like a thousand years of what you count. (Bayhaqi 806)"
37045,"(37045) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: I came Omar was among some of my people, so he made a group of two thousand men from Tayy, and turned away from me, so I said: O Commander of the Faithful, Do you not know me? He laughed until he lay on his back, then said: By God, I know you. You believed when they disbelieved, and you accepted when they turned away. Then he began to apologise, then he said: It was imposed on a people to whom it was unfair, and they were in secret from their clans when it came to them. Of the rights. (Bukhari 4394, Muslim 1957)"
37046,"(37046) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr said: Al-Sham is the first land in ruins."
37047,"(37047) Al-Fadl Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: I catch the people when they go They went to the funerals on foot and returned on foot, and the first to ride were his companions."
37048,"(37048) Awf told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: The first call to Daniel was in Sawsan, she was a young man. Beautiful among the Children of Israel, worshiping it. Then he mentioned a lengthy hadith."
37049,"(37049) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid: The first women used to place a shrine on the sleeves of their armor. One of them inserts it on her finger and covers the ring with it."
37050,"(37050) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, prayer has its beginning and last, and then He mentioned a hadith about it."
37051,"(37051) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Abu Al-Muhazam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The first to enter From this nation of fire are the thugs."
37052,"(37052) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The first to The angels circumambulated the House."
37053,"(37053) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: You should listen first."
37054,"(37054) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, he said: The first On the Day of Resurrection, the servant will be held accountable for the obligatory prayer, if he completes it. Otherwise, it will be said: See if he has performed it voluntarily. So the obligatory prayer was completed from his voluntary prayers. If you did not complete the obligatory prayers and there was no voluntary prayer for him, he will be taken from both ends and thrown away. With Him in Hell."
37055,"(37055) Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, he said: The first day I met Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila I saw an old man with a white head and beard riding a donkey as he followed a funeral procession."
37056,"(37056) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid Al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, he said: The first thing to be asked On his authority, a servant is asked about his prayer, and if it is accepted from him, then all of his deeds are accepted from him, and if it is rejected from him, then it is answered from him. All his work"
37057,"(37057) Affan and Ibn Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first person to be clothed with a garment of Hell will be Satan, so he will place it on His eyebrows and pulls her from behind him and he says: O Thabourahum, and his descendants are behind him and they say: Oh Thabourahum. Until he stands over the Fire and says: Oh, their destruction. And they say: Oh, their destruction. Then he says: (Do not call upon a single destruction today. And call upon much perseverance.)"
37058,"(37058) Affan narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ibrahim, he said: The first Whoever threw pebbles into the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, when the people raised their heads from prostration They shook their hands, so he ordered pebbles made of agate and brought them, and they were spread out in the mosque of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
37059,"(37059) Bakr bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, said: We stayed in Medina for two years before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. We saluted the mosques and established prayer."
37060,"(37060) Ghandar narrated to us, Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Muriya, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: The first to convert to Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali bin Abi Talib. He said: I mentioned that to Al-Nakha’i. He denied it and said: Abu Bakr was the first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
37061,"(37061) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi, he said: The first thing that God created From Adam’s head, he began to look while he was creating. He said: And his feet remained. So when it was after the afternoon prayer, he said: O Lord, hasten. Before the night, that is what God Almighty says: (And man was hasty)"
37062,"(37062) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: The first emigrants were those who reached the market under The tree"
37063,"(37063) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: He was the first to Abd al-Rahman bin Suhail built a gate in Mecca. Omar came and said: A man will come down to us and there is no servant with him, so he will leave. We put on his shoes and his she-camel, then he goes out, and you are safe for us, and we fear thieves, so give me permission and I will open a door. So he gave him permission, so I turned away. Quraysh and they opened the gates."
37064,"(37064) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The feast on the first day is true, the second day is fair, and anything beyond that is hypocrisy. (Abu Dawud 3738 and Abd al-Razzaq 10660)"
37065,"(37065) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The first thing that prevents the killer from inheritance is For the place of the owner of the cow."
37066,"(37066) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, who said: It was said to them on the Day of Badr: Make a sacrifice. For the angels have been made equal. He said: The first thing that was made was wool. For that day."
37067,"(37067) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd al-Madini, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, he said: When Othman bin Maz’un died, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, buried him in Al-Baqi’, the first to be buried in it, and then He said to a man beside him: Go to that rock and bring it to me and place it by his grave so that I can recognize it. Whoever of our family died, we buried him there."
37068,"(37068) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, on the day when people say: It is from Ramadan, he said: And he said: He does not fast except with the imam if he fasts, for it was the first group to do something like this."
37069,"(37069) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Israel, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Sulayman Al-Janni, That is, Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who mentioned the killing of Othman, and said: It was the beginning of the tribulation."
37070,"(37070) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Did you see that on the day of the Resurrection there was a trial, meaning the killing of Othman, for it was the beginning of the trials and the last of them was the Antichrist."
37071,"(37071) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, he said: Amer told us, that the first grandfather to quarrel with his children was Omar ibn al-Khattab. His son died and he left behind two sons, so he disputed with them to Zayd bin Thabit, and Omar saw him and looked into their affairs, so he said: Who? He is disputing with me about my children, and Zaid said: They have a father besides you, so share him among them."
37072,"(37072) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said: Ayoub, Abu Zayd al-Homsi, narrated to me, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah, on the authority of his father, that he entered upon Ubadah while he was sick, and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: The first thing God created was the pen, and He said: Run, so that Hour ran according to what it is.
(Tirmidhi 2155. Ahmad 317)"
37073,"(37073) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The first person to introduce the first call to prayer on the day of Friday prayer was Uthman. Let the people of the markets give the call to prayer."
37074,"(37074) Ismail, meaning Ibn Aliyah, narrated to us on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Al-Zuhri: The call to prayer was when the Imam appeared, so he introduced it. The Commander of the Faithful, Othman, gave the second call to prayer at Al-Zawra’ to gather the people."
